{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire","id":1502801,"title":"Ask a Simple Question: Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-11T18:26:37-08:00","id":1502801,"title":"Ask a Simple Question: Vampire","content":"As per <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1500621-ask-a-simple-question-post-closure-and-what-to-do-about-it?p=1500622#post1500622\">Ian\u2019s advice</a>, I\u2019m creating a similar thread as to the now closed <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire\">ask a simple question thread.\u200b</a><br /> <br /> What page and book has the rules for Averting One's Eyes from things like Dominate during combat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T20:15:14-08:00","id":1502807,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I don't think any book has that Action listed specifically.<br /> <br /> You might want to just wholly reframe Mesmerize's contested dice roll as the vampire trying to meet the enemy's eye versus the enemy trying to avoid it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T21:13:52-08:00","id":1502810,"title":"","content":"During <i>combat?</i> The Blinded Tilt (partial/one-eye version). Have fun fighting someone without looking at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T01:24:38-08:00","id":1502813,"title":"","content":"Where in the corebook is the rough estimate ratio of Vamp:Humies ?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I'm thinking on working on a Chronicle within my region and I thus need some estimate of the potential numbers since fewer vampires would mean fewer covenants and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T07:29:11-08:00","id":1502835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502813#post1502813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where in the corebook is the rough estimate ratio of Vamp:Humies ?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I'm thinking on working on a Chronicle within my region and I thus need some estimate of the potential numbers since fewer vampires would mean fewer covenants and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember the 1e corebook having something on the subject, i would imagine 2e simply keeping it out of convenience for STs wanting a reference jumping point to start and tweak from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T07:35:55-08:00","id":1502836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502813#post1502813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where in the corebook is the rough estimate ratio of Vamp:Humies ?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> I'm thinking on working on a Chronicle within my region and I thus need some estimate of the potential numbers since fewer vampires would mean fewer covenants and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR 1e Core talks about it on page 24 in the 'The Body Count' section. IIRC VtR 2e doesn't mention specific ratios as it leans more toward a 'as many as you need to support the type of stories you want to tell' approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T08:13:41-08:00","id":1502839,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot !<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with something like boosted 1:50 000, since the whole metorpolitan area is home to 800K peoples, so I could have twenty or so vampires, which is more than enough really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T09:43:16-08:00","id":1502846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502839#post1502839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot !<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with something like boosted 1:50 000, since the whole metorpolitan area is home to 800K peoples, so I could have twenty or so vampires, which is more than enough really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have gone as to conceive my chronicle's version of Rio de Janeiro as a city with possibly around 300-500 undead, but then we are talking of an urban center 6-9+ million people depending if one counts city proper or metropolitan area. Plus, i wanted to drive home a sense of a barely contained seething cauldron of hidden monsters that the night court barely controlled, supposing the Prince and its ilk even have a good grasp of their numbers, territories and activities (no, they didn't).<br /> <br /> Only about 50-60 were actually written out and i'm the first to admit a bunch were riffs on NPCs from the Core, Covenantbooks or characters from VtM: Bloodlines with some random ideas or nods to brazilian history &amp; folklore mixed in.<br /> <br /> (Though some end up distinctly different - Rodrigo Nunes as a <i>mulato </i>streetcar driver &amp; capoeirista made Toreador in the '30s is almost unrecognizable in relation to Nines from the game except for his name and Carthian allegiance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-12-2023, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T02:04:16-08:00","id":1502918,"title":"","content":"What kind of event may lead to the - official - wipe out of two Covenants in a City ?<br /> <br /> My campaign will focus only on Ordo Dracul and Carthians in the region of Toulouse and I need to find an explanation for the absence of the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum (Circle is absent since neo-paganism is very weak in France anyway but especially around here).<br /> <br /> I thought about using the events of WWII being abused by those Covenants only to blow up in their faces + influx of Spanish Carthians during the Retirada to explain it but I'm lacking on the actual vampiric reasoning and all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T06:13:44-08:00","id":1502924,"title":"","content":"They might have been kicked out when city government changed, maybe the Strix decided they needed to go, maybe they got into a fight with some other creature and got wiped out or perhaps they just weren\u2019t able to get a foothold in the city.<br /> If the city recently got depopulated of vampires maybe those are the only two covenants who have tried to settle it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T10:34:06-08:00","id":1502937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502918#post1502918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of event may lead to the - official - wipe out of two Covenants in a City ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very much of a 'whatever you need to have happened in order to work the story you and your players want to tell' question which could obviously have many valid answers. I am currently working up a City where the Lancea et Sanctum and Circle are very weak (but not absent) in the aftermath of them getting into a dispute that turned to blood in the streets when their leaders lost control of the situation. The other Covenants are expanding to fill the vacuum but the Ordo are particularly strong in part because they were the one who stepped in and put an end to the fighting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T11:36:57-08:00","id":1502944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502918#post1502918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of event may lead to the - official - wipe out of two Covenants in a City ?<br /> <br /> My campaign will focus only on Ordo Dracul and Carthians in the region of Toulouse and I need to find an explanation for the absence of the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum (Circle is absent since neo-paganism is very weak in France anyway but especially around here).<br /> <br /> I thought about using the events of WWII being abused by those Covenants only to blow up in their faces + influx of Spanish Carthians during the Retirada to explain it but I'm lacking on the actual vampiric reasoning and all...</div> </div> </div> </div>As others pointed out, it all depends on what you want to set up and how much of the secret &amp; not so secret <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toulouse#History\" target=\"_blank\">history of the city</a> you want to flesh out. It could be that the influx of spanish and italians leaving their fascism infested countries in the 1920s &amp; 1930s upended definitely a status quo already decadent and fragile since <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_Calas#Voltaire&#39;s_intervention_and_posthumous_exoneration\" target=\"_blank\">Voltaire's infamous accusations</a> exposed its parliament and city institutions as backward relics even by pre-enlightnement standards.<br /> <br /> Or were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toulouse#20th_and_21st_centuries\" target=\"_blank\">the wave of algerian repatriates alonside the extensive urban reforms of the &quot;balancing metropolis&quot; project in the 60s</a> that really kickstarted things?<br /> <br /> Supposing that some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toulouse#The_fight_against_Catharism_and_its_various_aspects\" target=\"_blank\">vengeful cathar</a> didn't rise from the grave for a bout of sanctified payback of biblical proportions, that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-13-2023, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T12:42:48-08:00","id":1502951,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot for the answers ! To not hobble this thread, I created a new one, that is pending validation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T16:36:58-08:00","id":1502969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1502951#post1502951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks a lot for the answers ! To not hobble this thread, I created a new one, that is pending validation <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> !</div> </div> </div> </div>Throw in a link when it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T02:03:18-08:00","id":1503008,"title":"","content":"Here it is ! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502930-campaign-brainstorming-help-what-can-wipe-out-covenants\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...-out-covenants</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:10:35-08:00","id":1503297,"title":"","content":"I've been looking in the 1e Requiem's book for Embracing a mortal; can't find any reference; and I don't recall in Masquerade, if there were rules covering that in that book. If I remember from V:tM, it was drain the mortal, and give them at least one point of blood and expand a Willpower-point(may have been a house-rule); but with Requiem, I was thinking the same, but you have to give up a Blood-Potency point to the new vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:55:50-08:00","id":1503303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1503297#post1503297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been looking in the 1e Requiem's book for Embracing a mortal; can't find any reference; and I don't recall in Masquerade, if there were rules covering that in that book. If I remember from V:tM, it was drain the mortal, and give them at least one point of blood and expand a Willpower-point(may have been a house-rule); but with Requiem, I was thinking the same, but you have to give up a Blood-Potency point to the new vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Edition applies the cost of a Humanity dot to Embrace deliberately without producing a revenant, as described in &quot;The Embrace&quot; on page 93-94.&quot;<br /> <br /> First Edition had the cost as a dot of Willpower, per &quot;The Tradition of Progeny&quot; on page 170.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T05:22:52-08:00","id":1503369,"title":"","content":"Does the 9-again bonus of Professional Training skills apply to Discipline rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T06:56:55-08:00","id":1503377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1503369#post1503369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 9-again bonus of Professional Training skills apply to Discipline rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mh, good question. I'd usually tend to consider discipline's rolls as something not related to mundane skills rolls, but I think there's no hard rule about it. <br /> i'd interpret this merit as strictly related to a profession which doesn't make you better in a suoernarur power that falla under that &quot;generic&quot; skillset.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T10:57:10-08:00","id":1503460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1503303#post1503303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second Edition applies the cost of a Humanity dot to Embrace deliberately without producing a revenant, as described in &quot;The Embrace&quot; on page 93-94.&quot;<br /> <br /> First Edition had the cost as a dot of Willpower, per &quot;The Tradition of Progeny&quot; on page 170.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you; I just found that last night while reading Requiem. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T15:13:38-08:00","id":1504076,"title":"","content":"So, Resilience doesn't protect against sunlight damage? Did I read that right? Fortitude not providing protection against sunlight seems like some sort of heresy: now, perhaps it throws off game balance, at least in lower-potency/higher-humanity; more powerful vampires, with higher potency/lower humanity, would burn up in a flash from an ACE sunlamp even with resilience. So, as anyone ignored that rule and let resilience protect against sunlight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T15:46:45-08:00","id":1504080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1504076#post1504076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Resilience doesn't protect against sunlight damage? Did I read that right? Fortitude not providing protection against sunlight seems like some sort of heresy: now, perhaps it throws off game balance, at least in lower-potency/higher-humanity; more powerful vampires, with higher potency/lower humanity, would burn up in a flash from an ACE sunlamp even with resilience. So, as anyone ignored that rule and let resilience protect against sunlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that I don't need Requiem to play like Masquerade and The Ordo Dracul have a whole ass Coil about sunlight, no, not particularly. The closest I get to it is running the damage rate from sunlight according to the rules found in Reap the Whirlwind rather than the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-28-2023, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T20:48:14-08:00","id":1504101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1504076#post1504076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Resilience doesn't protect against sunlight damage? Did I read that right? Fortitude not providing protection against sunlight seems like some sort of heresy: now, perhaps it throws off game balance, at least in lower-potency/higher-humanity; more powerful vampires, with higher potency/lower humanity, would burn up in a flash from an ACE sunlamp even with resilience. So, as anyone ignored that rule and let resilience protect against sunlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience protects against sunlight damage by the simple virtue of giving you more Health to burn through. That is the extent to which Resilience by itself lets you mitigate damage from sunlight compared to other banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T12:08:16-08:00","id":1504774,"title":"","content":"Gargoyle's vigilance can be used while slumbering with a point of willpower. Does that mean that in case an intruders is spot the kindred can wake up automatically or can attempt the awakening roll without being considered in direct danger?<br /> <br /> How is exactly the awakening mechanic working?<br /> Succeding in the roll the vampire wakes up for a number of turns equal to his humanity, after that it fall asleep again. But it's also written that once he reach 5+humanity successes he can stay awake indefinitely without penality. Does that imply that the humanity roll is repeated every turn he's awake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T17:01:23-08:00","id":1504793,"title":"","content":"You roll Humanity and get to act for a number of turns equal to your Humanity. During those turns, you're presumably performing actions to get whatever it is done that you needed to wake up for, like fending off an attacker or chasing away an intruder. Count up the total of all your successes across <i>those</i> rolls, the rolls to fend off or to chase away or whatever. If <i>that</i> number exceeds Blood Potency + 5 (not Humanity + 5, more Humanity does not make it harder to stay awake) before you fall asleep again, you get to stay up indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Gargoyle's Vigilance doesn't say anything about enhancing your ability to rise from daysleep, so I think you would still need to be in direct danger to rise. The utility of activating it in daysleep is that you know what's going on while you slumber, you're sleeping with your eyes open and can remember what anybody who snuck in did around the place.<br /> <br /> The benefits to moving against an intruder apply if you use Gargoyle's Vigilance during the night, or if the intruder threatens you enough to wake you from the daysleep while you have Gargoyle's Vigilance up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T20:00:40-08:00","id":1504807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1504774#post1504774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is exactly the awakening mechanic working?<br /> Succeding in the roll the vampire wakes up for a number of turns equal to his humanity, after that it fall asleep again. But it's also written that once he reach 5+humanity successes he can stay awake indefinitely without penality. Does that imply that the humanity roll is repeated every turn he's awake?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1504793#post1504793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You roll Humanity and get to act for a number of turns equal to your Humanity. During those turns, you're presumably performing actions to get whatever it is done that you needed to wake up for, like fending off an attacker or chasing away an intruder. Count up the total of all your successes across <i>those</i> rolls, the rolls to fend off or to chase away or whatever. If <i>that</i> number exceeds Blood Potency + 5 (not Humanity + 5, more Humanity does not make it harder to stay awake) before you fall asleep again, you get to stay up indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonably certain the &quot;falls asleep without another Humanity roll&quot; means the successes are being counted across the successive unfailed Humanity rolls to stay awake that you're making every [Humanity] turns rather than successes at actions taken during those turns \u2014 vampires with low Humanity wake up for longer by sleeping in well-defended Havens they have an affinity for, not by being more capable of ending an intruder quickly.<br /> \u200b<br /> You roll Humanity(+Haven), get Humanity turns of wakefulness, roll Humanity again after those turns expire to get another Humanity turns of wakefulness, repeat until you fail a roll/accumulate BP+5 successes/don't need to be awake anymore. The vast majority of social vampires having Humanity higher than 2 means most characters have at least a 2-in-3 chance of succeeding each roll outside a Haven, but particularly potent and callous vampires still have more chances to fail before they hit their heightened threshold, so they're incentivized further to prevent that from needing to be done by beefing up their security.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-08-2023, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T08:25:11-08:00","id":1504846,"title":"","content":"I don t understand the Liderc Bloodline Bane.<br /> In the first part of the description it states that when a Liderc gets the Dependent condition the effects of Touchstones are diminished.<br /> But &quot; If the subject of her affection was her Touchstone, she immediately loses her as opposed to detaching.&quot;, what does this mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T17:43:40-08:00","id":1504886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1504846#post1504846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don t understand the Liderc Bloodline Bane.<br /> In the first part of the description it states that when a Liderc gets the Dependent condition the effects of Touchstones are diminished.<br /> But &quot; If the subject of her affection was her Touchstone, she immediately loses her as opposed to detaching.&quot;, what does this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feed on your Touchstone more than once, they're not your Touchstone anymore.<br /> <br /> Normally, the Dependent Condition makes causing harm to a mortal you've fed on more than once prompt a Detachment check for characters at or above Humanity 3, which, if you lose Humanity, may cause an attached Touchstone to become detached. The Lid\u00e9rc instead immediately lose a Touchstone they feed on more than once, in addition to the Dependent Condition causing them to gain less benefits from their Touchstones in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-08-2023, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T11:02:01-08:00","id":1505125,"title":"","content":"What's the difference between using Shatter the Shroud - which can end the hiding effect of an obfuscated kindred - and the normal lash out action in case you are able to perceive the obfuscated vampire through Auspex or any other mean? It literally states that if you win the lash out, Obfuscate 3 - as any other obfuscate effect active - shatters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-11T13:11:21-08:00","id":1505133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1505125#post1505125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference between using Shatter the Shroud - which can end the hiding effect of an obfuscated kindred - and the normal lash out action in case you are able to perceive the obfuscated vampire through Auspex or any other mean? It literally states that if you win the lash out, Obfuscate 3 - as any other obfuscate effect active - shatters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main difference is that Shatter the Shroud works on other supernatural stealth ability that do not have Cloak of Night's particular fragility, and that Vitae is easier to come by than Willpower.<br /> <br /> Winning a Clash of Wills against any of the other Obfuscate powers or supernatural powers of stealth and deception that aren't Obfuscate 3 are subject to the normal stipulation for Clashes of Wills, that being that the losing power isn't cancelled unless only one power could possibly remain \u2014 being able to see a hidden character doesn't make everyone else able to see them except in the specific case of winning a Predatory Aura contest against a vampire you can perceive who is using Cloak of Night, and that's subject to the rules and modifiers for lashing out, not Clashes. The Devotion lets you just spend two Vitae after a successful Clash without having to spend Willpower and contend with a resisting character who's hungry or acting on their own Feeding Grounds.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Shatter the Shroud works on things that aren't vampires specifically turned physically invisible and doesn't require you to also spend Willpower on a Predatory Aura contest that you have to win as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T19:48:51-07:00","id":1505470,"title":"","content":"Taste of the strange merit; while reading Ancient Mysteries, I found this merit; odd, I just naturally assumed a vampire with a Blood-potency of seven plus, could, always gain sustenance from other supernatural-creatures like werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T20:40:28-07:00","id":1505472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1505470#post1505470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taste of the strange merit; while reading Ancient Mysteries, I found this merit; odd, I just naturally assumed a vampire with a Blood-potency of seven plus, could, always gain sustenance from other supernatural-creatures like werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely <b>not</b> the norm, at least in 1st edition, that Ancient Mysteries was clearly a book for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-15T20:47:35-07:00","id":1505473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1505470#post1505470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taste of the strange merit; while reading Ancient Mysteries, I found this merit; odd, I just naturally assumed a vampire with a Blood-potency of seven plus, could, always gain sustenance from other supernatural-creatures like werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the fact that the normal progression of feeding restrictions is animal blood -&gt; human blood -&gt; Kindred Vitae and things that aren't vampires don't have Kindred Vitae, it is entirely within reason for the 1e predecessor to Unnatural Affinity to require at least the minimum possible investment of experience for a character to develop an alternative to courting the Vinculum and potential temptation for diablerie rather than make it so that vampires in general can automatically sustain themselves at all ages on the blood of different monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T12:01:07-07:00","id":1508374,"title":"","content":"In the werewolf book Shunned by the Moon the Eaters of the Dead believe that vampires killed and drained their totem of its power a long time ago. Is that ever touched up on in VtR and if so what details does Vampire give?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T12:16:01-07:00","id":1508375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508374#post1508374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the werewolf book Shunned by the Moon the Eaters of the Dead believe that vampires killed and drained their totem of its power a long time ago. Is that ever touched up on in VtR and if so what details does Vampire give?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea whatsoever and considering the Eaters of Dead are a 2nd edition lodge, i'd say it's 50-50 chance of anyone having planned for a Requiem callback.<br /> But from what i saw <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eaters_of_the_Dead#Totem:_Isim-Ur\" target=\"_blank\">in the wiki</a>, his narrative gives me something of Strix vibes but could be something else altogether, considering <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eaters_of_the_Dead#The_Sacred_Hunt\" target=\"_blank\">his sacred hunt</a> also cites sin-eaters and mummies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T12:46:44-07:00","id":1508376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508375#post1508375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i'd say it's 50-50 chance of anyone having planned for a Requiem callback.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about what I figured so I thought I would ask. <br /> <br /> ETA: It's worth noting that the totem itself is from first edition. It's from a different lodge though: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lodge_of_the_Feast\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lodge_of_the_Feast</a> and isn't actually a second born, just pretending to be a second born it seems. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But from what i saw <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eaters_of_the_Dead#Totem:_Isim-Ur\" target=\"_blank\">in the wiki</a>, his narrative gives me something of Strix vibes but could be something else altogether, considering <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eaters_of_the_Dead#The_Sacred_Hunt\" target=\"_blank\">his sacred hunt</a> also cites sin-eaters and mummies. </div> </div> </div>The comment about &quot;drained her dry&quot; along with the numerous mentions of vampires in particular is what lead me to think Vampire. Could have been the strix though, but that would still typically be confirmed through the VtR books I would assume.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 04-14-2023, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T13:43:06-07:00","id":1508386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508376#post1508376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's about what I figured so I thought I would ask.<br /> <br /> ETA: It's worth noting that the totem itself is from first edition. It's from a different lodge though: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lodge_of_the_Feast\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lodge_of_the_Feast</a> and isn't actually a second born, just pretending to be a second born it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> That's good to know indeed. Really reminds me of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gh%C3%BBl\" target=\"_blank\">these guys</a> and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cult_of_the_Red_Word\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508376#post1508376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comment about &quot;drained her dry&quot; along with the numerous mentions of vampires in particular is what lead me to think Vampire. Could have been the strix though, but that would still typically be confirmed through the VtR books I would assume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but then the text also does some back &amp; forth between &quot;vampires&quot;, &quot;hungry dead&quot;, &quot;undead&quot; and so on, what makes things overall....sketchy i dare say.<br /> <br /> It could be strix-possessed, a bloodline or clan lost to the ages, some other sort of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_The_Wicked_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">wicked dead</a> not of the kindred like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jiang_Shi_(Night_Horrors)\" target=\"_blank\">Jiangshi</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Penanggalan_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Penanggal</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mnemovores\" target=\"_blank\">Mnemovores</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Gh%C3%BBl\" target=\"_blank\">Ghuls</a> or more, sekhem-hungry <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Amkhat_(MTC)\" target=\"_blank\">Amkhat</a>\u200b, weird escaped denizens of the Underworld, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lower_Depths\" target=\"_blank\">Lower Depths</a>, Abyss and who knows what else.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the &quot;draining it dry&quot; refers to someone <i>eliminating her cannibal followers</i> instead.....lots of room for interpretation there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-14-2023, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:24:33-07:00","id":1508613,"title":"","content":"Are disciplines that require multiple viate off limits to younger kindred or is the spend blood until you spend enough rule discussed under juggernaut's gait a universal rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T06:39:27-07:00","id":1508627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508613#post1508613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are disciplines that require multiple viate off limits to younger kindred or is the spend blood until you spend enough rule discussed under juggernaut's gait a universal rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no explicit statement that I can find, but considering that &quot;if an effect takes more fuel than you can spend in a single turn, you can spend it over multiple turns and the effect activates once you've met the cost&quot; is universally described in every other splatbook* with a fuel-per-turn limit** and vampires already need to spend multiple Vitae to heal aggravated damage, I'd say they're not off-limits so much as unable to be quickly marshaled \u2014 Juggernaut's Gait has that note because it's specifically there to negate damage immediately and that doesn't work if you can't have spent five Vitae by the time the damage would come due.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* See Werewolf 2e Core p100, Mage 2e Core p87, Promethean 2e Core p168, Changeling 2e Core p126, Geist 2e Core p101, and Demon Core p109.<br /> **Except Mummy, where Sekhem falling is a big deal, the least time-restricted things you can spend Pillars on only cost one or two Pillars, and you don't lose the ability to spend more than one Pillar per turn until the level at which you can't use Utterances that cost more than one Pillar anyway.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-17-2023, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T06:52:41-07:00","id":1508629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1508627#post1508627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no explicit statement that I can find, but considering that &quot;if an effect takes more fuel than you can spend in a single turn, you can spend it over multiple turns and the effect activates once you've met the cost&quot; is universally described in every other splatbook* with a fuel-per-turn limit** and vampires already need to spend multiple Vitae to heal aggravated damage, I'd say they're not off-limits so much as unable to be quickly marshaled \u2014 Juggernaut's Gait has that note because it's specifically there to negate damage immediately and that doesn't work if you can't have spent five Vitae by the time the damage would come due.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* See Werewolf 2e Core p100, Mage 2e Core p87, Promethean 2e Core p168, Changeling 2e Core p126, Geist 2e Core p101, and Demon Core p109.<br /> **Except Mummy, where Sekhem falling is a big deal, the least time-restricted things you can spend Pillars on only cost one or two Pillars, and you don't lose the ability to spend more than one Pillar per turn until the level at which you can't use Utterances that cost more than one Pillar anyway.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That is an exceptionally thorough answer. Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T13:50:55-07:00","id":1512045,"title":"","content":"Is there anything that ever converted KotE over to VtR 2e? I'm fine with someone's post on here or a product on the shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T14:16:52-07:00","id":1512047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1512045#post1512045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything that ever converted KotE over to VtR 2e? I'm fine with someone's post on here or a product on the shop.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T15:21:13-07:00","id":1512052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1512047#post1512047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm aware, nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ty for letting me know. Someone on Reddit asked what VtM vampires and Requiem Vampires would think of each other and that made me curious as to what KotE vampires would think of Requiem ones and vice versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T17:26:47-07:00","id":1512062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1512052#post1512052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ty for letting me know. Someone on Reddit asked what VtM vampires and Requiem Vampires would think of each other and that made me curious as to what KotE vampires would think of Requiem ones and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, KotE vampires would fit fine among kindred since spontaneous rising of corpses IS a thing that may happen in Requiem (though far from common knowledge, to the point of being seen as mere folklore by even many of them).<br /> <br /> That said they would still probably fit into one of the &quot;five clans&quot; or something similar enough, but then Requiem's perception of what a clan entails can be quite different from Masquerade's and in some aspects bleeds into KotE's conception of Dharma, might be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-18-2023, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:41:33-07:00","id":1512075,"title":"","content":"When someone who is already blood-bound is Embraced, does the blood bond persist? 1E gives conflicting answers in core vs the Ghouls book, and I'm not finding an answer in published 2E materials at all, which surprises me. My instinct says existing bonds are probably broken when the childe dies as part of the Embrace, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T06:55:27-07:00","id":1512210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1512075#post1512075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone who is already blood-bound is Embraced, does the blood bond persist? 1E gives conflicting answers in core vs the Ghouls book, and I'm not finding an answer in published 2E materials at all, which surprises me. My instinct says existing bonds are probably broken when the childe dies as part of the Embrace, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes as you are also giving him more of your vitae which reinforce/restart the bond","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T02:46:17-07:00","id":1514099,"title":"","content":"Can a Vampire willingly choose to enter Frenzy at any time? Riding the wave indicates you need to already be in Frenzy, not that you can enter it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T05:37:48-07:00","id":1514110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1514099#post1514099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Vampire willingly choose to enter Frenzy at any time? Riding the wave indicates you need to already be in Frenzy, not that you can enter it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stir the Beast, the first Coil of the Wyrm, allows you to enter frenzy &quot;unprompted,&quot; which indicates to me that normally you need an appropriate stimulus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T10:37:22-07:00","id":1514117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1514099#post1514099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Vampire willingly choose to enter Frenzy at any time? Riding the wave indicates you need to already be in Frenzy, not that you can enter it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can only let themeselves fall to frenzy if not using stir the Beast. That said, almost everything in the game is a stimulus to frenzy, even just a verbal insult. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bSo it depends on the situation you are thinking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T09:43:22-07:00","id":1518938,"title":"","content":"Is there any clan, bloodline, or covenant dedicated to working with the strix or enslaving them somehow? I've seen a few that are supposed to fight against the strix, but none on the other side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T10:44:22-07:00","id":1518940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1518938#post1518938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any clan, bloodline, or covenant dedicated to working with the strix or enslaving them somehow? I've seen a few that are supposed to fight against the strix, but none on the other side.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff from Requiem for Rome gives us a legend about a group/clan of vampires who decided to stand by their compact/tribute to the Birds, even though the Propinqui felt the owls had twisted and abused the original terms. There was fighting over this and those individuals, to whom the Julii refered as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Akhud#Rome\" target=\"_blank\">Traditores</a>, mostly erased and forgotten from history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-16T16:09:37-07:00","id":1520791,"title":"","content":"How much use do ghouls get from Protein? Can they in any way learn animal forms for Beasts Skin? Can they survive without air if they use Unmarked Grave? I don\u2019t see any reason they couldn\u2019t use any of the other abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T10:39:23-07:00","id":1522102,"title":"","content":"Can vampires smoke?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T18:50:40-07:00","id":1522131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1522102#post1522102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can vampires smoke?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they can, though it does nothing for a vampire since as undead they no longer require breathing.<br /> More importantly, lighting a cigarette or cigar might be a bit of a self-control exercise for some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T10:51:51-07:00","id":1522167,"title":"","content":"Or a quirk to help them feel closer to their lost humanity such as my character needing to smell coffee nearby or holding for little get togethers with mortals &amp; fellow Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,