lso bunch of other interesting bane ideas such as : being forced to count rice grains; being forced to dress in one color; having trouble with reflections; etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the &quot;Sun's Terrifying Visage&quot; severe bane from Danse Macabre (p199).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T09:09:27-07:00","id":1522268,"title":"","content":"Which is a kindred more likely ro share with a revenent thall a clan or covenent discipline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T10:40:01-07:00","id":1522270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1522268#post1522268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a kindred more likely ro share with a revenent thall a clan or covenent discipline</div> </div> </div> </div>More likely to share implies &quot;likely&quot; which I don't believe is the case. If they cared enough about the revenant to teach it a discipline they would probably be better off embracing it. <br /> <br /> But of the two options, I believe a clan discipline is more likely than a covenant one, the Gangrel won't hunt you down for teaching protean (probably) but the Lancea et Sanctum will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T10:51:41-07:00","id":1522272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1522236#post1522236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If i remember correctly that's a specific bane from the book that had bunch of thems(I can't remember the title). Basically the Bane made image of the sun trigger frenzy roll. There was also bunch of other interesting bane ideas such as : being forced to count rice grains; being forced to dress in one color; having trouble with reflections; etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is many versions of the vampire lore throughout the world. I remember in a direct to video Dracula 2000 sequel where Vampires can be complusive counters, needing to untie knots on a rope and the scene where Dracula beat those traps was cool and was the only worthwhile scene in the movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-11T18:37:11-07:00","id":1522441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1522272#post1522272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is many versions of the vampire lore throughout the world. I remember in a direct to video Dracula 2000 sequel where Vampires can be complusive counters, needing to untie knots on a rope and the scene where Dracula beat those traps was cool and was the only worthwhile scene in the movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though i didn't liked how the 3 episode dracula serie ended, it had something similar with his banes. It felt very requiem-ish, super cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-12T10:43:13-07:00","id":1522469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1522441#post1522441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even though i didn't liked how the 3 episode dracula serie ended, it had something similar with his banes. It felt very requiem-ish, super cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr. Hauer was the only worthwhile thing in the final film and funny story is all his lines were improvised on the spot as he mysteriously &quot;lost&quot; the script and what he came up was better then what they had written, which I guess told him right away about the skill level of the writing team he was working with.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-12-2023, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T18:10:56-07:00","id":1523153,"title":"","content":"Why was it decided that Composure is one of the favored attributes for gangrel and resolve for ventrue? Just curious","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T19:02:31-07:00","id":1523154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1523153#post1523153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why was it decided that Composure is one of the favored attributes for gangrel and resolve for ventrue? Just curious</div> </div> </div> </div>Composure is the Attribute for controlling your emotions and thoughts, and how you express those through your physicality. It is a good Attribute for a tough guy archetype who also has to wrestle their Beast more regularly than anyone else.<br /> <br /> Resolve is the Attribute for keeping to your commitments and long-term goal, and not being deterred by outside actions or persuasions. It is a good Attribute for someone who carefully programs people to the needed level to enact their large scale plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T19:09:44-07:00","id":1523155,"title":"","content":"You can also think of them in terms of their axes on the attribute grid. Composure is Social Resistance. It's the Attribute you use to ensure that force of personality will not sway you from what you want to do. Resolve is Mental Resistance. It's the Attribute you use to hold your will strong against mental influence and persist in your gambits against temptations wearing them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T20:33:57-07:00","id":1523159,"title":"","content":"Thank yall. I would like but the button ain't there for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-25T22:09:18-07:00","id":1523162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1523159#post1523159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank yall. I would like but the button ain't there for it</div> </div> </div> </div>You should see now on the right hand side a &quot;reactions&quot; button that includes a thumbs up (like the one I gave yours!), icymi","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-26T05:03:31-07:00","id":1523169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1523162#post1523162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should see now on the right hand side a &quot;reactions&quot; button that includes a thumbs up (like the one I gave yours!), icymi</div> </div> </div> </div>Left side, bottom of the post for me. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-25T16:55:08-07:00","id":1524515,"title":"","content":"Lost to the beast: surely, if a vampire PC can lose all their humanity, an NPC can as well; how common is that? That means, in a city full of vampires, they'll be one that's a monster that the others will have to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T04:46:07-07:00","id":1524519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1524515#post1524515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost to the beast: surely, if a vampire PC can lose all their humanity, an NPC can as well; how common is that? That means, in a city full of vampires, they'll be one that's a monster that the others will have to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at the sample breaking points at Humanity 1, I can only conclude that it's incredibly rare. There are incredibly few &quot;passive&quot; breaking points to be exposed to, and the ones that requires actions from the vampire will likely bring a lot of attention and thus be dealt with quite fast as vampires to commit them will likely be seen as a liability for all vampires in the domain.<br /> The two types of vampires who are most likely to become draugr (without already being marked for death) are these:<br /> Overly violent vampires who live outside domains (so mostly rural areas) and thus escape notice because there's no other vampires around to bring them in line.<br /> Serial diablerists who are good enough to cover their tracks to manage to become a draugr before being found out.<br /> <br /> The former are by far the most terrifying kind of draugr for humans. Human-like monstrosities that will hunt you down and tear you to shreds unless you manage to defend yourself until the sunrise. Depending on their Disciplines and mindset, staying inside at night might only offer a false sense of security.<br /> The latter are by far the most terrifying kind of draugr for Kindred. Vampires who have the skills and strength necessary to hunt down other Kindred and drain <i>them</i> dry, without getting caught, and now there's nothing stopping them from trying to indulge whenever they have an opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:15:57-07:00","id":1524776,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1524519#post1524519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looking at the sample breaking points at Humanity 1, I can only conclude that it's incredibly rare. There are incredibly few &quot;passive&quot; breaking points to be exposed to, and the ones that requires actions from the vampire will likely bring a lot of attention and thus be dealt with quite fast as vampires to commit them will likely be seen as a liability for all vampires in the domain.<br /> . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that most likely, an outcast-vampire will lose to the Beast, but, in some cases, a vampire can hide their deprivations as vampires are good at hiding things. Perhaps a frenzy or Wrath brought about a Humanity-roll? Especially if it's a Prince with a lot of power. Perhaps no one else noticed, or noticed but was afraid to say something? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:30:27-07:00","id":1524778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1524776#post1524776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that most likely, an outcast-vampire will lose to the Beast, but, in some cases, a vampire can hide their deprivations as vampires are good at hiding things. Perhaps a frenzy or Wrath brought about a Humanity-roll? Especially if it's a Prince with a lot of power. Perhaps no one else noticed, or noticed but was afraid to say something?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>People will notice when the Prince commits mass murder. And while the covenants aren't like the Camarilla from Requiem they do pay attention over multiple cities and high ups from other cities would take matters into their own hands. <br /> <br /> But why do you need the vampire to have lost all its humanity? A vampire can maintain humanity and still be a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T16:48:59-07:00","id":1524779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1524515#post1524515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lost to the beast: surely, if a vampire PC can lose all their humanity, an NPC can as well; how common is that? That means, in a city full of vampires, they'll be one that's a monster that the others will have to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tacking on a third category that's similarly uncommon enough to functionally be a plot device, there's vampires who Embrace their way out of human perspective altogether, whether that's out of desperation, weird occult urges, a desire to leave some form of positive legacy (i.e. both of the above), or for stranger reasons yet.<br /> <br /> The mechanics may &quot;only&quot; model it with a dice penalty, but vampires with Humanity below 3 are edging into if not directly occupying the same sort of atavistic alien headspace as Geist: the Sin-Eaters uses to make geister into ghosts who act more like cryptic horror-creatures than people who happen to be dead. The Kindred keep their safety margins up for insurance against more than just one bad night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T04:10:49-08:00","id":1526049,"title":"","content":"I was reassessing Majesty 3 applied to Confident and I had the feeling it is a bit too weak compared to even just Dominate 1.<br /> The book mention that any action that WOULD lead to a breaking point shatters away the charmed condition (so, in my understanding, before the breaking point occurs so before the action is taken, opposed to dominate where prior you have to hit the breaking point to be awakened, which make it far more useful). So, since almost everything, for a normal person, is a breaking point, does it seems fair to you? Unless you do not charm a professional assassin or a street thug, there are very few situation where a 3rd dot if this discipline can really be effective.<br /> <br /> Any thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T04:54:40-08:00","id":1526052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526049#post1526049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reassessing Majesty 3 applied to Confident and I had the feeling it is a bit too weak compared to even just Dominate 1.<br /> The book mention that any action that WOULD lead to a breaking point shatters away the charmed condition (so, in my understanding, before the breaking point occurs so before the action is taken, opposed to dominate where prior you have to hit the breaking point to be awakened, which make it far more useful). So, since almost everything, for a normal person, is a breaking point, does it seems fair to you? Unless you do not charm a professional assassin or a street thug, there are very few situation where a 3rd dot if this discipline can really be effective.<br /> <br /> Any thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are missing a good number of things, I think. First, Majesty 3 allows you to rewrite your victim's emotional state entirely for the cost of a viate. Clever use of that ability can often get you the effect you desire without you having to do more direct means. <br /> <br /> Second, the ability to make requests comes without a roll. Once a victim is charmed, Majesty 3 enables you to play with them safely, without concern for the whims of dice. Yes, they won't take a breaking point for you if they are charmed, but if that's a major limitation for you it seems like you're trying to fit a square leg in a round hole then complaining the round hole is too weak. <br /> <br /> But then again, the power doesn't stop there, either. If your victim is enthralled, Majesty 3 will have them blow through breaking points for you if you wish. <br /> <br /> All that said, I do believe the first level of most disciples is fairly pushed, but honestly I think that was an intelligent decision during Requiem's design, it enables multiple builds to be powerful and flexible rather than almost forcing players to rush level 5 of a chosen discipline. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T05:34:15-08:00","id":1526054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526052#post1526052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are missing a good number of things, I think. First, Majesty 3 allows you to rewrite your victim's emotional state entirely for the cost of a viate. Clever use of that ability can often get you the effect you desire without you having to do more direct means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526052#post1526052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the ability to make requests comes without a roll. Once a victim is charmed, Majesty 3 enables you to play with them safely, without concern for the whims of dice. Yes, they won't take a breaking point for you if they are charmed, but if that's a major limitation for you it seems like you're trying to fit a square leg in a round hole then complaining the round hole is too weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't agree with this argument. It's the same as Dominate: once the power takes effect you ask, victim executes. I'm comparing Majesty 3 to other similar discipline (mainly dominate), I'm not saying that Majesty 3 is useless as a whole. I'm surrounded by folks, I cannot ask anyone of them to defend me against an aggressor, as it would be pretty surely a breaking point for most of normal people (I can perhaps drive him into a violent range which will be not the same thing). I cannot ask to betray his friend (in any way) as it's pretty much a breaking point, making most of the appealing part of a mystical charming compulsion. I don't get the value of &quot;fitting a square leg in a round hole&quot; point. Mine it's a consideration about the design of the discipline. So the discussion should be around if you consider the round hole appropriate or not...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526052#post1526052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again, the power doesn't stop there, either. If your victim is enthralled, Majesty 3 will have them blow through breaking points for you if you wish.<br /> <br /> All that said, I do believe the first level of most disciples is fairly pushed, but honestly I think that was an intelligent decision during Requiem's design, it enables multiple builds to be powerful and flexible rather than almost forcing players to rush level 5 of a chosen discipline.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is out of the scope of this conversation as it would require the 4th level of the discipline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T06:17:46-08:00","id":1526056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526054#post1526054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't agree with this argument. It's the same as Dominate: once the power takes effect you ask, victim executes. I'm comparing Majesty 3 to other similar discipline (mainly dominate), I'm not saying that Majesty 3 is useless as a whole. I'm surrounded by folks, I cannot ask anyone of them to defend me against an aggressor, as it would be pretty surely a breaking point for most of normal people (I can perhaps drive him into a violent range which will be not the same thing). I cannot ask to betray his friend (in any way) as it's pretty much a breaking point, making most of the appealing part of a mystical charming compulsion. I don't get the value of &quot;fitting a square leg in a round hole&quot; point. Mine it's a consideration about the design of the discipline. So the discussion should be around if you consider the round hole appropriate or not...</div> </div> </div> </div>Defending an innocent bystander isn't going to be a breaking point for most people actually. They may just shout at the attacker and tell the person to back off, or perhaps call 911 rather than whipping out a submachine gun and going to town, but they will defend you. <br /> <br /> As to betraying the friend, that's a bit iffy as well, I've had plenty of &quot;friends&quot; betray me in my time without any need for supernatural coercion, and most people aren't all that clever to begin with. But you're also better off if you don't risk it, as you never know who is truly loyal to their friends and who isn't. So instead of being like &quot;hey, George, when is your bff getting home, i want to break in and rob him before he gets back&quot; try &quot;hey, George, it's vitally important that I talk to your bff in person, do you know when he'll get home?&quot; They accomplish the same thing, but one doesn't require George to betray his friend. <br /> <br /> Again, it sounds like you're trying to force a square peg into a round hole, then claiming the round hole is underpowered. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is out of the scope of this conversation as it would require the 4th level of the discipline. </div> </div> </div>It is still the third level of Majesty, and if your claim is &quot;the third level of Majesty is underpowered&quot; it cannot be discounted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T06:53:43-08:00","id":1526059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526056#post1526056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Defending an innocent bystander isn't going to be a breaking point for most people actually. They may just shout at the attacker and tell the person to back off, or perhaps call 911 rather than whipping out a submachine gun and going to town, but they will defend you.<br /> <br /> As to betraying the friend, that's a bit iffy as well, I've had plenty of &quot;friends&quot; betray me in my time without any need for supernatural coercion, and most people aren't all that clever to begin with. But you're also better off if you don't risk it, as you never know who is truly loyal to their friends and who isn't. So instead of being like &quot;hey, George, when is your bff getting home, i want to break in and rob him before he gets back&quot; try &quot;hey, George, it's vitally important that I talk to your bff in person, do you know when he'll get home?&quot; They accomplish the same thing, but one doesn't require George to betray his friend.<br /> <br /> Again, it sounds like you're trying to force a square peg into a round hole, then claiming the round hole is underpowered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is still the third level of Majesty, and if your claim is &quot;the third level of Majesty is underpowered&quot; it cannot be discounted.</div> </div> </div> </div>interesting how an effect which is not working without the 4th level of the discipline is still being considered a level 3 discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:06:00-08:00","id":1526062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526049#post1526049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reassessing Majesty 3 applied to Confident and I had the feeling it is a bit too weak compared to even just Dominate 1.<br /> The book mention that any action that WOULD lead to a breaking point shatters away the charmed condition (so, in my understanding, before the breaking point occurs so before the action is taken, opposed to dominate where prior you have to hit the breaking point to be awakened, which make it far more useful). So, since almost everything, for a normal person, is a breaking point, does it seems fair to you? Unless you do not charm a professional assassin or a street thug, there are very few situation where a 3rd dot if this discipline can really be effective.<br /> <br /> Any thought?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that, design-wise, the emotion-shifting ability is the main bulk of the power, while the ability to command Charmed/Enthralled targets is an add-on that allows a Majesty user to encroach Dominate in a purposefully limited context. So the Majesty user still has to focus more on emotional manipulation than direct mind control, as intended for the Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:13:36-08:00","id":1526063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526059#post1526059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> interesting how an effect which is not working without the 4th level of the discipline is still being considered a level 3 discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can tell its part of the third level power because it's written under the third level power and before the fourth level power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:29:15-08:00","id":1526065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_pos