animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not punishing them, but, giving them a lesson in real-world physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a magic vampire power that resembles functional teleportation. Physics doesn't enter into it and it's frankly weird to expect wardrobe malfunctions from a physical Discipline shared by the &quot;glamorous vampire&quot; clan and the &quot;mysterious vampire&quot; clan. It would be like expecting Vigor dots to scale how huge your Nosferatu's quads are because they can jump that much higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T01:10:58-08:00","id":1526441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526430#post1526430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not punishing them, but, giving them a lesson in real-world physics.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you should forbid any player to use Vigor to jump from anything that is not solid concrete cause, according to physic and its third dynamic's principle (action-reaction), the force required to have an human body jumping 40 meters broad is enough to break almost any support from which they are jumping.<br /> Also, when shape-shifting, you're literally creating matter which is forbidden by physics. Or converting energy in matter, which although it's physically possible, since the energy converted from matter and vice-versa is immense, it means you should probably melt everything around yourself when shape-shifting in something smaller than you, or freezing everything around when becoming larger.<br /> oh, it's also unjustifiable a werewolf healing up from any damage without the expense of any essence, since they're repairing something without consuming anything - again, violation of a fundamental physical principle: energy/matter conservation.<br /> <br /> There's very little you can do in vampire sticking to physics laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-08-2023, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T15:18:25-08:00","id":1527129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1526441#post1526441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you should forbid any player to use Vigor to jump from anything that is not solid concrete cause, according to physic and its third dynamic's principle (action-reaction), the force required to have an human body jumping 40 meters broad is enough to break almost any support from which they are jumping.<br /> Also, when shape-shifting, you're literally creating matter which is forbidden by physics. Or converting energy in matter, which although it's physically possible, since the energy converted from matter and vice-versa is immense, it means you should probably melt everything around yourself when shape-shifting in something smaller than you, or freezing everything around when becoming larger.<br /> oh, it's also unjustifiable a werewolf healing up from any damage without the expense of any essence, since they're repairing something without consuming anything - again, violation of a fundamental physical principle: energy/matter conservation.<br /> <br /> There's very little you can do in vampire sticking to physics laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a great idea; thanks!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T07:10:35-08:00","id":1527371,"title":"","content":"Christmas question :P<br /> Yesterday night we had our Christmas session and a player, during a combat already on-going, declared to attempt a surprise attack using the last Celerity's active effect: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moving in this way is sudden, jarring, the vampire appears to shift from point to point without crossing the space in-between. She may use this to briefly avoid detection or launch surprise attacks </div> </div> </div>Since, an unnoticed player can always declare the attempt to make a surprise attack (by rolling stealth or whatever makes sense in that situation), he was challenging that should be possible to use celerity to, somehow, re-establishing the surprise even during a combat. How is your interpretation of this? How do you handle this mechanically? A bonus to a surprise attack but only if not already in a fight? You give the possibility of a surprise attack upon a successful surprise roll that wouldn't be otherwise allowed without using celerity?<br /> <br /> Thanks and merry Christmas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T09:19:52-08:00","id":1527377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527371#post1527371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since, an unnoticed player can always declare the attempt to make a surprise attack (by rolling stealth or whatever makes sense in that situation), he was challenging that should be possible to use celerity to, somehow, re-establishing the surprise even during a combat. How is your interpretation of this? How do you handle this mechanically? A bonus to a surprise attack but only if not already in a fight? You give the possibility of a surprise attack upon a successful surprise roll that wouldn't be otherwise allowed without using celerity?</div> </div> </div> </div>It gives you the narrative positioning to launch a surprise attack against someone who could otherwise see you coming; it's descriptive text on the &quot;you can move multiple times your Speed rating without being seen in the intervening distance&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> If this is happening in the middle of an existing fight, this would give the positioning to deny the opponent their Defense (possibly requiring a roll in the same vein as a normal surprise attack does), but once Initiative has been determined, the only way the full &quot;you get to act and nobody else does&quot; effect of surprise is happening again is at the start of a later fight or through mechanics that aren't simply rolling your relevant Attribute + Skill pool against their Wits + Composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T10:49:36-08:00","id":1527387,"title":"","content":"I see. I tend to agree with you. Otherwise it would be too broken. Perhaps I would allow it having the PC speeding away from the close combat, hiding himself from sight at least for a turn or two, to allow a surprise attempt again. I agree it should be role-played, not just a mere dice roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T08:11:56-08:00","id":1527424,"title":"","content":"I agree with the roleplay angle but I am conflicted on this, it says the movement is jarring and sudden like teleportation, it also does not say it uses your action if it uses just your movement you could feasibly use it to move and then attack I would rule that you could attack in the same turn personally since it does not state that you cannot, and teleporting behind someone would in my view be a surprise attack as it is not something most would expect. Under surprise attacks it states &quot;Characters who don\u2019t realize that they\u2019re about to be on the receiving end of bloody violence have a chance to notice the ambush by rolling Wits + Composure, contested by the attacker\u2019s Dexterity + Stealth.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would personally argue teleporting several meters and behind an opponent even if combat began would count as a surprise attack if you succeeded on the roll, I know I would be pretty damned surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T08:23:59-08:00","id":1527426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527424#post1527424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the roleplay angle but I am conflicted on this, it says the movement is jarring and sudden like teleportation, it also does not say it uses your action if it uses just your movement you could feasibly use it to move and then attack I would rule that you could attack in the same turn personally since it does not state that you cannot, and teleporting behind someone would in my view be a surprise attack as it is not something most would expect. Under surprise attacks it states &quot;Characters who don\u2019t realize that they\u2019re about to be on the receiving end of bloody violence have a chance to notice the ambush by rolling Wits + Composure, contested by the attacker\u2019s Dexterity + Stealth.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would personally argue teleporting several meters and behind an opponent even if combat began would count as a surprise attack if you succeeded on the roll, I know I would be pretty damned surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many times would you be surprised? Vampires are immortal, they know celerity is a thing, they've probably seen it used or even used it themselves. This isn't some super rare bloodline devotion that no one has ever encountered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T09:01:08-08:00","id":1527427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527426#post1527426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many times would you be surprised? Vampires are immortal, they know celerity is a thing, they've probably seen it used or even used it themselves. This isn't some super rare bloodline devotion that no one has ever encountered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that a surprise attack can also be from the person standing right in front of you going from a seemingly pleasant conversation to suddenly putting their fist in your face. It's not about whether you're seeing the attacker or not, or whether you recognize such tactics or not. It's about being ready for violence happening right fucking <i>now</i>.<br /> <br /> If you initiate combat by teleporting behind the victim, that's 100% grounds for rolling for surprise attack even if they are fully aware of that particular tactic.<br /> If combat is already initiated, you can't make surprise attacks anymore (even if you haven't participated in the fighting yet). However, your victim can only apply Defense to attacks they're aware of. If you teleport behind them, it's very reasonable to roll whether they're aware of you (and your subsequent attack) or not.<br /> Prior knowledge of such tactics (especially if the victim has dots in Celerity) can be used as a modifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T09:52:47-08:00","id":1527429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527426#post1527426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many times would you be surprised? Vampires are immortal, they know celerity is a thing, they've probably seen it used or even used it themselves. This isn't some super rare bloodline devotion that no one has ever encountered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires were not specified, could be humans or any other non-vampire thing, if they have celerity that can allow a contest of wills but if they do not have celerity, I would argue they likely may not have the speed to react or be aware of all of its abilities without routine exposure to it.<br /> <br /> They still get to make the roll of course which in this case would be wits + composure to know where the attack is coming from vs dexterity+ stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","user":"BloodyRelight","date":".  added more. 12-25-2023, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T10:20:32-08:00","id":1527430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527427#post1527427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that a surprise attack can also be from the person standing right in front of you going from a seemingly pleasant conversation to suddenly putting their fist in your face. It's not about whether you're seeing the attacker or not, or whether you recognize such tactics or not. It's about being ready for violence happening right fucking <i>now</i>.<br /> <br /> If you initiate combat by teleporting behind the victim, that's 100% grounds for rolling for surprise attack even if they are fully aware of that particular tactic.<br /> If combat is already initiated, you can't make surprise attacks anymore (even if you haven't participated in the fighting yet). However, your victim can only apply Defense to attacks they're aware of. If you teleport behind them, it's very reasonable to roll whether they're aware of you (and your subsequent attack) or not.<br /> Prior knowledge of such tactics (especially if the victim has dots in Celerity) can be used as a modifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>On rereading it, surprise specifies first turn of combat, so I think you are right! I see where I made a mistake. I would still use the defense penalty as you suggested since you cannot see the attack, but the robbing of an action is not called for thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T10:29:14-08:00","id":1527431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527427#post1527427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that a surprise attack can also be from the person standing right in front of you going from a seemingly pleasant conversation to suddenly putting their fist in your face. It's not about whether you're seeing the attacker or not, or whether you recognize such tactics or not. It's about being ready for violence happening right fucking <i>now</i>.<br /> <br /> If you initiate combat by teleporting behind the victim, that's 100% grounds for rolling for surprise attack even if they are fully aware of that particular tactic.<br /> If combat is already initiated, you can't make surprise attacks anymore (even if you haven't participated in the fighting yet). However, your victim can only apply Defense to attacks they're aware of. If you teleport behind them, it's very reasonable to roll whether they're aware of you (and your subsequent attack) or not.<br /> Prior knowledge of such tactics (especially if the victim has dots in Celerity) can be used as a modifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, it's no different from any other tactic, if you're aware of it, you can be on your guard against it. This seems extraordinary to us because it is, it's literally superhuman, but among people for whom the superhuman is ordinary it's just another tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T11:03:40-08:00","id":1527434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527431#post1527431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree, it's no different from any other tactic, if you're aware of it, you can be on your guard against it. This seems extraordinary to us because it is, it's literally superhuman, but among people for whom the superhuman is ordinary it's just another tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Just another tactic&quot; is the majority use case for surprise attacks. This is before you involve any supernatural abilities or powers. And if you want known tactics to be less efficient, just add a bonus modifier to the roll to avoid surprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T03:23:14-08:00","id":1527687,"title":"","content":"Do you &quot;experience&quot; a breaking point just before to do the action which would lead to that or right after doing that?<br /> <br /> Asking that to understand when exactly someone can actually resolve the dominated condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T05:41:58-08:00","id":1527688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527687#post1527687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you &quot;experience&quot; a breaking point just before to do the action which would lead to that or right after doing that?<br /> <br /> Asking that to understand when exactly someone can actually resolve the dominated condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right after. Merely entertaining the idea of killing someone/being tortured/encountering something beyond mortal ken isn't going to provide the shock the Condition is using as a narrative beat for resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T06:36:42-08:00","id":1527689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527688#post1527688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right after. Merely entertaining the idea of killing someone/being tortured/encountering something beyond mortal ken isn't going to provide the shock the Condition is using as a narrative beat for resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also one of the reasons that guilt-induced hasty last second embraces have spared PCs and NPCs from Humanity degeneration spiral by killing since 1e Masquerade. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T09:24:08-08:00","id":1527694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527689#post1527689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also one of the reasons that guilt-induced hasty last second embraces have spared PCs and NPCs from Humanity degeneration spiral by killing since 1e Masquerade. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't quite work that way in Requiem though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T20:19:11-08:00","id":1527741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1527694#post1527694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't quite work that way in Requiem though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in 2nd edition Requiem it definitely doesn't. Truth be told, life got in the way and i never quite embarked and fully familiarized me with it, years notwithstanding.<br /> Even harder nowadays with a V20-ish game of my own to ST in this last year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T18:41:06-08:00","id":1530415,"title":"","content":"Why do Vampire Embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T20:31:41-08:00","id":1530419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530415#post1530415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Vampire Embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>Companionship, influence, feeding, preservation of skills/beauty/knowledge, etc. The usual reasons you'd want to make someone stop aging and be less likely to die permanently plus the usual reasons you'd want to make someone more susceptible to your powers of persuasion and also capable of getting you the stuff you need to &quot;live.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also the whole &quot;the Curse wants to spread&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T11:12:23-08:00","id":1530570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530415#post1530415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do Vampire Embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>The usual reasons. The kindred is lonely and wants a friend or sees you as an asset to help with there plans or deny a rival a chance to embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T04:43:07-08:00","id":1530632,"title":"","content":"Do Vampire still take Bashing damage from Supernatural attack that do lethal damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T06:30:11-08:00","id":1530637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530632#post1530632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Vampire still take Bashing damage from Supernatural attack that do lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, yes, unless the supernatural attack has a rule saying it does lethal even if it would normally do bashing. For example a Gauru form's claws would normally do lethal damage to it's foes, but against a vampire they will only do bashing. On the other hand, the bite attack of a werewolf ALWAYS does lethal damage (unless they're eating you) including to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T11:09:01-08:00","id":1530655,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I have it in my brain that Vampires are able to show up on camera and photos if they want to or through blush of life, but I wasn't able to find a reference for that in the 2nd Edition book. Am I misremembering? I have a character in my current Chronicle who is an Idol and this is definitely something I want to confirm before complicating her life further with blurry photos and music video appearances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12268-touchofdivine","name":"TouchofDivine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T15:56:17-08:00","id":1530678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530632#post1530632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Vampire still take Bashing damage from Supernatural attack that do lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, unless specified in the power description itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T15:58:43-08:00","id":1530679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530678#post1530678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, unless specified in the power description itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give me an example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T19:04:23-08:00","id":1530697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TouchofDivine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530655#post1530655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, I have it in my brain that Vampires are able to show up on camera and photos if they want to or through blush of life, but I wasn't able to find a reference for that in the 2nd Edition book. Am I misremembering? I have a character in my current Chronicle who is an Idol and this is definitely something I want to confirm before complicating her life further with blurry photos and music video appearances.</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation you're thinking of is from 1e, where you could spend Willpower to show up clearly in mirrors and recorded media (spending a dot for it to be permanent) and the occluding effect was more pronounced. 2e's version of the Lost Visage is more about the Beast knowing how to place you such that clear evidence of your presence is hard to get; presumably if you want to leave a clear image you get a clear image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T03:38:06-08:00","id":1530727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1530679#post1530679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you give me an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Werewolf's bite is specified to deal lethal also to vampire. There are other examples although I cannot remember by heart. Perhaps the protean 4 Power specifies the claws deal lethals to vampires as well, while the protean 2 claws deal lethals to anyone but vampire (or other undeads).<br /> The point is that vampire, just for being undead, downgrade any source of damage by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-13-2024, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T15:38:29-07:00","id":1532454,"title":"","content":"Auspex 3 can be done on places; what's the extension of the place? Can it be a whole real estate or just a specific room out of it? If activated at the doorway is it for just the entrance or for the whole structure?<br /> Is the question: Is there any supernatural creature hiding here, legit? If so should it also give the nature of the supernatural (e.g.: werewolf or vampire)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-30-2024, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T16:15:31-07:00","id":1532459,"title":"","content":"Remember your questions are supposed to be about the place or object, I might allow &quot;is there anyone inside&quot; but &quot;is there anyone supernatural inside&quot; is certainly not going to fly. <br /> <br /> As to would it provide information about supernatural types, I would generally say not unless that information was very obvious to the object. Like if you touch a metal ball bat and asked it &quot;who did you last strike&quot; and it was recently used to attack a Gauru form Uratha, I would show that, but if it just struck a human looking being that would be all you saw. <br /> <br /> As to what's the size allowed, I would probably be flexible there, the more specific the location the more detailed than answer. Like if you try and ask a five hundred square foot home if there's anyone within you might get an image of the occupant, but if you try the same thing at the White House you may see, momentarily through 3 dozen sets of eyes but be entirely unable to make out any details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T12:43:32-07:00","id":1533364,"title":"","content":"If auspex 2 lets you blatantly ask this: &quot;Is this person a supernatural creature \u2014 and if I have seen them before, what is she? The taste of torn flesh. The glowing halo of a mage\u2019s nimbus.&quot; I have no reason to believe that auspex three would not allow a similar question since it states: &quot;A vampire can turn his Beast\u2019s senses on an object or place, uncovering secrets and destroying lies just as surely as if he had focused on a person.&quot; This also leads me to believe your usage is possible since it affirms: &quot;In addition to the sample questions below, the character can ask questions suggested for Auspex 1 and 2 if they would be relevant.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T12:54:48-07:00","id":1533391,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that the equivalent of &quot;is this person a supernatural creature&quot; for using Auspex on a place isn't &quot;are there any supernatural creatures in this place&quot; but <i>&quot;is this place</i> a supernatural place.&quot; Great for finding Wyrm's Nests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T02:34:03-07:00","id":1536194,"title":"","content":"<b>Question:</b><br /> How do I read the Blood Sorcery spell requirements in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>?<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b><br /> The Mantle of Amorous Fire (\u2022, Transmutation \u2022)<br /> <br /> Does this mean I treat it like a 1 dot ritual and ignore the Transmutation part, if I don\u2019t own <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T06:52:01-07:00","id":1536202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1536194#post1536194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Question:</b><br /> How do I read the Blood Sorcery spell requirements in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>?<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b><br /> The Mantle of Amorous Fire (\u2022, Transmutation \u2022)<br /> <br /> Does this mean I treat it like a 1 dot ritual and ignore the Transmutation part, if I don\u2019t own <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-24T07:49:42-07:00","id":1536204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1536202#post1536202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T02:54:25-07:00","id":1536238,"title":"","content":"<b>Question:</b><br /> Is there a formula or book that helps you determine the needed success for a blood sorcery ritual from 1e, if you want to convert it to 2e?<br /> <br /> (My goal is to convert the rituals from the <b>Circle of the Crone</b> 1e covenant book to 2e.)<br /> <br /> <b>Examples:</b><br /> <br /> <b>1e core book (p. 143): </b><br /> Pangs of Proserpina (1 dot ritual) = 1 success<br /> Cheval (2 dot ritual) = 2 successes<br /> etc.<br /> <br /> Rule p. 142:<br /> The number of successes required to activate a ritual is equal to the level of the ritual\u2026)<br /> <br /> <b>2e core book (p. 152):</b><br /> Pangs of Proserpina (1 dot ritual) = 6 successes<br /> Cheval (2 dot ritual) = 5 successes<br /> <br /> <b>Rule / Formula / Book: ???</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T06:34:20-07:00","id":1536248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1536238#post1536238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Question:</b><br /> Is there a formula or book that helps you determine the needed success for a blood sorcery ritual from 1e, if you want to convert it to 2e?<br /> <br /> (My goal is to convert the rituals from the <b>Circle of the Crone</b> 1e covenant book to 2e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As indicated in the sidebar, the calculations for target number are described in Blood Sorcery as total Theme dots used modified by any Ritual Factors added to the baseline effect.<br /> <br /> None More Dark Publishing's <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/463075/Requiem-Errata\" target=\"_blank\">errata book on the Storyteller's Vault</a> does away with the extended action aspect and instead make rituals an instant action with a narrative time component a la Geist 2e's Ceremony mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixing name typo 05-25-2024, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T08:31:58-07:00","id":1536256,"title":"","content":"<br /> Thank you again. You are really helpful!<br /> <br /> What I learned so far:<br /> <br /> The complete official guide for the update of 1e rituals to 2e should be found here:<br /> - <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</b> by Onyx Path Publishing (Based on Mage 1e)<br /> <br /> The unofficial update of that book is:<br /> - <b>Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation</b> by Christopher Falco (Based on Mage 2e)<br /> <br /> Another unofficial alternative 2e mechanic can be found in:<br /> - <b>Requiem Errata</b> by None More Dark Publishing<br /> <br /> Based on you answer and my goal to stick to the official rules before adding any changes, I will get <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies </b>to update my rituals from 1e books. \ud83d\ude42<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T13:42:52-07:00","id":1537353,"title":"","content":"Is it allowed to spend willpower for both the activation roll of a discipline like dominate or Majesty and the resisting roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T14:00:52-07:00","id":1537355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537353#post1537353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it allowed to spend willpower for both the activation roll of a discipline like dominate or Majesty and the resisting roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't spend more than one willpower point per turn, unless a power or ability specifies an exception, which isn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T14:01:52-07:00","id":1537357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537353#post1537353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it allowed to spend willpower for both the activation roll of a discipline like dominate or Majesty and the resisting roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are both things you can spend Willpower on, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-14T15:49:13-07:00","id":1537362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537355#post1537355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't spend more than one willpower point per turn, unless a power or ability specifies an exception, which isn't the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per action, not per turn. This is something the writers also forget from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T01:27:09-07:00","id":1537385,"title":"","content":"My bad. It wasn't my intention to ask if same character can both use a wp to boost and defend from a discipline, just if wp can be spent for both situations.<br /> Reason I'm asking is especially because I'm not sure how much someone is aware of a power being used on him, untill the effect either fail or ends.<br /> This is very true, in example, for Auspex. There's no way to spot someone using Auspex 4 on you, so why should you be able to male a willpower effort to contrast it.<br /> From a different perspective, who is using the power is normally advantaged by the higher number of dice given by the sum of 3 factors in building up the pool, so giving him also the possibility to boost i more with WP doesn't seems fair enough if the same possibility is not given to the defender as well, to at least mitigate it.<br /> <br /> I was indeed tempted to not allow use of wp for using/defending of/from disciplines, or even just giving this chance to the defender, to mitigate the disvantage given by a mechanic, too attackers friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-15-2024, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T16:44:04-07:00","id":1537438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537385#post1537385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bad. It wasn't my intention to ask if same character can both use a wp to boost and defend from a discipline, just if wp can be spent for both situations.<br /> Reason I'm asking is especially because I'm not sure how much someone is aware of a power being used on him, untill the effect either fail or ends.<br /> This is very true, in example, for Auspex. There's no way to spot someone using Auspex 4 on you, so why should you be able to male a willpower effort to contrast it.<br /> From a different perspective, who is using the power is normally advantaged by the higher number of dice given by the sum of 3 factors in building up the pool, so giving him also the possibility to boost i more with WP doesn't seems fair enough if the same possibility is not given to the defender as well, to at least mitigate it.<br /> <br /> I was indeed tempted to not allow use of wp for using/defending of/from disciplines, or even just giving this chance to the defender, to mitigate the disvantage given by a mechanic, too attackers friendly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being friendly to the user of a power is usually a good thing, as they have a big investment in both acquiring such power and putting it to use. But that's another discussion.<br /> <br /> You can use Willpower to boost Resistances (+2 to the trait) or Contesting rolls. Don't worry too much about awareness, this is more of a instinctual reaction than any form of conscious choice.<br /> <br /> In fact, even on normal rolls this expenditure is a Player decision, not a Character one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-20T21:14:20-07:00","id":1537746,"title":"","content":"I've heard that V5 took a lot of queues from Requiem 2E and I certainly recognize some familiar things when I got V5, having read R2E before. However, my experience with VtM is limited and I only have the V5 book to work with here, so I'm unsure how much and what exactly V5 took.<br /> <br /> <b>Full Context:</b> I wanna create some YT shorts and Tiktoks comparing Masquerade and Requiem, essentially going on about potential reasons Masquerade fans might enjoy Requiem better (fightin' for the underdog, basically). One of the topics I wanted to go for is how V5 took stuff from R2E. I wanna get my facts straight, though; don't wanna go over something that was actually done in previous VtM editions. That, and there's bound to be some things I don't know about myself.<br /> <br /> So to put my question more simply: could anyone here give a neat list of themes, mechanics, systems, vampiric lore, etc. that was taken from R2E and put in V5, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T13:16:40-07:00","id":1537768,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my best recommendation is that if your experience with VtM is limited enough that you can't distinguish which rules present in one weren't present in the other, you probably shouldn't be producing these shorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-21T19:47:35-07:00","id":1537778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537768#post1537768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, my best recommendation is that if your experience with VtM is limited enough that you can't distinguish which rules present in one weren't present in the other, you probably shouldn't be producing these shorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one else is producing such shorts, so I thought I'd be the change I wanna see. I don't have VtM 1st, 2nd, Revised, or V20; only V5 (and that was only so I could familiarize myself with what's currently being played). I don't wanna assume something came from R2E when it originally came from V20 or some earlier edition. So I thought of asking someone who had some expertise on the matter to verify my information before making a fool of myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T18:49:43-07:00","id":1537925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1537778#post1537778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one else is producing such shorts, so I thought I'd be the change I wanna see. I don't have VtM 1st, 2nd, Revised, or V20; only V5 (and that was only so I could familiarize myself with what's currently being played). I don't wanna assume something came from R2E when it originally came from V20 or some earlier edition. So I thought of asking someone who had some expertise on the matter to verify my information before making a fool of myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can you make a reasonable comparison, much less a compelling point, without any interest in understanding the game they like? You want to convince people without even pretending to care about what they like.<br /> <br /> What you're asking for is an enormous task, it is basically to teach you everything so you don't need to waste your precious time researching. This is not being the change you want to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T05:14:55-07:00","id":1540345,"title":"","content":"How do Inamorata actually work?<br /> <br /> &quot;Drinking the blood of an Inamorata causes the effectiveness of the Kindred\u2019s Disciplines to be reduced by half while she is under her Inamorata\u2019s sway.&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess that's clear enough for the physical Disciplines, but how should it be handled for the others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:23:40-07:00","id":1540362,"title":"","content":"I always take it as it meaning that the dots of Discipline are basically divided by two when under that effect. Like a Ventrue with Dominate 5 actually count as 2/3 (depending on how you divide his dots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T11:07:07-07:00","id":1540371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1540362#post1540362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always take it as it meaning that the dots of Discipline are basically divided by two when under that effect. Like a Ventrue with Dominate 5 actually count as 2/3 (depending on how you divide his dots).</div> </div> </div> </div>Closing off higher-level powers? Or just losing half the dice from activation and Clash pools?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T11:45:16-07:00","id":1540375,"title":"","content":"Usually I close off the higher levels because the Kindred is so smitten by the Inamorata that he just can't use his best assets.<br /> <br /> Now, if he does not drink again I also revert him to full control by the next Sundown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T12:38:34-07:00","id":1540379,"title":"","content":"&quot;Effectiveness&quot; reads to me as it should be half dice, or half of any relevant value within the power. But I think whatever works is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T03:27:28-07:00","id":1540933,"title":"","content":"Does Vampire get affected from poision and disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-23T04:50:01-07:00","id":1540936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1540933#post1540933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Vampire get affected from poision and disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e doesn't specify (though one of the Strix writeups mentions vampires &quot;not falter[ing] to disease or poison&quot; as part of the reason that Strix is disappointed in the Kindred for keeping up the Masquerade), Blood and Smoke having not originally been made as a standalone book, but 1e's rules noted that vampires are not subject to the effects of diseases but can still act as carriers and that most poisons don't affect them unless they destroy the blood a la some types of snake venom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T15:09:14-07:00","id":1541213,"title":"","content":"Is there any requiem book that goes into a little more detail on Blood Dolls? Just a slight bit, Luke more than the 2nd edition core","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T17:32:54-07:00","id":1541217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541213#post1541213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any requiem book that goes into a little more detail on Blood Dolls? Just a slight bit, Luke more than the 2nd edition core</div> </div> </div> </div>They're mortals who're addicted to the Kiss and actively seek to give their blood to vampire. 1e Core has a sample writeup and brief discussion of what kinds of people tend to become blood dolls (tilted somewhat by the literal first book in the gameline's proximity to Masquerade), but they aren't mechanically or narratively special except in the sense that, as 2e notes, particularly dramatic feedings might result in them having Persistent Swooning towards one or more vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T18:38:53-07:00","id":1541219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541217#post1541217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're mortals who're addicted to the Kiss and actively seek to give their blood to vampire. 1e Core has a sample writeup and brief discussion of what kinds of people tend to become blood dolls (tilted somewhat by the literal first book in the gameline's proximity to Masquerade), but they aren't mechanically or narratively special except in the sense that, as 2e notes, particularly dramatic feedings might result in them having Persistent Swooning towards one or more vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T23:40:35-07:00","id":1541267,"title":"","content":"Can ghoul diabelire a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T01:07:54-07:00","id":1541273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541267#post1541267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can ghoul diabelire a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Only Revenant can diablerize a Vampire to be uplifted to a proper kindred. Necessary condition (but not sufficient) to become a vampire is that you must die (or be dead - Revenant).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T09:01:41-07:00","id":1541291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541267#post1541267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can ghoul diabelire a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls can't commit the final act of &quot;eating the soul&quot; of the victim, that's just not something they're physically capable of doing.<br /> <br /> Even if they could, it wouldn't have any effect on them. As much as they're empowered by Vitae, they're ultimately just human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T15:02:17-07:00","id":1541304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541291#post1541291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls can't commit the final act of &quot;eating the soul&quot; of the victim, that's just not something they're physically capable of doing.<br /> <br /> Even if they could, it wouldn't have any effect on them. As much as they're empowered by Vitae, they're ultimately just human.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Usually</b> not, but bizarre caveats/exceptions/reversals of expectations are always possible in CotD - the Betrayed version of VII's origin even literally hinges on that and the Phanariot in Mythologis makes for another subversion of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-04T19:52:04-07:00","id":1541562,"title":"","content":"I never heard of ghouls consuming a kindred's vitae in such a fashion as they still have a foot firmly attached to the land of the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T18:50:38-07:00","id":1541826,"title":"","content":"In the Contagion Chronicle Player Guide it's said &quot;When committing diablerie, a vampire doesn\u2019t consume<br /> the rules-defined soul of their victim, obtaining multiple souls<br /> in the process, and they also usually don\u2019t leave clear traces of<br /> the soul that a mage could follow.&quot; Does this mean Vampire obtain the soul of their victim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T21:25:04-07:00","id":1541829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541826#post1541826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Contagion Chronicle Player Guide it's said &quot;When committing diablerie, a vampire doesn\u2019t consume<br /> the rules-defined soul of their victim, obtaining multiple souls<br /> in the process, and they also usually don\u2019t leave clear traces of<br /> the soul that a mage could follow.&quot; Does this mean Vampire obtain the soul of their victim?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the opposite of what that means, as better demonstrated by the post-errata version specifying that diablerie destroys the rules-defined soul of their victim. The victim's soul is gone, the vampire having derived a benefit from consuming it that nevertheless is different from having a whole extra soul attached to their body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T21:34:20-07:00","id":1541831,"title":"","content":"In the Contagion Chronicle Player Guide, it's said that non-vampire can learn Blood Sorcery, but how would they learn Cruc when it need Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T21:52:54-07:00","id":1541832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541831#post1541831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Contagion Chronicle Player Guide, it's said that non-vampire can learn Blood Sorcery, but how would they learn Cruc when it need Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitae spent in Cruac rites doesn't have to all come from the caster. I'd allow non-vampiric practitioners to cast entirely from Vitae spilled from other sources, which does still mean you either need vampire friends... or vampire victims.<br /> <br /> Barring that? Get ghouled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T01:54:05-07:00","id":1541840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541832#post1541832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vitae spent in Cruac rites doesn't have to all come from the caster. I'd allow non-vampiric practitioners to cast entirely from Vitae spilled from other sources, which does still mean you either need vampire friends... or vampire victims.<br /> <br /> Barring that? Get ghouled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corebook page 297 - Ghouls may not use Disciplines which require one to spill blood or feed it to others. so RAW that doesn't work??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T03:55:52-07:00","id":1541845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541831#post1541831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Contagion Chronicle Player Guide, it's said that non-vampire can learn Blood Sorcery, but how would they learn Cruc when it need Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541832#post1541832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae spent in Cruac rites doesn't have to all come from the caster. I'd allow non-vampiric practitioners to cast entirely from Vitae spilled from other sources, which does still mean you either need vampire friends... or vampire victims.<br /> <br /> Barring that? Get ghouled.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541840#post1541840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corebook page 297 - Ghouls may not use Disciplines which require one to spill blood or feed it to others. so RAW that doesn't work??</div> </div> </div> </div>One Vitae needs to be spent as regular, while the remaining Vitae cost is spilt by either the ritualist or supporters. That means ghouls can perform single dot rituals without help (as they only cost 1 Vitae), and all rituals regardless of dot rating if they have a vampire assistant to spill the remaining Vitae.<br /> <br /> Anyone else is shit out of luck, though, since they can't spend that initial Vitae to power the ritual. Nothing bars them from learning Cr\u00faac, though, if they wish to teamwork their resident Acolyte's rituals with the Altar Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-10-2024, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T04:00:14-07:00","id":1541846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541840#post1541840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Corebook page 297 - Ghouls may not use Disciplines which require one to spill blood or feed it to others. so RAW that doesn't work??</div> </div> </div> </div>They can spend the first blood point to activate the Discipline, all the other ones required must come from spilled vampiric vitae, from other vampires in this case","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T04:42:17-07:00","id":1541847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541846#post1541846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can spend the first blood point to activate the Discipline, all the other ones required must come from spilled vampiric vitae, from other vampires in this case</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean sure, that defo sounds cooler, and probably what was intended.<br /> <br /> RAW however says that ghouls cannot learn powers which require spilling of blood.<br /> <br /> So RAW, you cannot buy Cruac 2, because it requires spilling of blood.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As contested in a post following this, this is actually false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 09-10-2024, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T05:00:14-07:00","id":1541849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1541847#post1541847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean sure, that defo sounds cooler, and probably what was intended.<br /> <br /> RAW however says that ghouls cannot learn powers which require spilling of blood.<br /> <br /> So RAW, you cannot buy Cruac 2, because it requires spilling of blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spilling Blood: If a Discipline power requires the user to<br /> spill blood or feed it to someone (such as Raise the Familiar),<br /> the ghoul may not <b>use</b> it. You as a player may buy the power on<br /> the way to purchasing another one, however.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, you can buy higher levels of Cr\u00faac as a ghoul. You just can't spill the blood. And even then, as we've already determined, you don't actually <b>need</b> to spill the blood since others can spill it for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T05:57:52-07:00","id":1541854,"title":"","content":"You're right. Cruac doesn't require the user to spill the blood, so they can use it, and as such can learn it. Thanks for clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T20:20:04-07:00","id":1542290,"title":"","content":"How much do you need to cover from sunlight to not take damage or have the Blood Potency be one step lower? Is a umbrella and big hat enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T21:07:24-07:00","id":1542292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1542290#post1542290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much do you need to cover from sunlight to not take damage or have the Blood Potency be one step lower? Is a umbrella and big hat enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Mummy up, put together an ensemble that covers your entire body. You can leave a little band open for your eyes to see through. That will tick your effective Blood Potency on the sunlight chart one lower. If you're Blood Potency 1 and it ticks down to effective BP 0, you can just go out in sunlight without damage as long as you stay covered like that. At effective BP 1-2, you get ten minutes of sun exposure before you take damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T22:14:50-07:00","id":1542293,"title":"","content":"How long do you need to stay out of sunlight before you can go into the sunlight again? Like if I can stay in the sun for 9 minutes, step into a building for 1 turn, and step out, would I have 1 minutes left before I take damage, or do the timer reset and I now have 10 more minutes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T22:55:34-07:00","id":1542295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1542293#post1542293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long do you need to stay out of sunlight before you can go into the sunlight again? Like if I can stay in the sun for 9 minutes, step into a building for 1 turn, and step out, would I have 1 minutes left before I take damage, or do the timer reset and I now have 10 more minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go for the first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T00:13:21-07:00","id":1542299,"title":"","content":"Remember also that these are system abstractions. It takes ten minutes in the sun at effective BP 1-2 to hurt enough to inflict actual lethal injury, but that doesn't mean your character is feeling fine at minute 9 and then at minute 10 their arm falls off. The sun is harming you. It's painful and you can feel it even through your bundled up clothes. Little patches of skin start to slough off underneath your disguise. You are burning.<br /> <br /> That time you spend under sunlight is time you're shoving your hand onto a hot stove and holding it there. If you let go of the stove fast enough you can get away with only superficial burns, yes. But are you going to measure how long you can put your hand on the stove and how long you need to let it cool and heal before you can do it again without losing sensation in your hand? Or are you going to <i>take your hand off the stove</i> and avoid touching it again unless it's for some godforsaken reason absolutely necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T01:20:12-07:00","id":1542301,"title":"","content":"Aaand that's why I rule that you take the damage whenether you get exposed to sunlight, and this repeats at that interval of time. <br /> <br /> No &quot;I make sure I'm only in the sunlight for 9 minutes and 59 seconds!&quot;. Nop, the pure blaze of the sun has gotten to you. Your skin is roasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:07:04-07:00","id":1542386,"title":"","content":"Those takes aren't strictly RAW, either. I think letting it up to the ST to adjudicate is far more interesting than being obnoxiously determined to make it as hard as possible.<br /> <br /> By RAW, a band of exposure for the eyes has the effect <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> described. There is nothing in the RAW about sunglasses, so a more thorough setup may have more benefits or not depending on what is better for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> For \u201cresetting\u201d time, I\u2019d avoid making hard statements. But given that entering a building by itself is already an effort in any scene where it matters, I think 2 or 3 turns is probably good enough.<br /> <br /> How it feels is hard to say. I personally think it doesn\u2019t hurt beneath the clothes, only in exposed skin, after all, this is a supernatural reaction to the light of the sun, not to the actual heat. But YMMV.<br /> <br /> Making sunlight too scary limits options for no good reason. It is already a big problem by RAW, one that\u2019s more than enough to guarantee most characters won\u2019t try (and succeed) most of the time. Remember that even if the character dress enough to be \u201csafe\u201d, clothes rip, so exposure is still a risk.<br /> <br /> Without an ST call, though, I\u2019d say the only guarantee a player may expect is the -1 BP, and to need, idk, at least another 10 minutes in a building to prepare for another stroll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T18:46:02-08:00","id":1546414,"title":"","content":"How long can a Dhampir live?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T21:01:57-08:00","id":1546417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1546414#post1546414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long can a Dhampir live?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reference to vampires seeing a dhampir as &quot;plagued by human frailties and a mayfly life,&quot; combined with the fact that dhampir are rare enough to be a curiosity and have to be conceived on purpose (and, in contrast with biological ghoul families described in the same book, are not strictly speaking difficult to create), my takeaway would be that they default to a normal human lifespan.<br /> <br /> They're odd in their relationship to vampires and fate moreso than in the more material qualities possessed by ghouls and Kindred proper \u2014 they have subtle Twists rather than concrete Disciplines, and I get the feeling if it was intended that their condition came with a reduced rate of aging it would've come along with the bloodthirst and insomnia (to say nothing of it going unmentioned in the 1e material on dampyr from Wicked Dead).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T18:11:03-08:00","id":1547170,"title":"","content":"Not really a question, but for being anti-social, Nosferatu with their Nightmare-discipline, can really mess with mortals. For a clan that shy's away in the sewers, they can really **** up a mortal's life. I'd expect a more social clan, like Daevas to have something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T21:23:32-08:00","id":1547173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1547170#post1547170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a question, but for being anti-social, Nosferatu with their Nightmare-discipline, can really mess with mortals. For a clan that shy's away in the sewers, they can really **** up a mortal's life. I'd expect a more social clan, like Daevas to have something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though <i>some </i>are subterranean like their VtM kin and play with this element and something of a cthonic theme even, a lot of VtR's Nosferatu are <i>quite </i>social and immersed in mortal society through a number of ways. Damn, the corebook's version of New Orleans had a Nosferatu as harpy and owner of one of the most popular nightclubs among the kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T23:09:59-08:00","id":1547174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1547170#post1547170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really a question, but for being anti-social, Nosferatu with their Nightmare-discipline, can really mess with mortals. For a clan that shy's away in the sewers, they can really **** up a mortal's life. I'd expect a more social clan, like Daevas to have something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the Chronicles of Darkness generally setting supernatural power and socialization on opposite ends of a spectrum is that the Daeva screw up your life the way normal people with massive charisma and societal assets do and the Nosferatu stereotypically occupy a niche that allows them to make full use of the fact that nobody wants to talk about distressing unreality inflicted upon you by an unsettling man you encountered in a haunted house, where e.g. the Ventrue will settle for ripping your mortgage out from under you or turning your neighbor into a sleeper agent to cause a gas leak in your house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-04T21:26:21-08:00","id":1547536,"title":"","content":"Agreed that you can have Nosferatu that can be quite social and can be likeable in a fashion. Especially with good knowledge of Majesty and looking normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-19T20:28:04-08:00","id":1547840,"title":"","content":"It's said in the Quickened Sight description &quot;She can apply her Defense to ranged attacks, and <b>can benefit from aiming <u>instantly</u></b>.&quot; Does it mean that she needs to take an instant action to get all the benefits from aiming, or just gets them at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 01-19-2025, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T00:58:08-08:00","id":1547842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1547840#post1547840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's said in the Quickened Sight description &quot;She can apply her Defense to ranged attacks, and <b>can benefit from aiming <u>instantly</u></b>.&quot; Does it mean that she needs to take an instant action to get all the benefits from aiming, or just gets them at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it that, upon quicken sight activation, you automatically benefit of a +2 bonus for aiming on that very ranged attack, without wasting 2 turns for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T04:28:08-08:00","id":1547843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1547842#post1547842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it that, upon quicken sight activation, you automatically benefit of a +2 bonus for aiming on that very ranged attack, without wasting 2 turns for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aiming normally goes up to +3.<br /> <br /> This is extremely potent combined with the Marksmanship Style which (at the first dot, no less) sets the maximum to the character's Composure + Firearms. For a starting character, this can quite easily reach +10. For a maxed vampire it's instead +20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-20T10:09:37-08:00","id":1547853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1547843#post1547843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aiming normally goes up to +3.<br /> <br /> This is extremely potent combined with the Marksmanship Style which (at the first dot, no less) sets the maximum to the character's Composure + Firearms. For a starting character, this can quite easily reach +10. For a maxed vampire it's instead +20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It's +3. My memory failed me as aiming it's not a maneuver my players use that often (if ever)\ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T09:18:55-08:00","id":1548333,"title":"","content":"Do bodies under corporate still suffer under the effects of the Lost Visage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T15:13:42-08:00","id":1548343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548333#post1548333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do bodies under corporate still suffer under the effects of the Lost Visage?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, being in torpor means none of the &quot;the Beast knows where to stand&quot; manifestations work. On the other hand, immobility and unconsciousness shouldn't prevent equipment malfunctions from obscuring the vampire's identifying features. It would ultimately come down to how your table interprets the effect to work, but the equivalent sidebar in the 1e core makes no statement that it requires the vampire to be awake and torpor is functionally a deeper form of daysleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-09T22:00:07-08:00","id":1548353,"title":"","content":"Or you can ignore the lost visage in your game and not worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T02:57:02-08:00","id":1548839,"title":"","content":"Guys, how do you calculate animal stats (you know Protean transformation)? I noticed people have different thoughts.<ul><li>Some claim to use basic stats and upgrade them if kindred attributes are higher.</li> <li>Others said to use just kindred stats and few animal advantages (sight, smell, etc).</li> <li>And now I noticed suggestion to use Deviant stats (calculate species factor by [Speed-4], and attributes by animal avarage + our attributes - 2 or something, etc)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T04:15:53-08:00","id":1548840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548839#post1548839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, how do you calculate animal stats (you know Protean transformation)? I noticed people have different thoughts.<ul><li>Some claim to use basic stats and upgrade them if kindred attributes are higher.</li> <li>Others said to use just kindred stats and few animal advantages (sight, smell, etc).</li> <li>And now I noticed suggestion to use Deviant stats (calculate species factor by [Speed-4], and attributes by animal avarage + our attributes - 2 or something, etc)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>As written, you just use the animal's Physical stats, but still benefit from your Disciplines, including Vigor/Celerity/Resilience. Presumably if you want a form to be stronger without buying more dots of Physical Disciplines you would find and consume a stronger specimen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T04:20:35-08:00","id":1548841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548840#post1548840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written, you just use the animal's Physical stats, but still benefit from your Disciplines, including Vigor/Celerity/Resilience. Presumably if you want a form to be stronger without buying more dots of Physical Disciplines you would find and consume a stronger specimen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean I will lose some attribute dots if animal has less?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T04:25:48-08:00","id":1548842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548839#post1548839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, how do you calculate animal stats (you know Protean transformation)? I noticed people have different thoughts.<ul><li>Some claim to use basic stats and upgrade them if kindred attributes are higher.</li> <li>Others said to use just kindred stats and few animal advantages (sight, smell, etc).</li> <li>And now I noticed suggestion to use Deviant stats (calculate species factor by [Speed-4], and attributes by animal avarage + our attributes - 2 or something, etc)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Rules as written you just use the stats of the animal, no additional calculations (other than, naturally, applying physical Disciplines on top). Official animal stats can be found <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wild-at-heart/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and in DtR: The Clades Companion.<br /> In our group we have homebrewed a two-dot Merit for using the higher of the character's and the animal's stats while in the animal form.<br /> <br /> Swarm Form uses different rules from the regular animal forms. Exactly what those rules are have been debated on this forum, but I'm personally confident it's just the character stats with the Speed modification mentioned in the Merit text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T05:36:34-08:00","id":1548843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548841#post1548841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does that mean I will lose some attribute dots if animal has less?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because you're bodily turning into that animal plus whichever other supernatural powers you have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T13:47:56-08:00","id":1548891,"title":"","content":"Can Oath of Serfdom increase the disciplines above 5 dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T16:32:08-08:00","id":1548893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548891#post1548891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Oath of Serfdom increase the disciplines above 5 dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because Discipline ratings of 6+ aren't a thing in 2e and were only very loosely a thing in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T07:53:26-08:00","id":1548905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1548893#post1548893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because Discipline ratings of 6+ aren't a thing in 2e and were only very loosely a thing in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, but with 'Strength of Empire' devotion and physical disciplines not really needing a cap, I thought I'd ask.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T08:55:36-08:00","id":1549015,"title":"","content":"When we played VTR we would have no problems with the strictly physical Disciplines being over the 6 dot, but for the others it was 5 dot limit with higher level devotions being used in place for level 6 and up powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T01:32:13-08:00","id":1549068,"title":"","content":"I do think that physical discipline can be expanded beyond 5 throught devotions. <br /> <br /> In 1st edition there were a couple of official example of disicipline in combo with Blood potency to effectively rise it above 5. Not sure it's a thing in 2ed anymore though. That would also means that, by lowerig BP throught torpor, you would also lose access to that power.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you can combo different disicipline: e.g.: Vigor+celerity, etc.<br /> <br /> For non physical disicipline I don't ser a real gap. Level 5 discipline are already equivalent to a Masquerade level 7or8, in most cases, and throught devotions there are little to no limits. <br /> <br /> Physical disiciplines are the only ones I feel have not the same growth potential compared to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T07:10:35-08:00","id":1549079,"title":"","content":"If anything can increase Disciplines above five dots, it would explicitly mention that since it's an exception to the rule that Disciplines only have five dots. Since Oath of Serfdom doesn't mention that, it can't push Disciplines above five dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T05:34:13-07:00","id":1549553,"title":"","content":"Awe (Majesty 1) and Dread Presence (Nightmare 1) impose their effects to anyone, no roll required, unless they are a vampire who successfully lashes their aura against the effect. <br /> <br /> I would assume other supernaturals could also do such &quot;aura lashing&quot;. How would this look for example for mages or werewolves? Or will it just be a Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T06:02:03-07:00","id":1549555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549553#post1549553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awe (Majesty 1) and Dread Presence (Nightmare 1) impose their effects to anyone, no roll required, unless they are a vampire who successfully lashes their aura against the effect.<br /> <br /> I would assume other supernaturals could also do such &quot;aura lashing&quot;. How would this look for example for mages or werewolves? Or will it just be a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would definitively use an aura clash, but some other splats could ALSO have other powers to defend from the Discipline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T11:50:50-07:00","id":1549560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549553#post1549553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awe (Majesty 1) and Dread Presence (Nightmare 1) impose their effects to anyone, no roll required, unless they are a vampire who successfully lashes their aura against the effect.<br /> <br /> I would assume other supernaturals could also do such &quot;aura lashing&quot;. How would this look for example for mages or werewolves? Or will it just be a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves have a Hunter's Aspect they can invoke in response.<br /> Mages automatically contest with a flare of their immediate Nimbus.<br /> Bound can flare the Liminal Aura to contest.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, changelings, mummies, demons, beasts, and deviants don't have any corresponding mechanic. You could give them a Clash of Wills, require them to have a specific relevant power to resist, or in the case of changelings, you might consider allowing bedlam as a counter-response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T14:56:13-07:00","id":1549566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549560#post1549560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves have a Hunter's Aspect they can invoke in response.<br /> Mages automatically contest with a flare of their immediate Nimbus.<br /> Bound can flare the Liminal Aura to contest.<br /> <br /> Prometheans, changelings, mummies, demons, beasts, and deviants don't have any corresponding mechanic. You could give them a Clash of Wills, require them to have a specific relevant power to resist, or in the case of changelings, you might consider allowing bedlam as a counter-response.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually let Changeling use Bedlam as an aura contest.<br /> For Promethean i consider Disquiet as an always on and zero cost (but low dice) aura.<br /> For Mummies i use Sybarys as an optional aura flare, with modifiers to penalyze the resistance roll applied to other auras rolls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-26T08:49:07-07:00","id":1549584,"title":"","content":"Hello quick question a bout resilence:<br /> <img title=\"obraz.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1819_1743004073903_254\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1819\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1819\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1819&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"obraz.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> What does a Vampire may spend additional vitae to invoke resilience mean? can i use both resilience abilities at the same time or that i can use another vitae ability in the same turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-26T10:25:46-07:00","id":1549585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549584#post1549584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello quick question a bout resilence:<br /> What does a Vampire may spend additional vitae to invoke resilience mean? can i use both resilience abilities at the same time or that i can use another vitae ability in the same turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's elaborating on &quot;For each point of Vitae spent, choose one effect from the following list&quot; to state that you can spend multiple Vitae for multiple effects but (as the rest of the sentence states) you can't spend multiple Vitae to use the same effect more than once in a turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T10:00:05-07:00","id":1549673,"title":"","content":"Probably I or someone else has already asked this question, but I wasn\u2019t able to find the topic again.<br /> <br /> Doesn\u2019t it seem to you that the system of using large objects (like cars, tables, etc.) as improvised weapons via Vigor is too weak? I mean, if I use a car as an improvised weapon thanks to Vigor, the weapon modifier would only be the durability of the object (2 or 3), since you take the lower between Size and Durability. Isn\u2019t that a bit too low?<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking that when using and throwing large objects, it could at least be treated as an area attack\u2014requiring a dodge roll and not just a standard defense to act in the same turn. The idea being that the object is too large to be avoided through passive defense alone, and would require a dedicated action to properly dodge it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T16:54:26-07:00","id":1549690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549673#post1549673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn\u2019t it seem to you that the system of using large objects (like cars, tables, etc.) as improvised weapons via Vigor is too weak? I mean, if I use a car as an improvised weapon thanks to Vigor, the weapon modifier would only be the durability of the object (2 or 3), since you take the lower between Size and Durability. Isn\u2019t that a bit too low?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's better than the normal calculation for improvised weapon damage, which is simply Durability - 1, and the same Discipline lets you spend one extra point of Vitae to add even more. A +3 weapon bonus alone means even a glancing hit does half the health of an average mortal in a system where dealing a single point of lethal damage is enough to call for an end to combat whose goals are not purely violent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I was thinking that when using and throwing large objects, it could at least be treated as an area attack\u2014requiring a dodge roll and not just a standard defense to act in the same turn. The idea being that the object is too large to be avoided through passive defense alone, and would require a dedicated action to properly dodge it. </div> </div> </div>The largest object a master of Vigor can wield as a thrown attack without having superhuman baseline Strength is the Size of a sports car. At base Strength 10 a master of Vigor can throw an SUV. The mechanics for thrown attacks specifically subtract the weapon's Size from the range it can be thrown, meaning unless your Vigor-enhanced Strength is substantially above the Size of the object you're looking at a short range of your unmodified Dexterity + Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T01:33:50-07:00","id":1549703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549690#post1549690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's better than the normal calculation for improvised weapon damage, which is simply Durability - 1, and the same Discipline lets you spend one extra point of Vitae to add even more. A +3 weapon bonus alone means even a glancing hit does half the health of an average mortal in a system where dealing a single point of lethal damage is enough to call for an end to combat whose goals are not purely violent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but throwing a sport car, getting one success on the roll, has the same effect of hitting with one success using a crowbar (3 damages). That just doesn't feel right to me. That's why I would at least add some other difficulty such as making the attack an area attack that would require a dedicated action to be avoided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1549690#post1549690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The largest object a master of Vigor can wield as a thrown attack without having superhuman baseline Strength is the Size of a sports car. At base Strength 10 a master of Vigor can throw an SUV. The mechanics for thrown attacks specifically subtract the weapon's Size from the range it can be thrown, meaning unless your Vigor-enhanced Strength is substantially above the Size of the object you're looking at a short range of your unmodified Dexterity + Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said throwing but I would have kept that generic. It's also usable as meele attack. Moreover, a vampire in frenzy can - potentially - have quite higher strength (depending on BP level). In a dramatic effort he could also throw a Van, with even less damage than a SUV.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T10:36:03-07:00","id":1550045,"title":"","content":"I am thinking about a custom bloodline.<br /> Basically the benefit is that members can feed on human blood at any blood potency level.<br /> The curse is that they can ONLY feed on PURE human blood (no major or minor splat).<br /> Do you think it would be balanced/possible/interesting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:53:57-07:00","id":1550054,"title":"","content":"Balanced, no. Pure humans are still the most common resource a vampire can ask for. Not only that, it makes feeding into a supernatural detector, which is actually an advantage.<br /> <br /> You should have a far more steep weakness to compensate the ability to ignore the core disadvantage of high level BP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T12:34:10-07:00","id":1550055,"title":"","content":"I would add to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> said, that such a bloodline is basically opting out of diablerie. I mean, that does come with the downside that you can't make use it, but socially that's a massive part of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T14:39:53-07:00","id":1550059,"title":"","content":"Technically they can still drain the Vitae without consuming it and then do the deed. But being <b>known</b> as virtually incapable of committing cannibalism, however true or not, quite a perk for gaining trust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T13:04:00-07:00","id":1550078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1550059#post1550059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically they can still drain the Vitae without consuming it and then do the deed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that works. You're still feeding. The fact you don't get vitae doesn't mean it isn't part of the same process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But being <b>known</b> as virtually incapable of committing cannibalism, however true or not, quite a perk for gaining trust. </div> </div> </div>That's partly it, but my thinking was more that this is a fundamental part of being a kindred. Like, every kindred has to live with the fact that other kindred have a fairly clear reason to want to eat them. Conversely, every kindred has to live with the temptation to themselves perform diablerie. Even if socially vampires greatly frown on the practice, it still leaves a level of base paranoia.<br /> <br /> This bloodline just short-circuits that by removing all temptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T18:10:26-07:00","id":1550084,"title":"","content":"Yes, one of the intended consequences was making them incapable of committing diablerie.<br /> Any advice on how to make the bloodline more balanced?<br /> The core idea was to create a vampire dedicated to acquire a semi human state (it practices the Coil of Ziva) by ingesting only human blood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T02:49:59-07:00","id":1550096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1550084#post1550084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, one of the intended consequences was making them incapable of committing diablerie.<br /> Any advice on how to make the bloodline more balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe keep the weakness, but just don't include the ability to drink human blood past BP5. Like, at that point they both <i>need</i> kindred blood and are prevented from drinking it by their own weakness, so they have to go into torpor. I made me think of maybe a bloodline that watch over other vampires whilst they're in torpor. You can trust that they're not going to snack on you whilst you sleep. On the one hand, that's giving up a lot of power... but also, being BP6+ always seemed a massive hassle to me. Also, if your bloodline are centred on guarding vampires in torpor, then you're maybe less worried about going through the process.<br /> <br /> I suppose the other issue is how you want their weakness to actually manifest? Like, there's a difference between non-human blood just not being 'nutritious', it being actively bad for the vampire, or them absolutely being unable to ingest it. (The latter has issues to do with avoiding the downsides of ingesting other kindred's vitae.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core idea was to create a vampire dedicated to acquire a semi human state (it practices the Coil of Ziva) by ingesting only human blood </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. I suppose there's a question of how mechanically beneficial you want it to be?<br /> <br /> Like, I think there's a good in-universe reason to strip your own ability to drink from other vampires... But as a player, that doesn't really do anything, it's basically a purely roleplay thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T12:41:57-07:00","id":1550171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1550084#post1550084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core idea was to create a vampire dedicated to acquire a semi human state (it practices the Coil of Ziva) by ingesting only human blood</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your best option would be to make a Scale, not a Bloodline. Both mechanically and (if I'm understanding your intent correctly) lore wise. The advantage of making a Scale is that you can make the rite as hard to enact as you want, or in this case as you need. Indeed, you can go all the way up (or down) to feeding on animals, which is more human-like than feeding on, well, humans.<br /> <br /> But if you want the Bloodline badly, and it is meant for NPCs, well... it's really hard to think of a good counterpoint for this ability without more context. As a Bloodline benefit it has the problem that it doesn't do shit for most of the game, but when it does it changes the whole game, that's not much of a good design. But with better context things can change.<br /> <br /> What <b>exactly</b> do you want? Which characters will have this power? What'll they do? What role they play in your story? It all matters, and it may pay to open a new thread just for this, the answer for your question isn't simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T15:54:02-07:00","id":1550179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1550171#post1550171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think your best option would be to make a Scale, not a Bloodline. Both mechanically and (if I'm understanding your intent correctly) lore wise. The advantage of making a Scale is that you can make the rite as hard to enact as you want, or in this case as you need. Indeed, you can go all the way up (or down) to feeding on animals, which is more human-like than feeding on, well, humans.<br /> <br /> But if you want the Bloodline badly, and it is meant for NPCs, well... it's really hard to think of a good counterpoint for this ability without more context. As a Bloodline benefit it has the problem that it doesn't do shit for most of the game, but when it does it changes the whole game, that's not much of a good design. But with better context things can change.<br /> <br /> What <b>exactly</b> do you want? Which characters will have this power? What'll they do? What role they play in your story? It all matters, and it may pay to open a new thread just for this, the answer for your question isn't simple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, by the various answers i ve a more complete vision of what i need.<br /> <br /> The character is an NPC, a Pijavica several millenia old now living in the Arthurian Britannia setting of Dark eras 2.<br /> <br /> The idea is that initially she searched for power, but after she had obtained it... it seemed a pointless existence.<br /> Then she found love, a mortal lover in a village, nothing special but a really human person.<br /> She realized the weight on her soul caused by the impossibility to have children.<br /> And then the man died, refusing the Embrace.<br /> Torpor soon came and the memory of the most important man in her life faded and blurred.<br /> She swore to protect the memory of that man (the village and his relatives) and to transcend vampire limitation (Developing after centuries the Coil of Ziva).<br /> <br /> Now, the role of this Npc is to appear initially as a monster, using other vampires as pawns to secure the well being of the humans of a whole region (the descendant of the man spreaded).<br /> Most of the vampires are bloodbonded to her, and some are turned into Pijavica (she uses the devotion on &quot;a thousand years of night), their role is to aggressively protect their master cattle and playthings.<br /> Lot of rumors are spreaded on The Lady s cruel deeds, mostly contraddictory, she must be an enigma.<br /> <br /> But in secret she is very &quot;human&quot; with humans.<br /> Using the Coil she conceives Dhampir childrens that then &quot;gift&quot; to trusted families, protecting them from afar.<br /> But the last one, a young boy, he has the same eyes of that man.. she couldn t resist and she raised him as his son.<br /> But she knows that he can t remain hidden forever.<br /> <br /> -\u2010-\u2010\u2010-\u2010--------------------<br /> <br /> The Bloodline was an initial solution to avoid torpor (she doesn t want to lose sight of her children) and to avoid being bonded (she is extremely paranoic about trusting other vampires) but with this developement it would not be necessary.<br /> <br /> I ve only two simple question remaining:<br /> -the idea of taking the Unnatural Affinity merit on Dhampirs to resolve feeding restriction could work (or, can minor splats in general be used on this merit) ?<br /> -the vampire has Blood Potency 10 and a very &quot;evolutionary&quot; mindset. It seems unlikely that she would not develop or adopt a bloodline.<br /> Any advices?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T12:06:25-07:00","id":1550222,"title":"","content":"Are you comfortable with the idea of a PC getting <b>Unnatural Affinity</b> to feed on Dhampirs or other Minor template? I'm personally unsure if I would let it pass. Then again, are you comfortable with an NPC having a rule that the PCs simply can't reproduce? If yes, the first point is moot. It doesn't seem to be how the Merit was meant to be used. But then again, it can be abused even if limited to Major Templates, so...<br /> <br /> Giving ideas on Bloodlines is out of the scope of this thread, better to make a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T06:46:20-07:00","id":1550266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> he can shift the emotional state of anyone he\u2019s Charmed, sending them into a violent rage (or even a frenzy, in the case of some supernatural creatures) or making them so depressed that they feel hollow without him. </div> </div> </div>From Green Eye description, what's the limit of this emotional control? How would this not overlap with the first two powers of Nightmare? If I'm able to instill a deep fear in a victim, wouldn't that have the same effect of Nightmare 2? How would you deal with the effect from a mechanical perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-19T07:25:07-07:00","id":1550268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1550266#post1550266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From Green Eye description, what's the limit of this emotional control? How would this not overlap with the first two powers of Nightmare? If I'm able to instill a deep fear in a victim, wouldn't that have the same effect of Nightmare 2? How would you deal with the effect from a mechanical perspective?</div> </div> </div> </div>Green Eyes lets you play with a target's emotions as an extension of your having Charmed or Enthralled them; you might make them scared you'll leave them, but that's ludonarratively very different from conjuring brief illusions, making them afraid of you, or amplifying their existing phobias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T20:30:11-07:00","id":1551578,"title":"","content":"Can a vampire use Movement of the Mind to remove a stake to their own heart? It's more of a V;tM question, but I can't be asked to make a new thread in that forum just to ask this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-10T20:56:00-07:00","id":1551581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551578#post1551578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire use Movement of the Mind to remove a stake to their own heart? It's more of a V;tM question, but I can't be asked to make a new thread in that forum just to ask this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess no, but i'd say ST call in the end either way or if any action might call for a willpower/self-control/etc roll and or willpower expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T14:18:49-07:00","id":1551661,"title":"","content":"Are there any bloodlines that have plant stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28463-bwhite24","name":"Bwhite24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-13T17:14:20-07:00","id":1551668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bwhite24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551661#post1551661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any bloodlines that have plant stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Nosferatu bloodline with something of a focus on Mandragora, though i can't remember the name now.<br /> <br /> More broadly, you can tinker with the Of Rose and Thorn merit in Gangrel: Savage &amp; Macabre, that basically gets Animalism and unlocks a whole new powerset out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T00:21:56-07:00","id":1551680,"title":"","content":"If not mistaken the mandragora thing is a Cruac's ritual from some book I cannot recall at the moment. Can't remember of any bloodline power related to plants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T06:30:58-07:00","id":1551681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551668#post1551668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Nosferatu bloodline with something of a focus on Mandragora, though i can't remember the name now.</div> </div> </div> </div>A cursory search suggests this is the Adroanzi, whose writeup is in Ancient Bloodlines. Their signature Discipline Nburu improves their changes of successfully creating mandragora but doesn't have any powers specifically relating to the process; its third dot allows them to merge with plants at least as large as they are and its fifth dot allows them to move between such plants while merged, but the rest of the ladder just includes a stealth-boosting power and a plant/organic object-destroying power that both are less effective or ineffective on worked or artificial ground/materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-15T19:44:57-07:00","id":1551700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551681#post1551681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cursory search suggests this is the Adroanzi, whose writeup is in Ancient Bloodlines. Their signature Discipline Nburu improves their changes of successfully creating mandragora but doesn't have any powers specifically relating to the process; its third dot allows them to merge with plants at least as large as they are and its fifth dot allows them to move between such plants while merged, but the rest of the ladder just includes a stealth-boosting power and a plant/organic object-destroying power that both are less effective or ineffective on worked or artificial ground/materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are the ones i meant. Will also admit i never went deep into the nitty-gritty of their signature Discipline because i discovered the Gangrel merit first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T13:43:37-07:00","id":1551757,"title":"","content":"Anyone know how do banes interact with humanity 0? I was wondering if there was any official answer.<br /> <br /> Since banes are either clan banes or banes to protect against detachment, I'm inclines to say that once a kindred reach humanity 0 they are freed of all their banes. <br /> <br /> Otherwise this means that Ventrue are the ultimate Belial Brood, since they no longer need any touchstones, while Gangrel are the worst since they will never have more than a chance dice to resist frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T16:02:37-07:00","id":1551760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551757#post1551757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone know how do banes interact with humanity 0? I was wondering if there was any official answer.<br /> <br /> Since banes are either clan banes or banes to protect against detachment, I'm inclines to say that once a kindred reach humanity 0 they are freed of all their banes.<br /> <br /> Otherwise this means that Ventrue are the ultimate Belial Brood, since they no longer need any touchstones, while Gangrel are the worst since they will never have more than a chance dice to resist frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no indication that draugr doesn't stop interacting with Banes. The sunlight damage and Torpor duration charts both list values at Humanity 0, meaning at least some of them explicitly apply to draugr. Based on that, and how boring and weird it would be if draugr didn't have some glaring weaknesses to inform their behaviours, I'm confident draugr keep their Clan, Bloodline, acquired Banes, and the Bane against fire as well.<br /> <br /> As for the Ventrue, no draugr need Touchstones regardless of Clan, so their (in my opinion already badly designed) Bane simply doesn't have any effect. The Nosferatu Bane is also practically meaningless, and both acquired and Bloodline Banes might as well depending on the draugr's personality and habits.<br /> <br /> Edit: The Gangrel Bane, despite how bad it might sound compared to the others, might actually not matter that much anyway, since a draugr is liable to not actively resist Frenzy in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-18-2025, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-18T17:08:53-07:00","id":1551761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551757#post1551757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise this means that Ventrue are the ultimate Belial Brood, since they no longer need any touchstones, while Gangrel are the worst since they will never have more than a chance dice to resist frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The metric you're using would make the <i>Mekhet</i> the worst Claimed (or the absolute best, if one were to follow your inclination), but also the Dependent Condition that the Daeva curse works on uses detachment rolls as its primary deterrent, and as Tessie notes, the Nosferatu bane similarly only scales in terms of how badly rolls to interact with humans are; as for the Gangrel, in addition to draugr not being likely to roll to resist frenzy in the first place, the Feral Curse specifically doesn't apply to rolls to ride the wave and Belial's Brood don't spend Willpower to ride the wave.<br /> <br /> From a raw ludonarrative perspective, it also makes absolutely no sense for occult peculiarities that are mitigated by maintaining one's Humanity to suddenly go away with the final loss of that spiritual bulwark. The Requiem is a game where power comes at a price and inhumanity makes those prices more intense; mechanics like Blood Potency most consistently rising with age, bloodlines having attached banes, adoption or creation of a bloodline having a Blood Potency prerequisite, elder vampires picking up an additional clan bane, and the development of banes being a character-involuntary player decision to mitigate their descent into are there both to incentivize players against losing too much Humanity and to demonstrate how maintaining Humanity gets harder the older and weirder a monster you've become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-19T17:42:00-07:00","id":1551778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no indication that draugr doesn't stop interacting with Banes. The sunlight damage and Torpor duration charts both list values at Humanity 0, meaning at least some of them explicitly apply to draugr. l.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. I wasn't really thinking of the Sun as a typical bane, they should absolutely get cooked by the sun that's fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on that, and how boring and weird it would be if draugr didn't have some glaring weaknesses to inform their behaviours, I'm confident draugr keep their Clan, Bloodline, acquired Banes, and the Bane against fire as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fair, i think previously held banes should definitely influence a Draugr being influenced by their bane, i just don't like how it interact with humanity. Some banes are absolutely devastating, while others have absolutely no mechanical effect nor narrative effect. Draugr.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1551760#post1551760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Ventrue, no draugr need Touchstones regardless of Clan, so their (in my opinion already badly designed) Bane simply doesn't have any effect. The Nosferatu Bane is also practically meaningless, and both acquired and Bloodline Banes might as well depending on the draugr's personality and habits.<br /> <br /> Edit: The Gangrel Bane, despite how bad it might sound compared to the others, might actually not matter that much anyway, since a draugr is liable to not actively resist Frenzy in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, most clan Bane are rather meaningless for Draugr. The Mekhet one might be extremely crippling, or not register at all, but i'm honestly not very concerned about Draugr, as they are mostly mindless monsters rather than interesting antagonists.<br /> <br /> I'm more worried about Belial Brood characters and how some banes makes them barely able to functions while others are meaningless.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The metric you're using would make the <i>Mekhet</i> the worst Claimed (or the absolute best, if one were to follow your inclination), but also the Dependent Condition that the Daeva curse works on uses detachment rolls as its primary deterrent, and as Tessie notes, the Nosferatu bane similarly only scales in terms of how badly rolls to interact with humans are; as for the Gangrel, in addition to draugr not being likely to roll to resist frenzy in the first place, the Feral Curse specifically doesn't apply to rolls to ride the wave and Belial's Brood don't spend Willpower to ride the wave.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't completely disagree, i just don't like how it currently is. I think all clans should be equally roughly penalized by turning into claimed or not at all. Gangrel can ride the wave for sure, but they have to do so at any provocation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a raw ludonarrative perspective, it also makes absolutely no sense for occult peculiarities that are mitigated by maintaining one's Humanity to suddenly go away with the final loss of that spiritual bulwark.</div> </div> </div> </div>For basic vampire bane and clan bane, i agree they shouldn't completely disappear. Banes gained through detachment only serves to protect one's humanity in face of the beast, so they could explained supernatural subconscious mechanism that keeps the beast at bay. Once the beast fully take over, their is no reason for it to be shackled by those anymore. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Requiem is a game where power comes at a price and inhumanity makes those prices more intense; mechanics like Blood Potency most consistently rising with age, bloodlines having attached banes, adoption or creation of a bloodline having a Blood Potency prerequisite, elder vampires picking up an additional clan bane, and the development of banes being a character-involuntary player decision to mitigate their descent into are there both to incentivize players against losing too much Humanity and to demonstrate how maintaining Humanity gets harder the older and weirder a monster you've become.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but there's already a heavy price to pay for being Claimed ; a permanent condition is nothing to scoff at. <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the answers. I was wondering if i had missed anything. I might come up with my own solutions for Belial Brood clan banes, a bit like how elders gets a different version of their curse in TYoN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T14:29:31-07:00","id":1553776,"title":"","content":"If you fail a diablerie-roll or say, get a minimal-success, what if you got the Clan's weakness with the soul of the vamp? I mean, I would consider it a dramatic-failure, but, in reality, you can't get another clan's weakness if you don't get the soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T15:33:13-07:00","id":1553777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1553776#post1553776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you fail a diablerie-roll or say, get a minimal-success, what if you got the Clan's weakness with the soul of the vamp? I mean, I would consider it a dramatic-failure, but, in reality, you can't get another clan's weakness if you don't get the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could perhaps develop an aditional weakness not exactly through consumption of another kindred's soul, but by unintended fracturing/mutilation of one's own in a botched diablerie, i guess.<br /> Or one does extract it, but instead of consuming it, the extracted soul metastases within the diablerist as a sort of spirit tumor, a dark passenger bringing all the cons and then some of diablerie with none of the pros, among other possibilities. Just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-31-2025, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-12T16:29:35-07:00","id":1553780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1553776#post1553776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you fail a diablerie-roll or say, get a minimal-success, what if you got the Clan's weakness with the soul of the vamp? I mean, I would consider it a dramatic-failure, but, in reality, you can't get another clan's weakness if you don't get the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The standard consequence for a dramatic failure is a Condition, because it plays within the dynamic of the game and reward the player for seeking drama and tension.<br /> <br /> Adding a Weakness doesn't has a lot of purpose, unless you somehow link it to something. One option may be to have this new Weakness work as a Bane for the purpose of mitigating a Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T20:47:38-07:00","id":1554464,"title":"","content":"Stolen Vitae; say, can a mortal, drink vampire-blood, then, take a drug that stops the heart, thereby making them a vampire? Is that even possible game-mechanics? Would they be a vamp, but, game-wise, they had to die first, so, they rise every night with a permanent-wound? By the time they rise, the drug is gone; would that be an issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-18T23:37:58-07:00","id":1554467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554464#post1554464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stolen Vitae; say, can a mortal, drink vampire-blood, then, take a drug that stops the heart, thereby making them a vampire? Is that even possible game-mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering occult phenomena previously described in Requiem such as spontaneous rising and the post mortem embrace, i'd say that yes, such individual being &quot;tainted/cursed&quot; to a degree than sufficient for him or her to return as a vampire - possibly of the same clan as the &quot;donor&quot; of vitae, but not exactly (that might inform some secondary changes leading to incidental manifestation of supernatural merits or a bloodline instead, or nothing at all, even) - sounds pretty feasible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554464#post1554464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would they be a vamp, but, game-wise, they had to die first, so, they rise every night with a permanent-wound?</div> </div> </div> </div>About there being a wound - maybe, maybe not, could go either way. Depends on what sort of narrative one feels like experiment with, really (and wouldn't that be pretty much just an injection mark for either vitae or poison inoculation anyway? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> (Unless you got in your mind the idea of some major scarring/mutilation from blood sacrifice like might happen to a victim of the Sons of Phobos or another similar secret tradition of mortal <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_Sorcery:_Sacraments_%26_Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">blood sorcery</a>)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554464#post1554464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the time they rise, the drug is gone; would that be an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>About the drug/poison/venom remaining in the bloodstream and its potential, again, i'd say it depends on the individual circunstances and what kind of story player &amp; ST want to tell through it.<br /> One's return to death could take seconds, minutes, hours, days , weeks or more, the time interval chosen affecting considerably the chances of any substance lingering into the bloodstream or infusing itself in the corpses tissues, with as little and as large an impact as the idea suits one's imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-19-2025, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T01:03:28-07:00","id":1554469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554464#post1554464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stolen Vitae; say, can a mortal, drink vampire-blood, then, take a drug that stops the heart, thereby making them a vampire? Is that even possible game-mechanics? Would they be a vamp, but, game-wise, they had to die first, so, they rise every night with a permanent-wound? By the time they rise, the drug is gone; would that be an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to say that here's a big difference between what <u><b>can</b></u> and what <b><u>usually does</u></b> happen.<br /> <br /> This is not by any means an Embrace, and the &quot;default&quot; assumption would be for this person to simply die. An Embrace requires completely draining the victim and spending the Willpower Dot. Absent this, most victims will just die.<br /> <br /> But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> said, such a happenstance is within the boundaries of strange things that do happen within the setting. This individual is now tainted by Vitae, and by itself that's enough to raise as a vampire or something anyway, so this arrangement may very well increase the chances. <br /> <br /> At most I think the most probable result isn't a full clan vampire, but a Revenant. But at the very least I think this Revenant would already have the scent of the vampire &quot;donor&quot; to seek and Diablerize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T04:40:58-07:00","id":1554473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554469#post1554469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's important to say that here's a big difference between what <u><b>can</b></u> and what <b><u>usually does</u></b> happen.<br /> <br /> This is not by any means an Embrace, and the &quot;default&quot; assumption would be for this person to simply die. An Embrace requires completely draining the victim and spending the Willpower Dot. Absent this, most victims will just die.<br /> <br /> But as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> said, such a happenstance is within the boundaries of strange things that do happen within the setting. This individual is now tainted by Vitae, and by itself that's enough to raise as a vampire or something anyway, so this arrangement may very well increase the chances.<br /> <br /> At most I think the most probable result isn't a full clan vampire, but a Revenant. But at the very least I think this Revenant would already have the scent of the vampire &quot;donor&quot; to seek and Diablerize.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything. Just side note, embrace requires Humanity not willlpower. Willlpower is for ghouls.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T05:32:19-07:00","id":1554475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554464#post1554464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stolen Vitae; say, can a mortal, drink vampire-blood, then, take a drug that stops the heart, thereby making them a vampire? Is that even possible game-mechanics? Would they be a vamp, but, game-wise, they had to die first, so, they rise every night with a permanent-wound? By the time they rise, the drug is gone; would that be an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The act of the Embrace is a willful action; Vitae alone is not enough to wake the victim, a sire must choose to commit the Embrace.&quot;<br /> <br /> What you're describing is not a regular Embrace, but it does fulfil the prerequisites for a posthumous Embrace. I would use the rules for that, and add a bonus to the BP roll to represent the exceptional circumstance of having no time between moment of death and contact with Vitae.<br /> <br /> And if the posthumous Embrace fails, there's still the possibility of a spontaneous Embrace. The circumstances doesn't quite match the two laid out in the book (being exsanguinated, or being a ghoul) but I'd say having Kindred Vitae in your body at the time of death is close enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-19T11:21:21-07:00","id":1554480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554473#post1554473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just side note, embrace requires Humanity not willlpower. Willlpower is for ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was doing it from memory and the Willpower Dot was the cost in First Edition, my bad.<br /> <br /> For a Ghoul it's a Willpower Point, not a Dot. This didn't change between editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T09:10:01-07:00","id":1554774,"title":"","content":"Do we have any details on the Aztec covenant that seemed to exist? I know going by dark eras the priests kept a close eye to make sure kindred didn't steal blood for the gods but Shadows of Mexico mentions a number of aztec bloodlines that existed and had power.<br /> <br /> If nothing canon is there any homebrew for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T19:39:24-07:00","id":1554808,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554774#post1554774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any details on the Aztec covenant that seemed to exist? I know going by dark eras the priests kept a close eye to make sure kindred didn't steal blood for the gods but Shadows of Mexico mentions a number of aztec bloodlines that existed and had power.<br /> <br /> If nothing canon is there any homebrew for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only small bits and pieces peppered across the books, no major exploration of pre-columbian kindred since Shadows of Mexico. While there was an aztec-inspired Dark Era, it was focused on Forsaken &amp; Demon, if memory tricks me not.<br /> <br /> That said there have been some quite interesting teasers for a player or ST to use as hooks or extrapolate all sorts of homebrew lore from.<br /> More than one thread compiling part of them through the years, as seen <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177930-ceceya-and-shadows-of-mexico\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1173804-native-american-vampires#post1266229\">here </a>and also with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1439928-when-would-each-group-have-gotten-to-the-americas#post1440110\">this</a>.<br /> A good spread of ingredients to experiment with or mix for any fancy imaginings one might feel like dishing out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T16:39:26-08:00","id":1555223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1554774#post1554774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any details on the Aztec covenant that seemed to exist? I know going by dark eras the priests kept a close eye to make sure kindred didn't steal blood for the gods but Shadows of Mexico mentions a number of aztec bloodlines that existed and had power.<br /> <br /> If nothing canon is there any homebrew for them?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Shadows of Mexico</i>, being NWoD, I tended to keep it in context with WoD rules, that is, no major creatures like vampires or werewolves. I did run it with Immortals in mind. The players faced Blood-Bathers and the Purifed, thinking they were, vampires and a new sect/clan they hadn't heard of and Predator's Taint, didn't work on them, they assumed they were something akin to VII.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T11:30:43-08:00","id":1555275,"title":"","content":"I know CoD has a new sunlight-damage system based on your humanity and Blood-Potency; now, just how much more effective, in game-play is that system vs. the 1e Requiem sunlight-damage? Same goes with Forsaken, harmony, and silver-damage. In the OG rules, it's been effective enough to deter each to their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T12:12:17-08:00","id":1555278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555275#post1555275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know CoD has a new sunlight-damage system based on your humanity and Blood-Potency; now, just how much more effective, in game-play is that system vs. the 1e Requiem sunlight-damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, sunlight damage was immediate and consistent and aggravated regardless of how potent or humanlike you were, with specific exceptions like the Mekhet clan weakness, scaling only with degree of exposure and intensity, such that as soon as someone turns into a vampire they would be vaporized in under ten seconds if thrown out on the street in the middle of the day without a shirt.<br /> <br /> In 2e, Kindred vampirism is meant to facilitate a more gradual slide from human to inhuman, as demonstrated by a new Humanity 7, Blood Potency 1 vampire needing ten minutes of exposure to sunlight to take a point of lethal damage and being able to avoid even that if almost totally covered; the same principle is why Clan Banes don't kick in until you first drop below Humanity 7 and elders develop a further Clan Bane at Humanity 3.<br /> <br /> In this model, it makes sense for 1e's level of sunlight damage in 2e to be the stuff of notably old and monstrous Kindred who use neonates for their greater surface mobility, in addition to bringing the Kindred a little closer to the rest of the supernatural world's denizens after ten years of power creep and a marked effort to more cleanly distinguish Requiem's vampires from Masquerade's without those attempts being to Requiem's detriment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same goes with Forsaken, harmony, and silver-damage. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf 2e didn't change the way silver damage works in any significant way \u2014 &quot;taking aggravated damage&quot; and &quot;taking damage from silver&quot; are nearly identical in practice \u2014 and the main distinction is that 2e makes Death Rage a two-stage process scaled from Harmony and Primal Urge where 1e had no buffer and the consequences of failing the roll to resist simply lasted until the end of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-09T13:22:57-08:00","id":1555283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555275#post1555275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know CoD has a new sunlight-damage system based on your humanity and Blood-Potency; now, just how much more effective, in game-play is that system vs. the 1e Requiem sunlight-damage? Same goes with Forsaken, harmony, and silver-damage. In the OG rules, it's been effective enough to deter each to their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that simply deterring them isn't good design.<br /> <br /> Harsh damage just means you have fewer avenues for telling stories because they're completely blocked by insta-kill, and it also fails to deliver the point of having a scale to begin with.<br /> <br /> Now most vampires suffer less damage from the sun, and have more means to mitigate it. The result is that doing things by day becomes feasible, if still not easy, as long as you plan ahead of time and don't try anything too crazy. That's also great for crossovers, but it's good even for pure Vampire games.<br /> <br /> And now you actually feel the difference from loosing it. You feel that things you could do before become too hard or impossible as you become more monstrous, instead of just having a few less or more seconds of life under the big ball of fire on the sky.<br /> <br /> Forsaken mostly does the same as before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T01:09:34-08:00","id":1555307,"title":"","content":"I overall think that the damage system from sunlight is quite good and balanced as it's showing the progression through montruosity. Sunlight is still a think also for Humanity 7 BP 1 vampires. Even if not so deadly as it was in 1ed, you still don't want to go around at day time. Not only because the raw damage - which is manageble - but also because ppl around would see you with your skin getting burnt and blosters popping up (like in afflicted movie in my view.)<br /> Also considering the permanent 2/4 dice of penality untill a full day sleep. Which means you have to deal with a -4 for the whole night after you stayed active during the day.<br /> <br /> Moreover, from a damage point of view, even though I can't recall if it was hardruled by the corebook, I personally do not allow to heal up damage during exposure. I don't see the lethal damage as occurring suddenly every 10 minutes of exposure (like she was hitted by a baton evey 10 minutes), but a damage occurred over time (over the 10 minutes). So I wouldn't allow to heal the damage for an ongoing harm.<br /> <br /> It gives the young vampire room of survival in case of emergency but it's still nothing less than hard to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T15:32:01-08:00","id":1555335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555307#post1555307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, from a damage point of view, even though I can't recall if it was hardruled by the corebook, I personally do not allow to heal up damage during exposure.<br /> <br /> It gives the young vampire room of survival in case of emergency but it's still nothing less than hard to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it doesn't stop you from healing, and I don't think it should, you're still consuming resources to do it, and it is a supernatural effect, not a natural thing. No healing is natural for vampires.<br /> <br /> You can also avoid damage with sufficient clothing, which is feasible in most places most of the time, it doesn't have to be heavy clothes, just to cover skin completely. It may be weird to be on a tropical beach with gloves and hat, but looking like a weirdo beats looking like barbecue. Also you can always claim a skin condition.<br /> <br /> Overall I think the penalties and demands are well balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T18:44:14-08:00","id":1555653,"title":"","content":"I was hoping I could get some help on &quot;getting&quot; the Lancea.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling to think of reasons anyone would see the Lancea as anything but losers and nutjobs even compared to the other covenants. I get the holy avenger angle, the batman/daredevil beating up the worst of mortal society and scaring the light of god into them. It and the lorekeeper angle are cool. I also understand they aren't catholic or even Christian but do believe they are divinely appointed.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't see what they offer that the other covenants don't blow them out of the water in. They don't offer any afterlife, they just say that all vampires are damned to Hell and they can rule in Hell (because ruling in a place doomed to be blown up is a positive??) They revel in being assholes. They feel more like a bunch of losers who wanted an excuse to be cruel to others and don't have the spine to admit it like the Circle do.<br /> <br /> To quote another who laid out all my problems with the Lance so well, <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/958806-why-is-it-so-easy-to-root-for-the-circle-against-the-sanctum?p=958904#post958904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Speaking for myself, there's also the different perceptions fostered by the different lores underlying each Covenant's credo.<br /> <br /> The Circle's philosophy is that vampires are natural in their own right; being a vampire is a normal thing, nothing to be ashamed of - indeed, it's something to be proud of. Crones accept who they are and make peace with their nature, trying to live what they consider a &quot;good&quot; unlife without hypocritically denying that their nature requires them to prey upon and sometimes kill human beings. A vampire isn't really human anymore, and the Circle accepts that; but just because a wolf does not cry when it eats a bunny does not mean it can't try to be a responsible wolf.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum, on the other hand, seems to build itself around some of the worst perceivable aspects of Christianity; excessive self-flagellation (&quot;woe is me, for I am cursed by god and will never be shown his merciful light again&quot;), hypocritical self-righteousness (&quot;in my damnation, god has empowered me to act as his scourge upon the wicked&quot;) and aggressive proselytizing (&quot;all man must heed unto god, and my depredations will punish those who stray from the flock&quot;). It paints the Sanctified as, ironically, more monstrous than Crones; these are vampires who will justify all the evil they do as &quot;God's Work&quot;, adding the least appealing traits of a fanatic's mentality to the already unpleasant aspects of life as a vampire.<br /> <br /> This, to me at least, paints a mental portrait of the typical Sanctified as either a cringing, passive-aggressive beast with no pride in itself, or as a cruel, hypocritical fanatic, whilst the Crone's portrait is of a proud, self-assured and stable vampire who accepts what they are and owns it. I don't know about anyone else, but to me, this makes the Crones far more interesting and personally appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This just doesn't seem appealing. If I'm joining one of the two religious covenants, and one is having parties and telling everyone they shouldn't be ashamed, while the other is doing the same with eyes wide shut parties but with added hypocrisy and acting like they are better for pretending to be just monsters instead of the monsters they are.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice or ideas to make them more appealing or to give a deeper look into their theology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28147-snailslayer","name":"Snailslayer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T19:09:41-08:00","id":1555656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555653#post1555653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping I could get some help on &quot;getting&quot; the Lancea.<br /> <br /> . . .<br /> <br /> This just doesn't seem appealing. If I'm joining one of the two religious covenants, and one is having parties and telling everyone they shouldn't be ashamed, while the other is doing the same with eyes wide shut parties but with added hypocrisy and acting like they are better for pretending to be just monsters instead of the monsters they are.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice or ideas to make them more appealing or to give a deeper look into their theology?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's really nothing appealing about the Lancea Sanctum. I've got the book, and, it's very boring. I wanted them to be life Ann Rice's medieval satanic-vampires. The book is as fun as the Catholic-church. <br /> <br /> And all religions are about hypocrisy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:07:26-08:00","id":1555665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555653#post1555653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also understand they aren't catholic or even Christian but do believe they are divinely appointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first thing is this. The <i>Lancea</i> <b>IS</b> Christian, and mostly Catholic, although they have elements of some early sects and some schismatic churches (Christianity had a lot of schisms before the Protestant Reform, since Nicea and up to the 12th century).<br /> <br /> And that is the key to understand them. Not because this is in some way representative of actual Christianity, but because <i>vampires already have beliefs when Embraced</i>. And after that, they'll still live in a society with a dominant belief system.<br /> <br /> You don't chose what you believe in, so analyzing those Covenants through a logical examination of what they offer misses the whole point. If you're the kind of person that's picking and choosing what to live and fight for, then you're not the kind of person that'll go far in a religious group to begin with, you may like, but you don't believe. And by the way, that applies to RL religions, too, as many of the criticism you make at the <i>Lancea</i> isn't too dissimilar with many of the criticism against actual religions that a lot of actual people believe in.<br /> <br /> So, there are actually two possible reasons for someone to follow the <i>Lancea</i>. The first and probably stronger in many cases, especially in the past, is that this person is already a Christian, the single most common religion (or group of religions) in the world. You may have been pious when mortal, or may have taken the Embrace and Kindred existence as a personal revelation, but you do believe in Jesus and the Bible. For those people the <i>Lancea</i> offers meaning within a framework that makes sense to them. Any advantage from the <i>Circle</i> gets negated by the fact they're heathens and witches, and work for other Covenants doesn't seems more important than the work of YHWH.<br /> <br /> Now, certainly characters can still think the <i>Lancea</i> does not reflects their religious beliefs. But they can't simply decide not to believe. If they want to live by the Work they have very few options, and they may face persecution if they try those that involve heresy in the eyes of the powerful. For the player the religious Covenant is a choice for a fictional character, but for said character it feels like something else, especially when it comes to religious Covenants.<br /> <br /> Religion is also about community, about feeling part of a group, and about showing piety to feel validated in the group and by the group. It's about liturgy and rites and stuff not because they give you direct benefits, but because they build shared experience and meaning. So the second reason is with whom you socialize. And here we have one of the strongest advantages of the <i>Lancea</i> over the <i>Circle</i> (and I say that as both a fan of the <i>Circle</i> and a pagan IRL): it creates and manages public spaces and rituals. It builds community with everyone, not just <i>Lancea</i> members, where the <i>Circle</i> <b>usually</b> has only closed affairs.<br /> <br /> Building community by itself is a powerful thing because the <i>Lancea</i> is frequently a &quot;second home/common ground&quot; for a lot of Vampires. On your &quot;typical&quot; city members of the <i>Invictus</i> and the <i>Unaligned</i> Kindred frequent the church, <i>Ordo</i> and <i>Carhian</i> may or may not, but are still possibly there, and it's even possible that some of the <i>Circle</i> go just because it's the main weekly social gathering in town. Even without that, though, if the local community is mostly Christian, then most new vampires will end up Christians if they weren't already, if you socialize your whole life with the Catholic rites and community, you'll feel at home with Catholic-like rites and community, and so on.<br /> <br /> Many other reasons may apply for someone to be a <i>Lancea</i>, and for the player to want to explore it. More than the <i>Circle</i>, they are used to partnership with political power structures and direct secular power. Some people want to live the idea of martyrdom, of suffering either because they feel guilt or because this massages their ego in the right way. Lots of people like the &quot;holier than thou&quot; attitude, and/or to preach and tell others how those others are wrong while they're saintly and right. Many like to have a reason to justify their desire for violence or cruelty, maybe because justification brings good feelings, maybe because justification makes doing so easier. Sometimes people don't really have a choice at all, the religion is mandatory in the city, or at least by their sire, and when they have the means to leave it behind they're already too entrenched and empowered by it to go ahead.<br /> <br /> Of course, from the Five Covenants I think the <i>Lancea</i> is the most likely one to not work on a lot of places. It makes a lot of sense in mainly Catholic areas, and then less sense the less influence you have from hardcore Christianity, or even worse, more influence from other religions. Similar but at the same time very different Covenants should replace the <i>Lancea</i> at many places in the world, matching local religions. But overall in Europe or the Americas, especially southern US and LatAm, I think the <i>Lancea</i> works pretty well as a point of familiarity, a dark reflection of mainstream religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:07:45-08:00","id":1555666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555653#post1555653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping I could get some help on &quot;getting&quot; the Lancea.<br /> <br /> I'm struggling to think of reasons anyone would see the Lancea as anything but losers and nutjobs even compared to the other covenants. I get the holy avenger angle, the batman/daredevil beating up the worst of mortal society and scaring the light of god into them. It and the lorekeeper angle are cool. I also understand they aren't catholic or even Christian but do believe they are divinely appointed.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't see what they offer that the other covenants don't blow them out of the water in. They don't offer any afterlife, they just say that all vampires are damned to Hell and they can rule in Hell (because ruling in a place doomed to be blown up is a positive??) They revel in being assholes. They feel more like a bunch of losers who wanted an excuse to be cruel to others and don't have the spine to admit it like the Circle do.<br /> <br /> To quote another who laid out all my problems with the Lance so well,<br /> <br /> This just doesn't seem appealing. If I'm joining one of the two religious covenants, and one is having parties and telling everyone they shouldn't be ashamed, while the other is doing the same with eyes wide shut parties but with added hypocrisy and acting like they are better for pretending to be just monsters instead of the monsters they are.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any advice or ideas to make them more appealing or to give a deeper look into their theology?</div> </div> </div> </div>For start, do you mean appealing for you as a player or for an in game character to join in?<br /> As a player i would find really challenging to portray such a contraddictory character, but i understand that for someone it would be simply not worth the effort.<br /> As the in game character instead.... well i think that the greatest motivation to join Lancea (and all religions by the way) is fear, fear of unknow and of death.<br /> Lancea gives answers, a lot of answers, easy and appealing answers, and a sense of safety that only great power and group dynamics can offer.<br /> I can also imagine that the quote &quot;hey, Theban sorcery works, God lets us do its miracles, we are good guys&quot; resonates eternally in their churches, conveniently ignoring the fact that Cruac is almost the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T22:55:26-08:00","id":1555671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snailslayer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1555653#post1555653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I don't see what they offer that the other covenants don't blow them out of the water in. They don't offer any afterlife, they just say that all vampires are damned to Hell and they can rule in Hell (because ruling in a place doomed to be blown up is a positive??)</div> </div> </div> </div>Genuine question: Why are you bringing up the afterlife for a religion that ministers to immortal corpses whose stated Earthly goal is making sure good people don't turn bad and bad people get punished and the rules of society are upheld?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They revel in being assholes. They feel more like a bunch of losers who wanted an excuse to be cruel to others and don't have the spine to admit it like the Circle do. </div> </div> </div>They have a nominal purpose that relates to keeping the world from changing so much that they don't have a place in it. If they were Embraced into the covenant it was because someone saw something worth preserving in them to the end of stress-testing the virtuous, making examples of sinners, or steering society toward maintaining its traditions. Not having any hope of redemption and thus leaning into a constructive form of their damnation \u2014 damnation likely levied on them by another vampire for their actions as a mortal \u2014 is notably different from &quot;reveling in being an asshole,&quot; just as the Circle having an ideology that treats the supernatural as part of nature does not mean they are the Chill Vibes Covenant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This just doesn't seem appealing. If I'm joining one of the two religious covenants, and one is having parties and telling everyone they shouldn't be ashamed, while the other is doing the same with eyes wide shut parties but with added hypocrisy and acting like they are better for pretending to be just monsters instead of the monsters they are. </div> </div> </div>The Sanctum is organized. They owe some of their big break to early Christianity hitching its wagon to the Roman Empire, and this organization and their lorekeeper/relic-hunter mode mean they are one of the major covenants best equipped for travel. The Ordo Dracul's niche includes squatting on real estate that normal people typically avoid and the Circle of the Crone is sufficiently sedentary that they're one of the primary textual use-cases for &quot;what happens if you make a garden full of ghouled plants?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Sanctum is (nominally) responsible. Their magic relies on intelligence, non-fungible sacrifice, and the cultivation and maintenance of a level of self-control and human comprehension typical of the average neonate to optimally work, so they are further incentivized to avoid the pitfalls of allowing their elders to fall out of touch with the herd. The Condition their blood sorcery instills on an exceptional success (which lay members can also provide with a proprietary Merit directly comparable to Inspiring) makes them better at controlled frenzy. Even if their claim that the Traditions came from them is false, that still demonstrates that they are invested in those laws of the All Night Society. Hypothetical Responsible Acolytes and Dragons do not outweigh the fact that Cr\u00faac stunts Humanity and runs on spilled blood and Coil research involves no small amount of unethical humanoid experimentation.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum is big. They're typically deliberately playing second fiddle to the Invictus in most domains because it turns out that it's real easy for the covenant with strong incentives to control information and supernatural resources to get in bed with something that calls itself The Conspiracy of Silence. Not for nothing does Hunter 1e's writeup of the Malleus Maleficarum's note on the gaps in secret ghoul Ambrogio Baudolino's pet witch-hunting conspiracy's knowledge of vampire society still boil down to &quot;it's useful to know that the Invictus, the Carthians, the Lancea, and the Brood exist in broad ideological strokes, but the rest is irrelevant.&quot; Whether they're fairly or unfairly persecuted by other groups (including the Lancea), the Circle and the Ordo are the smallest of the major covenants and are institutionally characterized as cultish or disinterested in participating in city politics.<br /> <br /> The Sanctum is not about having an orgy and saying it's for the greater good, it's about selling a form of vampirism that gives its bearers something to agree on to do that isn't going to step on too many important toes and has an ideological reason for it that they can take some comfort in while they carefully acclimate to losing their heartbeat and reversing their sleep/wake cycle after breaking the wrong taboos too many times. It's about vampirism being a moral punishment for sins whose sting is reduced by participation not because participating makes the sins go away, but because punishment following sin is the world working the way it's supposed to in a world where many things, particularly magical things, do not seem to work the way the world is supposed to.<br /> <br /> <i>For people that are not satisfied with &quot;You're just a vampire, nothing else to it&quot; as an explanation for their condition, the Sanctum provides a support structure, a broad directive, and a way to make sense of a chaotic universe</i>. If you have a problem with faith and/or people doing nasty stuff in the name of it, the Sanctum is not going to be for you. If you are interested in playing a character who has to deal with the principle tension of What A Covenant Is in relation to Humanity, the Sanctum is there precisely because of the thing you are describing as hypocrisy \u2014 this is a group that is specifically interested in maintaining their self-control and understanding of the humans around them while firmly institutionally dividing themselves from humanity, and that means strong odds on many of them having developed banes to slow their descent (and, like with the Mekhet clan bane, this means having more secrets to safeguard).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T01:24:12-08:00","id":1556703,"title":"","content":"How much &quot;explicit&quot; do you think the Blood of the unwilling bane details are required to be?<br /> The vampire must clearly say &quot;now i ll take your blood&quot; or a consensual &quot;i m gonna give you a strong kiss&quot; is enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T05:58:27-08:00","id":1556709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556703#post1556703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much &quot;explicit&quot; do you think the Blood of the unwilling bane details are required to be?<br /> The vampire must clearly say &quot;now i ll take your blood&quot; or a consensual &quot;i m gonna give you a strong kiss&quot; is enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the bane applying to taking sustenance from vessels who are &quot;unwilling or unknowing&quot; specifically rules out any sort of subterfuge over the fact that you are drinking their blood, but the details of why are about as necessary for the other party to know as the partner in a bargain with a changeling \u2014 the point is to soft-eliminate particular modes of feeding like the Assault or drinking from people who are asleep and push toward using ghouls and blood dolls as your primary source of Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T06:55:47-08:00","id":1556713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556709#post1556709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bane applying to taking sustenance from vessels who are &quot;unwilling or unknowing&quot; specifically rules out any sort of subterfuge over the fact that you are drinking their blood, but the details of why are about as necessary for the other party to know as the partner in a bargain with a changeling \u2014 the point is to soft-eliminate particular modes of feeding like the Assault or drinking from people who are asleep and push toward using ghouls and blood dolls as your primary source of Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>The primary concern of the vampire of the example is, &quot;must i reveal my nature as a vampire (breaching the masquerade) each time i feed without using ghouls or blood dolls?&quot;<br /> Could a consensual, albeit kind of unusual, &quot;intimacy&quot; work as a willing and knowing subjet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T07:58:37-08:00","id":1556720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556713#post1556713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary concern of the vampire of the example is, &quot;must i reveal my nature as a vampire (breaching the masquerade) each time i feed without using ghouls or blood dolls?&quot;<br /> Could a consensual, albeit kind of unusual, &quot;intimacy&quot; work as a willing and knowing subjet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as changelings don't need to disclose the details of why their mien looks the way it does and demons don't need to explain the mechanism of a pact to get the right to take someone's soul, the bane doesn't imply full disclosure is necessary \u2014 the point is for the vessel to knowingly allow you to take their blood.<br /> <br /> We know from the section on the risks of creating revenants (and other aspects of the fiction throughout the line) that not all vampires feed directly on their vessels, but also the Kiss doesn't necessarily do anything to obviate the basic permission. The operative distinction I would make is that, regardless of how the offer was secured, the character willingly and knowingly gave their blood \u2014 doesn't ultimately matter if that offer was secured through threats or deception, as long as it wasn't being directly taken by force or supernatural compulsion (i.e. the character allowed some agreeable amount of their blood to leave their body) it offers sustenance normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T10:26:04-08:00","id":1556725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556720#post1556720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as changelings don't need to disclose the details of why their mien looks the way it does and demons don't need to explain the mechanism of a pact to get the right to take someone's soul, the bane doesn't imply full disclosure is necessary \u2014 the point is for the vessel to knowingly allow you to take their blood.<br /> <br /> We know from the section on the risks of creating revenants (and other aspects of the fiction throughout the line) that not all vampires feed directly on their vessels, but also the Kiss doesn't necessarily do anything to obviate the basic permission. The operative distinction I would make is that, regardless of how the offer was secured, the character willingly and knowingly gave their blood \u2014 doesn't ultimately matter if that offer was secured through threats or deception, as long as it wasn't being directly taken by force or supernatural compulsion (i.e. the character allowed some agreeable amount of their blood to leave their body) it offers sustenance normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>My doubt is mostly about the definition of unknow vessel.<br /> &quot;I ll take a little of your blood&quot; with no other explaination is clearly enough but what about &quot;this guy i m attracted to had just bitten my neck during foreplay, he probably has a bite kink or something like that. It s strange and i feel a little drowsy, but it s pleasurable so i want he to continue&quot; situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T10:39:59-08:00","id":1556726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556725#post1556725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I ll take a little of your blood&quot; with no other explaination is clearly enough but what about &quot;this guy i m attracted to had just bitten my neck during foreplay, he probably has a bite kink or something like that. It s strange and i feel a little drowsy, but it s pleasurable so i want he to continue&quot; situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrative framing of the latter is very clearly not the bane steering the vampire's behavior except in the sense that the vessel is likely to be put near death if not outright exsanguinated if the vampire is relying on implicit permission from the Kiss. An unhampered vessel is <i>giving</i> the vampire their blood, not tacitly validating their taking it with &quot;you felt good so it's okay.&quot;<br /> <br /> The bounds of the First Tradition are fuzzy and the Merit representing a reliable source of Vitae models people who are basically blood dolls. Requiem already paints the Kindred as social enough to seek confidants and most of the people you'd establish a Vinculum with are people you can get blood from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T19:57:43-08:00","id":1556741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556725#post1556725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My doubt is mostly about the definition of unknow vessel.<br /> &quot;I ll take a little of your blood&quot; with no other explaination is clearly enough but what about &quot;this guy i m attracted to had just bitten my neck during foreplay, he probably has a bite kink or something like that. It s strange and i feel a little drowsy, but it s pleasurable so i want he to continue&quot; situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it perhaps more clearly:<br /> <br /> The vessel must unambiguously <i>understand</i> and <i>accept</i> that you are taking some substantial amount of <i>blood</i> from them, without the use of physical or supernatural coercion, <i>before</i> you may begin taking blood from them. If you tell them you would like to drink their blood and it is going to have a soporific, pleasurable effect, and they know they have a choice in the matter, and they permit it because they want to feel that, that's valid. If you bite them and begin drinking blood when they didn't know you were going to be drinking blood, it doesn't matter if the Kiss renders the experience hazy and unclear or pleasurable and acceptable, you have not obtained informed consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T20:14:27-08:00","id":1556742,"title":"","content":"I don't even think this is unclear in any way, and it's scary to still see people that try to blur the notion of informed consent that much, as this is <i>literally</i> a thing that happens a lot in very bad situations.<br /> <br /> The goal of the bane is to bar deception or coercion in the strict act of taking blood. The person must know you'll take blood. What's at all unclear about that?<br /> <br /> And blood kinks are also a thing, as are people who drink blood for other reasons, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T22:15:30-08:00","id":1556744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556742#post1556742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even think this is unclear in any way, and it's scary to still see people that try to blur the notion of informed consent that much, as this is <i>literally</i> a thing that happens a lot in very bad situations.<br /> <br /> The goal of the bane is to bar deception or coercion in the strict act of taking blood. The person must know you'll take blood. What's at all unclear about that?<br /> <br /> And blood kinks are also a thing, as are people who drink blood for other reasons, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for clarification, i am aware that each form of feeding without prior declaration is by definition without consent.<br /> Even the vampire in the example probably know this, my doubt is about the precise wording of the bane (the text don t use informed consent as a dedinition) , and how much a vampire can test the limit of this curse.<br /> The vampire in the example is very careful, and will tend to value secrecy more than consent.<br /> His concern is about &quot;how much informed this consent has to be?&quot; while examining the bane (he is an ordo dracul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 12-17-2025, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-16T22:58:07-08:00","id":1556746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556744#post1556744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the vampire in the example probably know this, my doubt is about the precise wording of the bane (the text don t use informed consent as a dedinition) , and how much a vampire can test the limit of this curse.<br /> The vampire in the example is very careful, and will tend to value secrecy more than consent.<br /> His concern is about &quot;how much informed this consent has to be?&quot; while examining the bane (he is an ordo dracul)</div> </div> </div> </div>The precise wording of the bane is not how the character will be encountering the bane, which is instead that (barring high Humanity or vessels with high Stamina) attempting to nonfatally derive sustenance from blood that has been taken from characters without their knowledge and against their will requires taking enough from the vessel that the damage alone will have a measurable impact on their effectiveness in non-routine tasks of the sort that require a dice roll.<br /> <br /> You can coerce the vessel into agreement by offering alternatives they would definitely not prefer \u2014 including &quot;if you do not give me some of your blood I will kill you,&quot; in a pinch, or &quot;if you don't let me suck your blood I'm not giving you the substance you're addicted to \u2014 and nothing stops you from employing Dominate or good old-fashioned gaslighting after the fact, but any situation where the character is not consciously giving up some amount of their blood to you, regardless of what they contextually believe about that offer/relinquishment, is one where you are not getting sustenance out of at least some of that blood. That means no sneaking sips from the bottom bunk, no hypnotizing strangers into presenting their necks, no grab-and-gulps in back alleys, no opportunistic licks at open wounds, and so on.<br /> <br /> Experiments of interest may include seeing how such a vampire processes different types of stored or non-sapient blood \u2014 can animals dedicate their Vitae in the way humans and vampires can? does a human's permission apply retroactively to blood separated from their body before they made the offer? does mixing blood from willing and unwilling vessels affect the conversion rate? \u2014 but the basic intention of the bane is pretty clearly the same as why the action that triggers its effects is a Detachment trigger one dot below &quot;Lying in defense of the Masquerade&quot; and one dot above &quot;Depriving another of consent with a Discipline&quot; (and at the same level as &quot;Urging another's behavior with a Discipline&quot;). The semantics of how much the vessel knows about why you're asking for their blood are irrelevant \u2014 the complications of the fact that you cannot bypass the vessel's will without wasting Vitae are the important part in a game where difficult power dynamics and the psychological strain of secrecy are baked into the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T00:17:49-08:00","id":1556749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556744#post1556744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for clarification, i am aware that each form of feeding without prior declaration is by definition without consent.<br /> Even the vampire in the example probably know this, my doubt is about the precise wording of the bane (the text don t use informed consent as a dedinition) , and how much a vampire can test the limit of this curse.<br /> The vampire in the example is very careful, and will tend to value secrecy more than consent.<br /> His concern is about &quot;how much informed this consent has to be?&quot; while examining the bane (he is an ordo dracul)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your character takes no sustenance from the blood of the unwilling or unknowing.<br /> \u25cf <b>Does the vessel <i>know beforehand</i> that you are taking blood from them?</b> Being able to tell only mid-bite that that's what's happening is a useless definition of &quot;knowing&quot; here. Nobody would bother specifying that you can bite them but only if they can see that they are bleeding.<br /> \u25cf <b>Is the vessel <i>willing to give you</i> that blood?</b> It doesn't matter if it uses the word &quot;consent&quot; or not. This is what consent is, definitionally.<br /> That's it.<br /> <br /> Does the vessel need to know you are a vampire? No. Do you need to brief them on every little thing that's going to happen? No. If they know you're taking their blood, and you convince them to be okay with that, you get sustenance.<br /> Can you bite who doesn't <i>already know, and accept voluntarily,</i> that you are going to drink their blood? No. You get no Vitae from doing this.<br /> <br /> This bane makes it very hard to maintain <i>complete</i> secrecy as a vampire. Most vampires are not expected to maintain complete secrecy in gameplay, but if you want your character to maintain complete secrecy, probably do not give them this bane.<br /> <br /> Is it possible for a vampire with this bane to obtain blood without revealing themselves as a vampire? It's a hassle, but yes. Just don't bite them. Get a syringe. Convince them you are a medical professional and you need to draw blood. They have to know you are taking their blood. You're not required to be honest about <i>why</i>. Fill some vials and chug it from the vials. Sustenance.<br /> You can also convince people that this is some weird sex thing you're into and find somebody who is also into it. You don't have to be undead to drink someone's blood.<br /> <br /> Much more commonly, a vampire with this bane is going to have a small number of mortals who know they are a vampire (but may not really know much of anything about vampires besides &quot;they bite people and drink their blood&quot;) and who for whatever reason (bribes, blackmail, supernatural favors, the ecstasy of the Kiss, the Vinculum, ghouling, genuine concern for your wellbeing) are willing to let you drink from them. Make sure they don't tell anyone. Make sure nobody spies on them. As long as these things hold, you're good.<br /> <br /> Vampire games are about things going wrong and what you'll do to deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T00:27:25-08:00","id":1556750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556746#post1556746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The precise wording of the bane is not how the character will be encountering the bane, which is instead that (barring high Humanity or vessels with high Stamina) attempting to nonfatally derive sustenance from blood that has been taken from characters without their knowledge and against their will requires taking enough from the vessel that the damage alone will have a measurable impact on their effectiveness in non-routine tasks of the sort that require a dice roll.<br /> <br /> You can coerce the vessel into agreement by offering alternatives they would definitely not prefer \u2014 including &quot;if you do not give me some of your blood I will kill you,&quot; in a pinch, or &quot;if you don't let me suck your blood I'm not giving you the substance you're addicted to \u2014 and nothing stops you from employing Dominate or good old-fashioned gaslighting after the fact, but any situation where the character is not consciously giving up some amount of their blood to you, regardless of what they contextually believe about that offer/relinquishment, is one where you are not getting sustenance out of at least some of that blood. That means no sneaking sips from the bottom bunk, no hypnotizing strangers into presenting their necks, no grab-and-gulps in back alleys, no opportunistic licks at open wounds, and so on.<br /> <br /> Experiments of interest may include seeing how such a vampire processes different types of stored or non-sapient blood \u2014 can animals dedicate their Vitae in the way humans and vampires can? does a human's permission apply retroactively to blood separated from their body before they made the offer? does mixing blood from willing and unwilling vessels affect the conversion rate? \u2014 but the basic intention of the bane is pretty clearly the same as why the action that triggers its effects is a Detachment trigger one dot below &quot;Lying in defense of the Masquerade&quot; and one dot above &quot;Depriving another of consent with a Discipline&quot; (and at the same level as &quot;Urging another's behavior with a Discipline&quot;). The semantics of how much the vessel knows about why you're asking for their blood are irrelevant \u2014 the complications of the fact that you cannot bypass the vessel's will without wasting Vitae are the important part in a game where difficult power dynamics and the psychological strain of secrecy are baked into the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you are saying.<br /> From the three answers i ve received i think that actually my doubt springs from the fact that English is not my native language, as every one of you from what i understand reads the rules of the Bane as &quot;it applies whenever the human has not given the informed consent of giving up some of his blood&quot;.<br /> My understanding of the word unknowing was then, simply put, wrong","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T20:25:35-08:00","id":1556773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556750#post1556750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the word unknowing was then, simply put, wrong</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it like that, but knowing your native language could help clear things up.<br /> <br /> This is not by any means &quot;Informed Consent&quot;, as this is a more specific concept, and one with ethical and legal repercussions that give it a reasonably clear definition. And at least in Portuguese I can guarantee it exists and has this same definition.<br /> <br /> An &quot;Informed Consent&quot; is Informed about the circumstances, causes and developments of the act. Being directly asked to state your full name isn't asking Informed Consent, for that the person asking should also state their reasons, how they plan to use this information and what they plan to do with it afterwards. There's a lot of details we may discuss about how thorough or detailed such information should be, but it must be given and must <b>not</b> induce wrong conclusions by falsehood or selective omission.<br /> <br /> So, Informed Consent would mean at least telling the victim you drink blood for sustenance (circumstance and cause), you'll drain such amount from them (developments, as they must know how this may let them debilitated), and after that the blood will be processed in your body and mixed with previous victim's, rendering it useless for most known uses of blood. You may also have to answer follow-up questions. <b>That</b> is Informed Consent.<br /> <br /> What we said is, not only in at least some languages but also in several relevant contexts, just consent. If we're talking &quot;consent on taking blood&quot;, absent the core information of &quot;taking blood&quot; it isn't consent to begin with.<br /> <br /> Yet the way you worded isn't strange, but this is more worrying than justifying. The scenario you described is extremely common all around the world IRL and is a common argument for predators to throw uncertainty on the level of &quot;consent&quot; in the attack. Most women know situations like that very well, frequently by having been there as victims. This isn't just clear, it's a familiar but worrisome argument from someone who isn't trying to find the limits of the rule, but to blatantly talk their way out of it.<br /> <br /> Of course, given the setting, a character trying this is perfectly well within the theme. But it's not a reasonable rules question for someone who isn't already prone to very problematic ways of thinking consent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T21:52:59-08:00","id":1556776,"title":"","content":"I'll take responsibility for part of the confusion, as I did use the phrase &quot;informed consent&quot; in my first post, and I can see now that I did so carelessly and without consideration. Thank you for the clearer definition, monteparnas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-17T23:54:11-08:00","id":1556780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556773#post1556773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say it like that, but knowing your native language could help clear things up.<br /> <br /> This is not by any means &quot;Informed Consent&quot;, as this is a more specific concept, and one with ethical and legal repercussions that give it a reasonably clear definition. And at least in Portuguese I can guarantee it exists and has this same definition.<br /> <br /> An &quot;Informed Consent&quot; is Informed about the circumstances, causes and developments of the act. Being directly asked to state your full name isn't asking Informed Consent, for that the person asking should also state their reasons, how they plan to use this information and what they plan to do with it afterwards. There's a lot of details we may discuss about how thorough or detailed such information should be, but it must be given and must <b>not</b> induce wrong conclusions by falsehood or selective omission.<br /> <br /> So, Informed Consent would mean at least telling the victim you drink blood for sustenance (circumstance and cause), you'll drain such amount from them (developments, as they must know how this may let them debilitated), and after that the blood will be processed in your body and mixed with previous victim's, rendering it useless for most known uses of blood. You may also have to answer follow-up questions. <b>That</b> is Informed Consent.<br /> <br /> What we said is, not only in at least some languages but also in several relevant contexts, just consent. If we're talking &quot;consent on taking blood&quot;, absent the core information of &quot;taking blood&quot; it isn't consent to begin with.<br /> <br /> Yet the way you worded isn't strange, but this is more worrying than justifying. The scenario you described is extremely common all around the world IRL and is a common argument for predators to throw uncertainty on the level of &quot;consent&quot; in the attack. Most women know situations like that very well, frequently by having been there as victims. This isn't just clear, it's a familiar but worrisome argument from someone who isn't trying to find the limits of the rule, but to blatantly talk their way out of it.<br /> <br /> Of course, given the setting, a character trying this is perfectly well within the theme. But it's not a reasonable rules question for someone who isn't already prone to very problematic ways of thinking consent.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, i think that every step of the unlife of a vampire would be an ethical nightmare (to me at least).<br /> Defining boundaries in real life is easier, a no is a no, not a maybe or something else.<br /> But vampires feeding... they are methapors of violation.<br /> The victim of my example expected sexual intimacy and instead a monster bited her and stole some of his life force, it s not hard to see that she was hurted and deceived.<br /> But even if the vampire had told her about the feeding, what about the kiss effect?<br /> The kiss is a terrible thing, as if it is executed properly he FORCE the victim to fell good, an added violation (that in real life doesn t exist).<br /> Oh, and should the vampire inform the person that the kiss could easily cause dependency? And that it could cause spontaneous embraces after death?<br /> I find it hard to consider every single feeding, even an informed one, still not a violation.<br /> Even blood dolls, are they really willing or you are simply victim of the kiss dependency effect?<br /> Ok, then you steal some blood bags from an hospital, but doing that you put the life of injuried people at risk (and as a thief you are still a violator).<br /> And drinking from a vampire could deprive you of your free will...<br /> It scares me the idea of living like that, i easily see why all vampire stories are considered horror themed.<br /> <br /> With that premises, about the bane wording.<br /> I firstly translated unknowing in Italian as &quot;ignaro&quot; which could mean not knowing a predator is here but also not knowing what s going on.<br /> And eveng the willing word is not straightforward.<br /> In the best case the human offers the blood AND wants it to happen during the act.<br /> This is my interpretation of willing, but how does a mystical curse decides?<br /> A wyrd perspective would only consider the first element for example.<br /> That s why i asked here.<br /> Also i know that Banes are not supposed to be balanced between them, but Blood of the unwilling is surely going to impact a story a lot more than &quot;oh, i m stucked in a web&quot;.<br /> What i wanted to know was if the authors wanted to penalize simply all feeding that is not a Kiss or even those that are not discussed before with the victim, mostly because in an historical setting (i m running one) telling someone &quot;i drink blood&quot; could easily translate in &quot; death to the witch! &quot; reaction.<br /> <br /> On a more personal note, if my question seemed as a justifying of an abusive behaviour i m sorry, i understand that it s a delicate argument and that wasn t my intention.<br /> I really not wanted to offend or hurt anyone, if that has happened i humbly excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:39:51-08:00","id":1556801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556776#post1556776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll take responsibility for part of the confusion, as I did use the phrase &quot;informed consent&quot; in my first post, and I can see now that I did so carelessly and without consideration. Thank you for the clearer definition, monteparnas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think as a coloquial use of the word it was ok, didn't seemed like a situation where this level of nuance should be necessary.<br /> <br /> And it ended up being a good opportunity to explore things that an ST can really explore on how much information is needed beyond blood being taken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556780#post1556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bTo be honest, i think that every step of the unlife of a vampire would be an ethical nightmare (to me at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure as hell would. In a sense this Bane may even be welcomed by some characters as in a certain sense it eases the ethical conundrum.<br /> <br /> And at the same time may create where there shouldn't be, because there's still plenty of ways to violate people within the Bane.<br /> <br /> But this is precisely the theme being explored. You have a character that's barred from committing one of the biggest violations, yet has to find ways to continue to violate people.<br /> <br /> The point is more that the <i>consent</i> here isn't semantically on the intimacy, nor about the quality of the experience, and crucially isn't about the Kiss <i>per se</i>, it's strictly about the &quot;taking blood&quot; clause. Which closes this particular way of violating her, but opens up all those others where you're now forced to violate emotions, relationships, or any other aspect of the victim's life.<br /> <br /> One curiosity that this reminds me: BDSM practitioners are, precisely because of all this context, one of the most ethically aware communities around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556780#post1556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that premises, about the bane wording.<br /> I firstly translated unknowing in Italian as &quot;ignaro&quot; which could mean not knowing a predator is here but also not knowing what s going on.<br /> And eveng the willing word is not straightforward.<br /> In the best case the human offers the blood AND wants it to happen during the act.<br /> This is my interpretation of willing, but how does a mystical curse decides?<br /> A wyrd perspective would only consider the first element for example.<br /> That s why i asked here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> While there may still be some nuance, in English (and, to a lesser extent, Portuguese) those words are more straightforward. Willingness will connect directly to the stated clause, and covers other clauses only if circumstance strongly dictates it.<br /> <br /> Circumstance <i>may</i> cause a similar interpretation to yours, but not only it is to a lesser degree, this has changed considerably in the last three decades precisely because it became a sensitive social and legal matter. By the time the books were written, it would already be too much of a stretch here to interpret the consent being about the pleasurable experience and not the blood itself.<br /> <br /> Also, for whatever it's worth, the wyrd interpretation is usually the most likely one even if not in its most strict sense, especially since gaming the Bane becomes a matter of survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556780#post1556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also i know that Banes are not supposed to be balanced between them, but Blood of the unwilling is surely going to impact a story a lot more than &quot;oh, i m stucked in a web&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>IME, it isn't so disruptive because you have a lot of agency on when it's triggered. A character with such a Bane will adapt their strategies and lifestyle accordingly, so while it <b>will</b> have an intense impact in how much it informs characterization, it ends up being fairly situational as an actual disadvantage because most of the time the character will have it figured out. It's more of a play style thing than as big a deal as it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556780#post1556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i wanted to know was if the authors wanted to penalize simply all feeding that is not a Kiss or even those that are not discussed before with the victim, mostly because in an historical setting (i m running one) telling someone &quot;i drink blood&quot; could easily translate in &quot; death to the witch! &quot; reaction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the opposite, they wanted to penalize <b><u>the Kiss</u></b> above all, or those who rely on it's effects to turn bypass witness problems.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, the Bane doesn't stop you from feeding to the death of the person, or simply killing them afterwards.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1556780#post1556780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more personal note, if my question seemed as a justifying of an abusive behaviour i m sorry, i understand that it s a delicate argument and that wasn t my intention.<br /> I really not wanted to offend or hurt anyone, if that has happened i humbly excuse.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>We're all learning to deal with this yet, it's a complicated thing when you literally live in a society built around doing this, that's just recently trying to deconstruct, which is most modern societies if not all of them.<br /> <br /> And it's undeniably worse in this particular respect in Mediterranean (or derived) societies, like ours. Iberians, Italians and LatAm, we have a reputation for a reason.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T08:55:42-07:00","id":1559374,"title":"","content":"Were there rules / mechanics or story containing information about bloodlines and banes? Homerule?<br /> <br /> Kindreds can create bloodlines, and those bloodlines can become a clan (in theory). Some clans even states they were a bloodline once. I can't find anything about changing bloodline or evolving it.<br /> <br /> Banes. Kindreds could get those to mitigate some trauma. Yet there is no clues if it is possible to change or remove/heal such spiritual trauma. They have time, mysteries, diablerie (elders eat mortal souls), powers to physically transform or travel astral... yet, nothing to heal banes or humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T10:28:35-07:00","id":1559376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559374#post1559374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were there rules / mechanics or story containing information about bloodlines and banes? Homerule?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics for bloodlines in general are as printed in the corebook on page 98. Night Horrors: Spilled Blood contains a number of bloodlines as examples, and there are <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/tag/bloodlines/\" target=\"_blank\">some old blog posts</a> with earlier examples cut from the corebook for space.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindreds can create bloodlines, and those bloodlines can become a clan (in theory). Some clans even states they were a bloodline once. I can't find anything about changing bloodline or evolving it. </div> </div> </div>This is for much the same reason as there are no mechanics in Werewolf for a lodge becoming a tribe \u2014 it's a plot device that happens rarely enough and on a large enough timescale that the particulars (beyond reaching a fuzzy threshold of scope of membership) are going to vary by individual group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Banes. Kindreds could get those to mitigate some trauma. Yet there is no clues if it is possible to change or remove/heal such spiritual trauma. They have time, mysteries, diablerie (elders eat mortal souls), powers to physically transform or travel astral... yet, nothing to heal banes or humanity. </div> </div> </div>You restore Humanity by spending Experiences to buy Humanity dots. Banes are permanent changes to the character, whether gaining your Clan Bane when you first hit Humanity 6, elders getting an Elder Clan Bane when they first hit Humanity 3, or developing more unique Banes from Detachment.<br /> <br /> The heretical Coil of Ziva from Secrets of the Covenants concerns itself with mitigating the effects of Banes not covered by the Coil of the Ascendant, but it's by definition not going to be your Mystery Coil and therefore even if you're allowed to learn it you'd need to climb the ranks in the Ordo to advance it to the cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T23:58:07-07:00","id":1559386,"title":"","content":"Speaking of mechanics, I'm skeptical about how easy it is for a player to lose all their Humanity and succumb completely to the Beast.<br /> <br /> At least in the case of first edition, it makes a point of explaining that the lower your Humanity is, the more egregious the act needs to be to cause you to suffer a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Which suggests to me that the player isn't at risk of losing those final Humanity dots, unless they are deliberately trying to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T01:04:39-07:00","id":1559387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559386#post1559386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of mechanics, I'm skeptical about how easy it is for a player to lose all their Humanity and succumb completely to the Beast.<br /> <br /> At least in the case of first edition, it makes a point of explaining that the lower your Humanity is, the more egregious the act needs to be to cause you to suffer a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Which suggests to me that the player isn't at risk of losing those final Humanity dots, unless they are deliberately trying to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>After more than 15 years playing 2ed. I really don't feel it so easy to lose all humanity. First of all because of the 3 banes that mitigates the most recurring breaking points based on players play style/interpretation of their character. Secondly because to go below humanity you need to actions that are rarely needed during a game if not done on purpose because of character interpretation.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you abuse those actions, the risk is there and I like it to be there, as the very theme of the game is the struggle to not get overwhelmed by the Beast. But I would not call it easy in a sense where it means that it can happen by &quot;accident&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-13-2026, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T05:20:27-07:00","id":1559389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559386#post1559386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which suggests to me that the player isn't at risk of losing those final Humanity dots, unless they are deliberately trying to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>The consequences of dramatic failure on rolls to resist frenzy (or regular failure on attempts to ride the wave), combined with the stacking effects of the Tempted Condition and the lower odds of success on Detachment rolls for lower-level Humanity breaking points, serve as a nominal point of pressure, but yes, the primary reason to maintain your Humanity is for Bane mitigation and managing the Social penalty rather than the outside possibility of becoming a draugr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T05:23:04-07:00","id":1559390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559386#post1559386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of mechanics, I'm skeptical about how easy it is for a player to lose all their Humanity and succumb completely to the Beast.<br /> <br /> At least in the case of first edition, it makes a point of explaining that the lower your Humanity is, the more egregious the act needs to be to cause you to suffer a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Which suggests to me that the player isn't at risk of losing those final Humanity dots, unless they are deliberately trying to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it s designed to not doom the players to an easy game over.<br /> But consider that a humanity 1 sin, mass murder, could totally happen while in frenzy, expecially for strong and low humanity vampires caught by surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T12:08:29-07:00","id":1559391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559387#post1559387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After more than 15 years playing 2ed. I really don't feel it so easy to lose all humanity. First of all because of the 3 banes that mitigates the most recurring breaking points based on players play style/interpretation of their character. Secondly because to go below humanity you need to actions that are rarely needed during a game if not done on purpose because of character interpretation.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you abuse those actions, the risk is there and I like it to be there, as the very theme of the game is the struggle to not get overwhelmed by the Beast. But I would not call it easy in a sense where it means that it can happen by &quot;accident&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A level 1 breaking point is the combined act of rape, murder and torture<br /> <br /> Which is kind of strange, when you consider that vampires don't have a functional sex drive.<br /> <br /> Seduction is just another tool in their arsenal for manipulating people.<br /> <br /> I would also say the Beast isn't in the habit of letting fresh blood go to waste, by inflicting unnecessary wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T12:11:31-07:00","id":1559392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559390#post1559390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it s designed to not doom the players to an easy game over.<br /> But consider that a humanity 1 sin, mass murder, could totally happen while in frenzy, expecially for strong and low humanity vampires caught by surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also want to point out that Cruac reduces your maximum Humanity cap by 1 dot per level of mastery. Meaning that if you have 5 dots in Cruac, your Humanity is capped at 5.<br /> <br /> Seems like it would be pretty hindering for one of the main playable covenant's signature technique to put its members under threat of becoming Draugr, unless it was more difficult than presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T13:26:27-07:00","id":1559393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559391#post1559391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A level 1 breaking point is the combined act of rape, murder and torture</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not put extra qualifiers where none exist; you can commit a Humanity 1 breaking point by killing multiple people in one sitting. Less overtly extreme examples include diablerie and acting to harm your regnant with a third-stage Vinculum or killing a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also say the Beast isn't in the habit of letting fresh blood go to waste, by inflicting unnecessary wounds. </div> </div> </div>The Beast avoids letting fresh blood go to waste by consuming it. It does not especially care about the long term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T13:37:22-07:00","id":1559394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559393#post1559393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not put extra qualifiers where none exist;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you mean? I went back and checked my book before posting that. It literally said combining those three acts would trigger a break.<br /> <br /> But yeah, mass murder would be much easier to accomplish for a low humanity vampire. Especially when in the grips of a frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T13:49:33-07:00","id":1559396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559394#post1559394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you mean? I went back and checked my book before posting that. It literally said combining those three acts would trigger a break.</div> </div> </div> </div>A page number would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T14:33:32-07:00","id":1559398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559396#post1559396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A page number would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>182 - Humanity and Sins chart<br /> <br /> Humanity - Threshold Sin<br /> <br /> 1 - Utter perversion, heinous acts (e.g, combined rape, torture and murder; mass murder)<br /> <br /> Roll 2 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T17:16:43-07:00","id":1559402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559398#post1559398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">182 - Humanity and Sins chart<br /> <br /> Humanity - Threshold Sin<br /> <br /> 1 - Utter perversion, heinous acts (e.g, combined rape, torture and murder; mass murder)<br /> <br /> Roll 2 dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to be looking at the entire wrong edition for discussing breaking points and Detachment. 2e gives you a base dicepool of zero dice for things that threaten Humanity 1 vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T17:53:22-07:00","id":1559405,"title":"","content":"I did explicitly say I was using 1st edition back on page 18.<br /> <br /> Still, though, my point stands that the lower your humanity dropped, the more egregious the act needed to be to push you further down the path. It wasn't as simple as just having an accidental screw up now and then. Once you got around 3 dots, you needed to start acting like an edge lord to suffer additional breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T18:17:10-07:00","id":1559407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559405#post1559405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, though, my point stands that the lower your humanity dropped, the more egregious the act needed to be to push you further down the path. It wasn't as simple as just having an accidental screw up now and then. Once you got around 3 dots, you needed to start acting like an edge lord to suffer additional breaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes?<br /> <br /> This has historically been one of the things that made people complaining about ladder-of-sins-type Morality meters not letting them do as they please particularly weird, but 3 or 4 is the functional low end of typical character Morality/Integrity ratings in most of the gamelines, with lower ratings being indicative of aberrant circumstances allowing the character(s) in question to go off the rails, even if there's no greater impetus than power-tripping and doing horrible things because they think they can get away with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T07:51:12-07:00","id":1559413,"title":"","content":"I was asked to provide a page number.<br /> <br /> I not only provided a page number, but also quoted the chart directly.<br /> <br /> Still get downvotes...<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Again, I'd like to point out that Cruac caps your maximum Humanity rating in proportion to your level of mastery. It's good that a vampire can still remain semi-functional at that level, because a 5 dot master of Cruac has a maximum cap of 5 dots in humanity. All it takes is 2 breaks, before they're on the verge of becoming a gibbering madman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T08:17:04-07:00","id":1559414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559413#post1559413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Again, I'd like to point out that Cruac caps your maximum Humanity rating in proportion to your level of mastery. It's good that a vampire can still remain semi-functional at that level, because a 5 dot master of Cruac has a maximum cap of 5 dots in humanity. All it takes is 2 breaks, before they're on the verge of becoming a gibbering madman.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how the math works. A cap of 5 is a cap of the de facto upper range for most vampires who've been around the block.<br /> <br /> 1e's systems having the Humanity-based social penalty work via dice cap doesn't change the fact that Chronicles' dice math gives about a 75% chance of rolling any successes once you have four dice in your pool, and in 1e the cap is specific to three Skills being used against non-vampires in a mundane fashion.<br /> <br /> By the same math as above and 1e's systems for derangement acquisition, you have reasonable odds of not developing a derangement upon losing Humanity until around Humanity 2 or 3, severe derangements require the character to already have the corresponding mild derangement, and basically every mild derangement uses a Resolve + Composure roll to determine if it comes into play in relevant circumstances.<br /> <br /> Being two breaks away from being on the verge of becoming a gibbering madman is not a huge issue for characters who avoid torture and murder and other heinous activity. Cr\u00faac limits the character's ability to relate to humans such that they'll never do great at it (in 2e's system, they'll never not be rolling at some level of penalty). It is still not a meaningful threat to their actual functioning except as it relates to their banes, which is more emphasized in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T09:49:56-07:00","id":1559415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559414#post1559414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same math as above and 1e's systems for derangement acquisition, you have reasonable odds of not developing a derangement upon losing Humanity until around Humanity 2 or 3, severe derangements require the character to already have the corresponding mild derangement, and basically every mild derangement uses a Resolve + Composure roll to determine if it comes into play in relevant circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant madman in regards to the Beast's influence, not in terms of mental derangements.<br /> <br /> Humanity rating of 1-2 is described as <i>'barely sentient'</i>. You have just enough self awareness remaining to not be completely mindless, but you are by no means pleasant to be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T12:30:54-07:00","id":1559417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559415#post1559415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I meant madman in regards to the Beast's influence, not in terms of mental derangements.<br /> <br /> Humanity rating of 1-2 is described as <i>'barely sentient'</i>. You have just enough self awareness remaining to not be completely mindless, but you are by no means pleasant to be around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, 2e represents those levels' ability to relate to humans, in descending order, with a -5 penalty and a chance die. At minimum you have to routinely do things on par with planned murder to erode your Humanity to that level or else be going nearly a decade without human contact, which 2e uses as its first example Humanity 1 breaking point as the culmination of the example chart's set of isolation-based breaking points.<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure why the cap from Cr\u00faac is relevant to this, given that Cr\u00faac is not assumed to go above five dots and the level of Humanity you're here expressing concern about (after correctly observing that getting that low tends to involve egregious decisions and circumstances) is three levels below the maximum Humanity the Discipline allows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T15:04:11-07:00","id":1559419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559417#post1559417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity to that level or else be going nearly a decade without human contact, which 2e uses as its first example Humanity 1 breaking point as the culmination of the example chart's set of isolation-based breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow.<br /> <br /> Fuck us autistic introverts, I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T17:23:18-07:00","id":1559420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559419#post1559419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow.<br /> <br /> Fuck us autistic introverts, I guess? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though being a dead thing that needs externally-sourced human blood to survive, initiated into undeath by another dead thing that needs externally-sourced human blood to survive, and being given to frequent temptations to abandon your vestigial humanity in the name of fear, hunger, and/or dominance not helped by retreating from society is not a commentary on human psychology of the sort that can be termed prejudicial.<br /> <br /> In 1e it's a gameplay incentive against trying to retain your Humanity by simply not interacting with people so you can't sin against them. In 2e it's part of the larger framework of Humanity being specifically maintained by keeping in practice at acting like a human who can blend in with mortal society and avoiding reminders that you're no longer counted amongst the living.<br /> <br /> My social battery and placement on the spectrum don't enter into it; if I can go a decade without human contact (especially in a system where having a human contact or at least something that reminds me of my mortal days), I am unlikely to stay in practice with the niceties that make my tactics as a predator operate under the assumption that I need to avoid setting off alarm bells in the minds of human prey and thus am liable to let my skills in that field atrophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T18:03:51-07:00","id":1559422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559420#post1559420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though being a dead thing that needs externally-sourced human blood to survive, initiated into undeath by another dead thing that needs externally-sourced human blood to survive, and being given to frequent temptations to abandon your vestigial humanity in the name of fear, hunger, and/or dominance not helped by retreating from society is not a commentary on human psychology of the sort that can be termed prejudicial.<br /> <br /> In 1e it's a gameplay incentive against trying to retain your Humanity by simply not interacting with people so you can't sin against them. In 2e it's part of the larger framework of Humanity being specifically maintained by keeping in practice at acting like a human who can blend in with mortal society and avoiding reminders that you're no longer counted amongst the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you go your entire life struggling to recognize social cues, or manage your emotions, you learn that avoiding human interaction is the less stressful option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559420#post1559420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My social battery and placement on the spectrum don't enter into it; if I can go a decade without human contact (especially in a system where having a human contact or at least something that reminds me of my mortal days), I am unlikely to stay in practice with the niceties that make my tactics as a predator operate under the assumption that I need to avoid setting off alarm bells in the minds of human prey and thus am liable to let my skills in that field atrophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as how Presence (Majesty) and Dominate are no longer common disciplines in Requiem, I can see your point about needing to maintain your social skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-14T19:19:20-07:00","id":1559423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559422#post1559422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you go your entire life struggling to recognize social cues, or manage your emotions, you learn that avoiding human interaction is the less stressful option.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if your sire abandoned you after you were Embraced because they were one of the rare unfortunates who let their Humanity wither to the level where murder no longer bothers them, you may well follow in their footsteps and isolate yourself out of ever needing to act like anything but a blood-drinking feedback loop, but most vampires operate in situations where there's at least one other entity who is concerned with masking and self-regulating as a matter of survival.<br /> <br /> Going literally years without so much as an attempt at small talk with another person says something about a vampire, especially in 1e when the criteria for staving off isolation included interaction with other vampires. Much as Mummy makes it so that acting like an incarnate curse or a lich-king or an instrument of divine wrath instead of a human with a lived history is a lot easier at a level of Memory that doesn't care about murder and mass property damage, Requiem makes it so that your Humanity will adjust accordingly if your night-to-night existence indicates you don't need to act like anything other than a blood-drinking undead monster. You're welcome to find bits of that resonant with parts of the autistic condition and/or being an introvert, but it's very obviously not an allegory for those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T03:21:08-07:00","id":1559426,"title":"","content":"Probably a better analogy would be psychopaths.<br /> I m not a psychologist but if i understand it rightly a psychopath person can understand people motivation and feelings but the utter lack of empathy makes treating them as something different from tools almost impossible.<br /> Substitute food to tool and you got it...<br /> As a note a humanity 1 vampire in game could have empathy at 7 dots and intelligence at 8 and still don t feel nothing but hunger when talking to someone.<br /> An alien intelligence difficult to understand, deranged from our standard but perfectly funcional in regard of its motivation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T14:23:19-07:00","id":1559434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559426#post1559426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a better analogy would be psychopaths.<br /> I m not a psychologist but if i understand it rightly a psychopath person can understand people motivation and feelings but the utter lack of empathy makes treating them as something different from tools almost impossible.<br /> Substitute food to tool and you got it...<br /> As a note a humanity 1 vampire in game could have empathy at 7 dots and intelligence at 8 and still don t feel nothing but hunger when talking to someone.<br /> An alien intelligence difficult to understand, deranged from our standard but perfectly funcional in regard of its motivation</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the symptoms of aspergers is reduced empathy; viewing people based on their utility, rather than emotional connections.<br /> <br /> But to get the subject back on track...<br /> <br /> What's up with the Ordo Dracul? I've been told that in second edition they went from trying to overcome the weaknesses of vampirism, to instead focus on becoming the perfect monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T18:21:46-07:00","id":1559437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559434#post1559434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's up with the Ordo Dracul? I've been told that in second edition they went from trying to overcome the weaknesses of vampirism, to instead focus on becoming the perfect monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people may have taken the functional benefits of some of the Coils of the Dragon in 1e as an indication that they were the most ethical and/or humane covenant, a perspective not helped by the fact that the Coil of Blood immediately cutting out the logistics issue behind extracting Vitae dealing lethal damage and feeding restrictions being hard limits and the Coil of the Beast allowing the character to simply Stop a frenzy by spending Willpower if they failed to resist it normally, which game the impression that, in the absence of purely narrative safeguards, the covenant who takes Dracula as their role model in the pursuit of having the advantages of vampirism without the drawbacks would allow dabblers in their mysteries to learn a few useful tricks for pretending they aren't still vampires.<br /> <br /> In 2e, by contrast, the first tier of the Coil of the Wyrm (replacing the Coil of the Beast) allows you to spend Willpower to voluntarily enter frenzy toward a specific goal (which can be used to avoid an involuntary frenzy) and enhances the benefits of being in frenzy, the Coil of the Ascendant (replacing the Coil of Banes) roots its enhanced daytime activity in the blush of life, and instead of the Coil of Blood messing with Vitae efficiency, the Coil of the Voivode tweaks how Vitae addiction, blood bonds, blood sympathy, and the Embrace work for the Dragon. In addition, Coils are part of Mysteries that each Dragon can only specialize in one of and needs to increase their Covenant Status to learn higher-level Coils, and each Coil has procedures called Scales that allow the Dragon to share aspects of their (possibly altered) vampiric condition with others in ways that risk their Humanity to research but can be learned without the prerequisite Coil rating and can accomplish things like reversing a vampire's sleep-wake cycle, removing blood bonds, or imbuing Physical Intensity into a consumable solution that enhances a mortal's physical abilities by the same amount for a longer time.<br /> <br /> Retaining one's humanity is not the goal of the Ordo, and though there is some argument within the covenant about what the end target of transcending their limits is it's sufficiently clearly not just &quot;turn off all the downsides of vampirism and chill as a normal human&quot; that the Coil based around increasing your effective Humanity and lessening the effects of your Humanity-scaled banes is considered heretical. They're not trying to <i>cure</i> vampirism, they're trying to <i>refine</i> it, most notably by experimentation and exposure to supernatural phenomena that mortals tend to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T18:30:35-07:00","id":1559438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559437#post1559437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people may have taken the functional benefits of some of the Coils of the Dragon in 1e as an indication that they were the most ethical and/or humane covenant, a perspective not helped by the fact that the Coil of Blood immediately cutting out the logistics issue behind extracting Vitae dealing lethal damage and feeding restrictions being hard limits and the Coil of the Beast allowing the character to simply Stop a frenzy by spending Willpower if they failed to resist it normally, which game the impression that, in the absence of purely narrative safeguards, the covenant who takes Dracula as their role model in the pursuit of having the advantages of vampirism without the drawbacks would allow dabblers in their mysteries to learn a few useful tricks for pretending they aren't still vampires.<br /> <br /> In 2e, by contrast, the first tier of the Coil of the Wyrm (replacing the Coil of the Beast) allows you to spend Willpower to voluntarily enter frenzy toward a specific goal (which can be used to avoid an involuntary frenzy) and enhances the benefits of being in frenzy, the Coil of the Ascendant (replacing the Coil of Banes) roots its enhanced daytime activity in the blush of life, and instead of the Coil of Blood messing with Vitae efficiency, the Coil of the Voivode tweaks how Vitae addiction, blood bonds, blood sympathy, and the Embrace work for the Dragon. In addition, Coils are part of Mysteries that each Dragon can only specialize in one of and needs to increase their Covenant Status to learn higher-level Coils, and each Coil has procedures called Scales that allow the Dragon to share aspects of their (possibly altered) vampiric condition with others in ways that risk their Humanity to research but can be learned without the prerequisite Coil rating and can accomplish things like reversing a vampire's sleep-wake cycle, removing blood bonds, or imbuing Physical Intensity into a consumable solution that enhances a mortal's physical abilities by the same amount for a longer time.<br /> <br /> Retaining one's humanity is not the goal of the Ordo, and though there is some argument within the covenant about what the end target of transcending their limits is it's sufficiently clearly not just &quot;turn off all the downsides of vampirism and chill as a normal human&quot; that the Coil based around increasing your effective Humanity and lessening the effects of your Humanity-scaled banes is considered heretical. They're not trying to <i>cure</i> vampirism, they're trying to <i>refine</i> it, most notably by experimentation and exposure to supernatural phenomena that mortals tend to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly, the Coil of Blood reduced the cost of waking up down to 1 BP a week. A frugal vampire who avoided using disciplines could go for months without needing to feed!<br /> <br /> But overcoming the weaknesses of vampirism doesn't mean you become a normal human. Even in 1E, they weren't presented as that being their goal. They wanted to evolve to a higher state, keeping all the benefits of being a vampire, with few or none of the drawbacks.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> But from what you describe, it sounds like they turned the Tzimisce into their own faction, minus the flesh crafting aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T19:10:11-07:00","id":1559439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559438#post1559438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, the Coil of Blood reduced the cost of waking up down to 1 BP a week. A frugal vampire who avoided using disciplines could go for months without needing to feed!</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Vitae per [Resolve] nights, which at least doubled the value per Vitae spent on waking up. The fact that the 1e covenant sourcebook introduced a term in its lexicon and a related sidebar for the feedback loop produced by two vampires with the &quot;feeding on supernatural vessels gives you double the normal Vitae&quot; level of the Coil suggests maintaining Vitae scarcity without extraordinary methods or dedicated resources was not something they wanted to maintain in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But overcoming the weaknesses of vampirism doesn't mean you become a normal human. </div> </div> </div>No, but it sure makes it easier to pretend, which raises the question for a certain subset of readers of &quot;why don't they?&quot; in a game whose central mechanics included pretending to be a normal human at least well enough to discourage serious investigation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in 1E, they weren't presented as that being their goal. They wanted to evolve to a higher state, keeping all the benefits of being a vampire, with few or none of the drawbacks. </div> </div> </div>For which again see &quot;Some people may have taken the functional benefits of the Coils as an indication that they were the most ethical and/or humane covenant&quot; despite these being the folks who poke around haunted houses and have a dedicated faction whose practices include doing things to their bodies that mortals would not survive.<br /> <br /> The books aren't obligated to address egregious misreadings, but it certainly helps to be up-front when presenting a new edition whose focal goals include specifically demonstrating the gameline's specific angle of monstrosity and presenting its own take on vampirism that isn't self-consciously stepping out of the shadow of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But from what you describe, it sounds like they turned the Tzimisce into their own faction, minus the flesh crafting aspect. </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to pretend I have the Masquerade expertise to know what gave you this idea, but I recognize a reductive reading when I see one.<br /> <br /> The Ordo studies the vampiric condition and the supernatural more generally, especially where the two overlap. They meditate and perform geomancy on Wyrm's Nests, which is the generalized term they use for any sort of supernatural real estate. They study the particulars of how their Disciplines manifest. They impale themselves and experiment on others with procedures that would be called torture by many standards. They have an institutional mandate against offering subservience to gods and spirits and ghosts as part of their goal of self-refinement as one of the more naturally bastardly monsters in the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixing typo. 04-16-2026, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T20:40:36-07:00","id":1559443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559439#post1559439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to pretend I have the Masquerade expertise to know what gave you this idea, but I recognize a reductive reading when I see one.<br /> <br /> The Ordo studies the vampiric condition and the supernatural more generally, especially where the two overlap. They mediate and perform geomancy on Wyrm's Nests, which is the generalized term they use for any sort of supernatural real estate. They study the particulars of how their Disciplines manifest. They impale themselves and experiment on others with procedures that would be called torture by many standards. They have an institutional mandate against offering subservience to gods and spirits and ghosts as part of their goal of self-refinement as one of the more naturally bastardly monsters in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - The leaders of the clan are straight up given the title of 'Voivode,' which one of the coils is named after.<br /> <br /> 2 - The members of Old Clan Tzimisce rejected the practice of Vicissitude, in favor of pursuing a more spiritual form of metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> 3 - They generally viewed themselves as the absolute authority within their domains. Even using Koldunic Sorcery to enslave the spirits of the land and harness their power.<br /> <br /> <br /> But don't misunderstand me, I'm not disparaging the covenant. I happen to like both them and the Tzimisce!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T23:55:32-07:00","id":1559446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559443#post1559443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from what you describe, it sounds like they turned the Tzimisce into their own faction, minus the flesh crafting aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. Mixed with the Tremere social structure.<br /> <br /> Though, come to think of it, that may well explain why Dracula is the Ordo's founder. Like, it always seemed an odd choice, but it makes more sense if it's an iteration on the Dracula in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1 - The leaders of the clan are straight up given the title of 'Voivode,' which one of the coils is named after. </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing the bigger picture. The commonality is Dracula, the <i>Voivode</i> of Wallachia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - The members of Old Clan Tzimisce rejected the practice of Vicissitude, in favor of pursuing a more spiritual form of metamorphosis. </div> </div> </div>Do the Ordo reject physical change?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 - They generally viewed themselves as the absolute authority within their domains. Even using Koldunic Sorcery to enslave the spirits of the land and harness their power. </div> </div> </div>...That's kinda just a vampire thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T09:31:25-07:00","id":1559456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559446#post1559446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, come to think of it, that may well explain why Dracula is the Ordo's founder. Like, it always seemed an odd choice, but it makes more sense if it's an iteration on the Dracula in Masquerade.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the original story of Dracula wasn't harmed by sunlight. He was just severely weakened in it. There's even a scene where he's walking around in broad daylight, so if there's any vampire that could serve as the mascot for evolution, it would be him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559446#post1559446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're missing the bigger picture. The commonality is Dracula, the <i>Voivode</i> of Wallachia.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the Coil seems to be focused around the idea of strengthening the Dragon's authority over others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559446#post1559446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Ordo reject physical change?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> If there's a Coil that causes you to transform into what can only be described as a vampiric demon, I have yet to hear about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T11:13:31-07:00","id":1559457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559456#post1559456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Coil seems to be focused around the idea of strengthening the Dragon's authority over others.</div> </div> </div> </div>And &quot;voivode&quot; is a title of authority that the historical Vlad the Impaler held. How is this a contradiction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T11:50:54-07:00","id":1559459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559456#post1559456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the original story of Dracula wasn't harmed by sunlight. He was just severely weakened in it. There's even a scene where he's walking around in broad daylight, so if there's any vampire that could serve as the mascot for evolution, it would be him.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's because he's not a Requiem vampire, not because he's some symbol of evolution. Also, isn't his aim more implied to be taking over the UK rather than personal evolution?<br /> <br /> Look, it's quite possible that's the idea. It just always struck me as an odd choice. It feels more likely that it's a direct iteration on Dracula being a Tzimisce in the previous Vampire game.<br /> <br /> Though, come to think of it, it's also possible that both are riffing on another source. Like, I've never read <i>Necroscope, </i>the usual source given for the Tzimsce; maybe that's the common source for a Dracula interested in evolution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Coil seems to be focused around the idea of strengthening the Dragon's authority over others. </div> </div> </div>So? It's poetic. I mean, page 158 of the 2e core directly relates the name to Vlad Tepes having the title of Voivode.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there's a Coil that causes you to transform into what can only be described as a vampiric demon, I have yet to hear about it. </div> </div> </div>But that's the point. The Coils not doing that isn't necessarily indicative that the Ordo would mind if they did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T14:13:46-07:00","id":1559466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559457#post1559457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And &quot;voivode&quot; is a title of authority that the historical Vlad the Impaler held. How is this a contradiction?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said it was?<br /> <br /> I said the Ordo sound like the Tzimisce remade into a covenant, and then pointed out how the Voivodes were the title held by their clan leaders.<br /> <br /> I'm confused now, because it sounds like you and me had a bit of a communication error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T14:34:56-07:00","id":1559467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559466#post1559466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said it was?<br /> <br /> I said the Ordo sound like the Tzimisce remade into a covenant, and then pointed out how the Voivodes were the title held by their clan leaders.<br /> <br /> I'm confused now, because it sounds like you and me had a bit of a communication error.</div> </div> </div> </div>Step 1: You point out that Voivode is a title held by clan leaders in the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Step 2: It is pointed out that it is also a title held by the historical figure identified with the fictional Dracula, who is a point of commonality between the Ordo Dracul in Requiem and the Tzimisce in Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Step 3: You make a response to Step 2 that starts with the word &quot;But&quot; and is followed by something that doesn't have any contextual reason to be lead into with a &quot;but,&quot; which is that the name of the Mystery that is named for the leadership title held by Vlad Tepes enhances your social power over other vampires.<br /> <br /> Step 4: Both I and the poster who bothered to dignify Step 1 with a response are confused what the point of Step 3 is, given the extremely simple and minor explanation for that overlap.<br /> <br /> Step 5: Apparently two different groups of vampires in two different games that both claim Dracula as a potent legendary figure using the same title as the historic figure Bram Stoker's <i>Dracula</i> drew inspiration from is supposed to be significant.<br /> <br /> Step 6: You Are Here. Setting aside a simple overlap in nomenclature, we have the Ordo engaging in typical Requiem vampire behavior and the Tzimisce rejecting a type of power that the Defiant don't have any institutional objections to. (&quot;Dracula was a Gangrel&quot; is an in- and out-of-setting theory with legs to it throughout the gameline, and the Gangrel are the most physically-inclined clan of the core five.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T01:04:58-07:00","id":1559473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559459#post1559459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's because he's not a Requiem vampire, not because he's some symbol of evolution. Also, isn't his aim more implied to be taking over the UK rather than personal evolution?<br /> <br /> Look, it's quite possible that's the idea. It just always struck me as an odd choice. It feels more likely that it's a direct iteration on Dracula being a Tzimisce in the previous Vampire game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a key thing about the portrayal of Dracula in the novel is that the influence of his life as a statesman under duress gives him a mind set towards attempting a more sophisticated approach to being a vampire. His capacity to keep a living human around for an extended period of time in the interests of information gathering is contrasted against the feral appetite of his brides. And his whole scheme is predicated on being unusually strategic around overcoming the limitation of needing to remain in a specific location.<br /> <br /> I would find another fiction depicting Dracula as being introspective about the condition of being a vampire and trying to test out the parameters of that to have a certain consistency. To the extent that both are taking certain creative liberties with how much can be inferred from the character of a historical figure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T01:19:28-07:00","id":1561594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559473#post1559473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a key thing about the portrayal of Dracula in the novel is that the influence of his life as a statesman under duress gives him a mind set towards attempting a more sophisticated approach to being a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a &quot;simpler&quot; reason: the novel's Dracula is a sorcerer who studied in Scholomance. The novel is unclear about which of the many feats he display is due to vampiric nature or to his magical knowledge.<br /> <br /> Another theme common to both the Ordo, the Tzimisce and Vlad Tepes III is sheer audacity. It is a common way to interpret the way Dracula (the actual Voivode) defied both the Turkish and the other Voivodes and Walachian nobles. The Ordo defies nature (in the broader sense) itself, refusing to accept the limits of the Curse no matter what caused it. The Tzimisce defy the proper form of living beings.<br /> <br /> But the Ordo is not the Tzimisce. Sure the Path of Metamorphosis taught the Tzimisce to look for Transcendence, but the philosophy is based in constant change and method introspective. The Ordo looks everywhere, applies a rational, empirical approach, and seek to crystallize the findings, through Coils, Mysteries, Scales. They share and discuss results (to an extent), their take assumes Transcendence as a goal to be codified through collective work, a goal for the institution and its methods. Metamorphosis is a spiritual search for personal enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T04:42:33-07:00","id":1561598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1559439#post1559439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but it sure makes it easier to pretend, which raises the question for a certain subset of readers of &quot;why don't they?&quot; in a game whose central mechanics included pretending to be a normal human at least well enough to discourage serious investigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I just caught this after re-reading back through the comments again.<br /> <br /> While the core mechanics may have presented the idea that you want to try remaining human, not all of the covenants seemed to agree with that sentiment.<br /> <br /> Cruac, the signature discipline of the <b>Circle of the Crone</b> actively caps your Humanity rating based on your level of mastery. With a maximum cap of 5 Humanity at the 5th dot of mastery.<br /> <br /> While the <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> openly views pretending to be human as a sin. In their eyes, God created vampires to be monsters, and so they should conduct themselves accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only the <b>Invictus</b> and <b>Carthian Movement</b> seem to favor pretending to be human. But that's because they were just Camarilla / Anarchs wearing a different hat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-11-2026, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T06:53:29-07:00","id":1561601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561598#post1561598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the core mechanics may have presented the idea that you want to try remaining human, not all of the covenants seemed to agree with that sentiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> Humanity in VtR doesn't measure <i>proximity</i> to mortals. It measures your ability to <i>feel the character</i> of one.<br /> <br /> It's not about nature, but about comprehension. The analogy to a psychopath fits, though it may need refinement:<br /> <br /> Empathy is the human capacity to recognize in others their own mental process. Feeling fear or anger is an emotion. Recognizing that other people feel fear or anger and mentally picture what it's like is empathy.<br /> <br /> Autistics have a hard time processing Empathy, frequently get it wrong, but the <i>notion</i> is there. Psychopaths don't, or has it reduced. Not get it wrong, don't get the very <i>idea</i> except the most abstract way. They observe people behave, and so can learn their reactions, but have no idea of how their perspective could be, even imagined.<br /> <br /> So Humanity here is your Empathy. A vampire may know human behavior abstractly with skill dots, but Humanity measures their ability to mentally picture the mindset of a mortal.<br /> <br /> Your feelings of being close to humans are just a your thoughts problem. You can have very low Humanity and still think yourself not really that different, that's philosophy. Or feel you like them as family, that's sentiment. But can you imagine how it feels to be like them? That's Humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T06:57:26-07:00","id":1561602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561598#post1561598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the core mechanics may have presented the idea that you want to try remaining human, not all of the covenants seemed to agree with that sentiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they're allowed. It being a matter of degrees doesn't change the fact that any covenant that isn't Belial's Brood still incentivizes its members to keep their Humanity at least high enough to buffer the risk of becoming a draugr from one bad night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cruac, the signature discipline of the <b>Circle of the Crone</b> actively caps your Humanity rating based on your level of mastery. With a maximum cap of 5 Humanity at the 5th dot of mastery. </div> </div> </div>And Humanity 5 is where most neonates comfortably sit in 2e's metrics, which both editions demarcate approximately as &quot;this character hasn't killed people very often or is at least taking the spiritual countermeasures to keep it from affecting them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the <b>Lancea Sanctum</b> openly views pretending to be human as a sin. In their eyes, God created vampires to be monsters, and so they should conduct themselves accordingly. </div> </div> </div>And because the Lancea is explicitly not the Circle and prizes patience and being better than wild beasts, that conduct includes maintaining their ability to pass for human for the sake of camouflage and control even without 2e explicitly capping use of Theban Sorcery rituals with Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only the <b>Invictus</b> and <b>Carthian Movement</b> seem to favor pretending to be human. But that's because they were just Camarilla / Anarchs wearing a different hat. </div> </div> </div>No, it's because they're the two covenants who have the most direct truck with human society as institutions. An Invictus monastery or a Carthian wilderness retreat are unusual for the same reason the typical setting of a Vampire game is a large population center \u2014 ascetic practices, occult rituals, and communion with the wild stand out as weird if (or, sometimes, are mutually incompatible with) living among a group of people who you don't want to find out you're a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T09:11:26-07:00","id":1561606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561598#post1561598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only the <b>Invictus</b> and <b>Carthian Movement</b> ... But that's because they were just Camarilla / Anarchs wearing a different hat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Though V5 tried hard to do that.<br /> <br /> Previous to V5, the Camarilla was a common understanding among Princes: enforce the 6 Traditions, try to follow &quot;Best Practices&quot;, and protect the status quo so that Elders can stay in power.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, each Prince does whatever. They're similar only in the sense that the game explored few cities and not always with peak creativity.<br /> <br /> The Invictus defend the method. The specific style of hierarchy. The need for a specific kind of Order. And they are willing to throw the Elder under the bus in favor of a more promising young Vampire.<br /> <br /> Anarchs are just Vampires in a city that don't like how things are going and voice it aloud at least in their areas. This is it. An Anarch can have any idea at all of what's better for the city, just not the current state of affairs. It was not a sect, the Anarch Free States were an anomaly no one knew what to do with, especially not themselves.<br /> <br /> Carthians are political explorers. They think the Invictus way don't work well enough and there's something better. They don't agree what it is, but are willing to find out. They're not necessarily in it against Elders.<br /> <br /> Many Carthian Domains and individuals would be firmly Camarilla in Masquerade. Many firm Invictus cells would definitely be Anarchs. The only thing none would be is Sabbat, but they'd be quite more receptive to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T11:50:52-07:00","id":1561611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561606#post1561606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs are just Vampires in a city that don't like how things are going and voice it aloud at least in their areas. This is it. An Anarch can have any idea at all of what's better for the city, just not the current state of affairs. It was not a sect, the Anarch Free States were an anomaly no one knew what to do with, especially not themselves.<br /> <br /> Carthians are political explorers. They think the Invictus way don't work well enough and there's something better. They don't agree what it is, but are willing to find out. They're not necessarily in it against Elders.<br /> <br /> Many Carthian Domains and individuals would be firmly Camarilla in Masquerade. Many firm Invictus cells would definitely be Anarchs. The only thing none would be is Sabbat, but they'd be quite more receptive to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have clarified. I see the Carthians as a version of Anarchs who managed to get their shit together, and do something more productive than metaphorically pissing in the wind.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm confusing Anarch behavior with Brujah behavior? After all, the clan is practically synonymous with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T21:08:13-07:00","id":1561617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561611#post1561611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I should have clarified. I see the Carthians as a version of Anarchs who managed to get their shit together, and do something more productive than metaphorically pissing in the wind.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm confusing Anarch behavior with Brujah behavior? After all, the clan is practically synonymous with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are very rapidly veering off-topic on a thread that has a broad but very clearly stated topic.<br /> <br /> Requiem's core five covenants at least pay lip service to the three Traditions for reasons of practicality and social cohesion. They are a population of predators whose prey outnumber them dramatically and have physical, social, and metaphysical advantages over them unless actively suborned, sabotaged, and/or exploited. The darker urges undergirding their unlives make collaboration and planning fraught endeavors, to say nothing of the Weird Shit that comes with being a magical entity, and keeping in practice with passing for human is a literal exercise in self-control.<br /> <br /> A certain amount of resignation to (or perverse delight in) violation of social mores does not change the fact that most vampires are human enough that serial murder is a bridge too far (or at least a serious and lasting commitment) and look ill instead of dead without spending Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T13:46:08-07:00","id":1561640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561611#post1561611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I should have clarified. I see the Carthians as a version of Anarchs who managed to get their shit together, and do something more productive than metaphorically pissing in the wind.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm confusing Anarch behavior with Brujah behavior? After all, the clan is practically synonymous with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still missing the point.<br /> <br /> Anarchs as a sect is a Carthian-imitating retcon. The original concept is a loose term for those in a city that don't like how government is governing.<br /> <br /> There's no shit to get together: there's no link between groups. There's no groups. What the people getting labeled Anarchs want differs as they're not the ones globally organizing this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T13:52:24-07:00","id":1561641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561640#post1561640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still missing the point.<br /> <br /> Anarchs as a sect is a Carthian-imitating retcon. The original concept is a loose term for those in a city that don't like how government is governing.<br /> <br /> There's no shit to get together: there's no link between groups. There's no groups. What the people getting labeled Anarchs want differs as they're not the ones globally organizing this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That kind of sounds like it overlaps with Autarkis, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-12T20:57:46-07:00","id":1561645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561641#post1561641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That kind of sounds like it overlaps with Autarkis, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only as much as political disagreement overlap with apolitical hermits.<br /> <br /> You're an Anarch when you're a part of Kindred society and think the Prince is doing a shitty job at running it. You have opinions and want to see political change.<br /> <br /> It's important to observe that the game doesn't originally put Anarchs as opposed to the Cam, only to the actual current Prince. Most Anarchs are expected to be Camarilla in practice, very few really proposing a strong departure. After all, the one Anarch movement that did so is the Sabbat, whose common ground isn't really the religion, but the position against the Traditions and power of Elders.<br /> <br /> Autarkis don't give a fuck, to society, politics or princes. They go their merry way to the edge of town and shut themselves, everyone else be damned.<br /> <br /> Carthians seek political experimentation. While this means uncommon structures, it also does include at least some Traditions, so many of them would be Camarilla full stop. And it also involves a complete political theory rather than just local disagreement, which is not at all what Anarchs are about.<br /> <br /> The Anarch Free States are a demonstration of the distinction: they're what happens when the local Anarchs go overboard <u><b><i>because</i></b></u> they're not the Carthians or Autarkis.<br /> <br /> Were they Carthians, they'd have a plan to build a new system with solid premises. Were they a bunch of Autarkis, it would be an unclaimed area where scattered independent individuals take care of their own business with very little or no contact with other vampires.<br /> <br /> Being Anarchs who don't actually defend such unified framework, just share a loose sense of dissatisfaction, they got nothing to work with and straddle between improvising and ignoring the problem while hoping things will hold for at least a few more days at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T11:48:09-07:00","id":1561726,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that, when Requiem 1e was developed, Unaligned was considered the spiritual successor to Anarchs, and Carthians were their own thing.<br /> With Unaligned being phased out, it's natural to want to retrofit Carthians to fill the role of Anarchs, but Carthians has their own identity.<br /> <br /> I also think a lot of people base their view of Anarchs on VtM:B, which paints them in a light that doesn't seem to reflect what Anarchs actually are in VtM, though my perspective of VtM is limited compared to Requiem and I might be mistaken there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T12:01:29-07:00","id":1561729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561726#post1561726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think a lot of people base their view of Anarchs on VtM:B, which paints them in a light that doesn't seem to reflect what Anarchs actually are in VtM, though my perspective of VtM is limited compared to Requiem and I might be mistaken there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's close to this.<br /> <br /> Most people based their views on the By Night books, each giving a deep dive in a particular city.<br /> <br /> The problem with this is that even later authors frequently forgot those cities were just a few examples of how things could be.<br /> <br /> For the Anarchs, the HUGE problem was LA by Night, presenting the Anarch Free States. They are repeatedly stated as a weird outlier and not by any stretch of imagination anything seen as a common ideal or whatever by everyone who call themselves Anarch for any reason.<br /> <br /> But could as well have said it's the Headquarter of a new sect and every Anarch in the world is bound to them by Blood Oath. To the point that even V5 goes through that stupid path.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T09:35:15-07:00","id":1561897,"title":"","content":"I was wondering how Obfuscate 4 - Familiar Stranger would interact with humanity penalty to interact with humans and to greater extend the Nosferatu curse.<br /> <br /> For example, would you remove penalty for socializing as the Familiar Stranger power would do the heavy lifting by reflecting what the other wanted to see? <br /> <br /> Or since it specifically cannot be used to influenced reactions, all penalty would still apply? <br /> <br /> Is this power a false hope for those poor Nosferatus who tries to circumvent their curse by hiding their nature?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T10:15:14-07:00","id":1561899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561897#post1561897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering how Obfuscate 4 - Familiar Stranger would interact with humanity penalty to interact with humans and to greater extend the Nosferatu curse.<br /> <br /> For example, would you remove penalty for socializing as the Familiar Stranger power would do the heavy lifting by reflecting what the other wanted to see?<br /> <br /> Or since it specifically cannot be used to influenced reactions, all penalty would still apply?<br /> <br /> Is this power a false hope for those poor Nosferatus who tries to circumvent their curse by hiding their nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not, honestly. Humanity penalty does not represent something easthetic but rather your inability do deal with humanity which make you appear weird, alien, psycopath.<br /> You can have the look of her/his lover and yet make her/him wondering what's wrong with you today.<br /> <br /> The only discipline I see can cancel that penalty is Awe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-18-2026, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T10:20:30-07:00","id":1561900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561897#post1561897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering how Obfuscate 4 - Familiar Stranger would interact with humanity penalty to interact with humans and to greater extend the Nosferatu curse.<br /> <br /> For example, would you remove penalty for socializing as the Familiar Stranger power would do the heavy lifting by reflecting what the other wanted to see?<br /> <br /> Or since it specifically cannot be used to influenced reactions, all penalty would still apply?<br /> <br /> Is this power a false hope for those poor Nosferatus who tries to circumvent their curse by hiding their nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't affect it any more than the Blush of Life does \u2014 the penalty is from the character's inability to relate to humans, not other characters' reaction to them, and the Lonely Curse is deeper than appearances. A given disguise might provide a bonus that helps offset the penalty, but looking like a normal store clerk isn't going to make up for being weeks out of practice with normal human conversation or stop a Nosferatu from giving off serial killer vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T10:28:51-07:00","id":1561901,"title":"","content":"My question was originally prompted by those following lines :<br /> <br /> '' She can specify a particular image that she wants to project, either a subjective category or a specific person. If she takes the form of a specific person, everyone sees and hears what they would expect were that person present. ''<br /> <br /> It seems to suggest that the power alter more than appearance, but also some kind of projected mannerism instead. <br /> <br /> But, i do agree with both of you however. I was wondering if anyone else had different take on it. <br /> <br /> Thanks for quick answers !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T12:40:54-07:00","id":1561906,"title":"","content":"I at least agree with them.<br /> <br /> You're perceived like the person in the sense of not giving off your disguise, but it ends there.<br /> <br /> Otherwise you'd be getting the full social stats of that person, which isn't the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T12:56:06-07:00","id":1561908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561901#post1561901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question was originally prompted by those following lines :<br /> <br /> '' She can specify a particular image that she wants to project, either a subjective category or a specific person. If she takes the form of a specific person, everyone sees and hears what they would expect were that person present. ''<br /> <br /> It seems to suggest that the power alter more than appearance, but also some kind of projected mannerism instead.<br /> <br /> But, i do agree with both of you however. I was wondering if anyone else had different take on it.<br /> <br /> Thanks for quick answers !</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sees and hears what they would expect that person&quot; means that you cannot decide how you're dressed etc. Two guys could see you dressed up in a different way.<br /> <br /> If I'm not wrong, the text also states that you cannot describe what that person feels for you (like the person she loves, etc). I have not the book with me to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T13:15:11-07:00","id":1561909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1561908#post1561908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not wrong, the text also states that you cannot describe what that person feels for you (like the person she loves, etc). I have not the book with me to check.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct \u2014 if you're specifying a subjective category of person instead of a specific person, that category can't be e.g. &quot;someone Janice will find trustworthy&quot; or &quot;a woman Daryl will fall in love with.&quot; You can pick an objective image to project or imitate a specific person that you know the people you're interacting with feel a certain disposition toward, but you can't blind-fire an emotional response or line of thought for your target to have in response to a generalized disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T18:30:24-07:00","id":1564462,"title":"","content":"why does a traditional book seem more likely to be a touchstone then A E reader","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-01T21:55:08-07:00","id":1564467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564462#post1564462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why does a traditional book seem more likely to be a touchstone then A E reader</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite a passage that states this?<br /> i mean i think you can estabilish strong emotional bonds with both","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T06:43:16-07:00","id":1564529,"title":"","content":"Are Ghoul merits conditional on having Vitae?<br /> <br /> I am think of things like Taste of the Serpent, Sexualized.<br /> <br /> Will these be lost if the ghoul is unghouled temporarily (lacking vitae, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:26:30-07:00","id":1564532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564529#post1564529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Ghoul merits conditional on having Vitae?<br /> <br /> I am think of things like Taste of the Serpent, Sexualized.<br /> <br /> Will these be lost if the ghoul is unghouled temporarily (lacking vitae, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no, they're not lost unless the Ghoul condition expires (after one year withou having ingested vitae if memory deserves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:54:44-07:00","id":1564536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564532#post1564532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say no, they're not lost unless the Ghoul condition expires (after one year withou having ingested vitae if memory deserves).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is for the Blood bond, but in fact there is no mention about the ghoul condition expiring, only that during a blood withdrawal Ghoul powers doesn t works","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T09:05:30-07:00","id":1564537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564536#post1564536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is for the Blood bond, but in fact there is no mention about the ghoul condition expiring, only that during a blood withdrawal Ghoul powers doesn t works</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a ghoul goes without for a month, she loses all these gifts as if she never had them. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A ghoul automatically spends one point of Vitae per month to maintain his ghoul state. If, at the end of the month, he has no Vitae to spend, he must somehow acquire more.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a ghoul doesn\u2019t get his fix, he gains the Deprived Condition (see p. 302). In withdrawal, he begins to age towards his natural age, at a rate of one year per week. This aging remains even if he gets his fix and resolves the Deprived Condition.\u200b </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A ghoul in withdrawal cannot use any Disciplines (even those that do not cost Vitae or which have persistent effects), but retains knowledge of them if his withdrawal ends\u200b </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's not expiring the accurate word but the meaning remain: Even if the ghoul has no vitate left, for the month he's still considered a ghoul and all the merit and powers persists (he cannot just use those that require vitae to be spent. Once the month expire and if he has no vitae left to sustain his/her condition, then he lose any merit/power related to the ghoul condition (until he get his fix).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T09:53:38-07:00","id":1564542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564536#post1564536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is for the Blood bond, but in fact there is no mention about the ghoul condition expiring, only that during a blood withdrawal Ghoul powers doesn t works</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564537#post1564537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps it's not expiring the accurate word but the meaning remain: Even if the ghoul has no vitate left, for the month he's still considered a ghoul and all the merit and powers persists (he cannot just use those that require vitae to be spent. Once the month expire and if he has no vitae left to sustain his/her condition, then he lose any merit/power related to the ghoul condition (until he get his fix).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So just to clarify with an example:<br /> <br /> Martha the Ghoul has a Daeva regnant. The Vitae in her has helped her develop unnatural abilities such as 2 dots of Majesty, the merits <b>Sexualized </b>and <b>Taste of the Serpent</b>.Sadly her regnant is destroyed, and she has been without Vitae for over a year, a horrible experience to be sure.<br /> <br /> Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What exactly does she keep in when she has no Vitae at all after such a long time? </b>I think she no longer qualifies as a Ghoul so everything, including the merits, should go.</li> <li>I<b>f she drinks Vitae again from another non-Daeva vampire, does she recover both merits if she ever lost them? Or <u>Taste of the Serpent</u> is gone as the regnant changed?</b> I think she starts anew as a Ghoul, so everything resets, but my opinion.</li> <li><b>Same as the previous question but what if she drank from a another non-Daeva vampire BEFORE losing the Ghoul condition?</b></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-05-2026, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T10:00:58-07:00","id":1564543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564542#post1564542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So just to clarify with an example:<br /> <br /> Martha the Ghoul has a Daeva regnant. The Vitae in her has helped her develop unnatural abilities such as 2 dots of Majesty, the merits <b>Sexualized </b>and <b>Taste of the Serpent</b>.Sadly her regnant is destroyed, and she has been without Vitae for over a year, a horrible experience to be sure.<br /> <br /> Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What exactly does she keep in when she has no Vitae at all after such a long time? </b>I think she no longer qualifies as a Ghoul so everything, including the merits, should go.</li> <li>I<b>f she drinks Vitae again from another non-Daeva vampire, does she recover both merits if she ever lost them? Or <u>Taste of the Serpent</u> is gone as the regnant changed?</b> I think she starts anew as a Ghoul, so everything resets, but my opinion.</li> <li><b>Same as the previous question but what if she drank from a another non-Daeva vampire BEFORE losing the Ghoul condition?</b></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>What i think is that she will FOREVER qualify as a ghoul.<br /> As stated in the core book, blood deprivation seems to only prevent discipline use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T10:32:00-07:00","id":1564544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564543#post1564543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What i think is that she will FOREVER qualify as a ghoul.<br /> As stated in the core book, blood deprivation seems to only prevent discipline use.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not just about disciplines. The book specifically mentions, p. 100, that after a month she lose ALL THESE GIFTS, and just a paragraph above the gifts are listed as: quick heal, no aging, increased physical potency AND SOME disciplines. Not sure why you want to consider Ghoul's specific merits as no part of these gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564542#post1564542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So just to clarify with an example:<br /> <br /> Martha the Ghoul has a Daeva regnant. The Vitae in her has helped her develop unnatural abilities such as 2 dots of Majesty, the merits <b>Sexualized </b>and <b>Taste of the Serpent</b>.Sadly her regnant is destroyed, and she has been without Vitae for over a year, a horrible experience to be sure.<br /> <br /> Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What exactly does she keep in when she has no Vitae at all after such a long time? </b>I think she no longer qualifies as a Ghoul so everything, including the merits, should go.</li> <li>I<b>f she drinks Vitae again from another non-Daeva vampire, does she recover both merits if she ever lost them? Or <u>Taste of the Serpent</u> is gone as the regnant changed?</b> I think she starts anew as a Ghoul, so everything resets, but my opinion.</li> <li><b>Same as the previous question but what if she drank from a another non-Daeva vampire BEFORE losing the Ghoul condition?</b></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, I agree with you. All get lost untill she gets the fix<br /> <br /> 2. The regnant to me will remain the original one. Manual specifies that once she gets the fix all the lost gifts get back, so I would allows also regnant specific merits. But this is no hard rule, so I guess it's more about what would work at your table and what's your interpretaition.<br /> 3. Drinking from another non-Daeva vampire before ghoul condition expires it's still fine. It is never specified that the fix must come from the original regnant. She refills vitae. That's it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-05-2026, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T12:46:05-07:00","id":1564548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564542#post1564542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just to clarify with an example:<br /> <br /> Martha the Ghoul has a Daeva regnant. The Vitae in her has helped her develop unnatural abilities such as 2 dots of Majesty, the merits <b>Sexualized </b>and <b>Taste of the Serpent</b>.Sadly her regnant is destroyed, and she has been without Vitae for over a year, a horrible experience to be sure.<br /> <br /> Questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>What exactly does she keep in when she has no Vitae at all after such a long time? </b>I think she no longer qualifies as a Ghoul so everything, including the merits, should go.</li> <li>I<b>f she drinks Vitae again from another non-Daeva vampire, does she recover both merits if she ever lost them? Or <u>Taste of the Serpent</u> is gone as the regnant changed?</b> I think she starts anew as a Ghoul, so everything resets, but my opinion.</li> <li><b>Same as the previous question but what if she drank from a another non-Daeva vampire BEFORE losing the Ghoul condition?</b></li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>1. At first nothing happens. When her Regnant was destroyed, Martha the Ghoul was still the same. The countdown since her last renewal is in the same place, her Vitae pool is untouched and IIRC she's still Blood Bound (but don't quote me on that).<br /> <br /> 2. When the renewal date comes she has to spend 1 Vitae to renew for a month. If she has this Vitae, she's good.<br /> <br /> 3. Once the renewal date comes and she can't pay the Vitae, she enters withdrawal and get the Deprived Condition. At this stage, by RAW:<br /> <br /> - She's still a Ghoul,<br /> - She's still Daeva,<br /> - She's still Bound,<br /> - She's has lost <u><b>access</b></u>, <i>not requisite</i>, so nothing vanishes.<br /> <br /> 4. Then a year has passed <i>since her last drink</i>, not Vitae expenditure, she breaks the Bond and is again Bondable. No other effect changes:<br /> <br /> - She's still a Ghoul,<br /> - She's still Daeva,<br /> - She's still Deprived,<br /> - She's still without <u><b>access</b></u>, <i>not requisite</i>, so nothing vanishes.<br /> <br /> 5. If at any moment then she drinks Vitae, she spends 1 point to Resolve Deprived and all the powers come back. <b>Nothing else</b>:<br /> <br /> - She's still a Ghoul,<br /> - She's still Daeva,<br /> - She still fulfills all requisites, so nothing vanishes.<br /> <br /> By RAW, Regnant is permanent. Martha the Ghoul is a Daeva Ghoul. As long as she lives, if nothing breaks the Ghoul condition, she will stay Daeva. This is unclear for a reason, but strictly speaking that's the simplest interpretation.<br /> <br /> IMPORTANT<br /> <br /> By RAW there's no RAW. This is official because one important element of the game is that the Curse (which is actually multiple Curses) is unpredictable and mutable. Strange things happen.<br /> <br /> Martha may be so bound to the Daeva clan that even if Embraced by a vampire of any other clan she will become Daeva. Maybe even if she or her corpse becomes something else, it may be marked by the Daeva or be a Vampire rather than what she should become, and Daeva. Finds out she's an Uratha, but instead of turning Werewolf she turns Daeva. Awakens to a Watchtower and the Supernal turns her Daeva. The Fair Folk kidnaps her and both she becomes Daeva in Arcadia and her Fetch is actually a Daeva. A Geist offer renewed life but instead she becomes Daeva. Her corpse is used to make a Promethean, but while what awakens isn't really her, it's Daeva.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Deprived Condition may resolve in any other way, she may lose the Ghoul state, or maybe she does change Regnant. You may decide any of those is the most common outcome in your game. And then what happens is up to the ST because the game <i>by design</i> has no answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T13:31:01-07:00","id":1564550,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> Thanks for the detailed explanation, just a bit of clarity for my sake.<br /> <br /> Regarding the access as you mention. She has the Disciplines (but can not use), and the merits (but can not use). Is my understanding correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T13:59:42-07:00","id":1564552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564550#post1564550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> Thanks for the detailed explanation, just a bit of clarity for my sake.<br /> <br /> Regarding the access as you mention. She has the Disciplines (but can not use), and the merits (but can not use). Is my understanding correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> She can't use because her access is blocked by the Deprived Condition, but the powers/traits are still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-16T22:43:05-07:00","id":1564797,"title":"","content":"Why is it easier for me to imagine a leather bound book as a touchstone then an E reader","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T01:14:32-07:00","id":1564798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564797#post1564797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it easier for me to imagine a leather bound book as a touchstone then an E reader</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a simple question, that's a question of your personal psychology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-17T15:09:34-07:00","id":1564807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1502801-ask-a-simple-question-vampire?p=1564797#post1564797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it easier for me to imagine a leather bound book as a touchstone then an E reader</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed not a simple question.<br /> <br /> RAW they're equally viable. And RAI what matters is the character's attachment, and people can get attached to anything.<br /> <br /> Beyond that we'd be discussing psychology or literature, games, etc. And the answer wouldn't be simple. For that you open an actual thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}